@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .


#
# prima-materia — Transerfing: Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III:
# Vpered v proshloe! (2004)
#
# The harvest of the third Stupen', kept apart from traditions/transerfing.ttl,
# which declares the tradition and its works. The whole Stupen' was read,
# chapters XI to XV of the combined edition (Ves, 2012), in its English
# translation; the nodes follow the chapters. The text layer has no page
# numbers; every source names chapter and section heading.
#
# Two independent passes over three parts with reconciliation, then one
# integrator per part reading the whole part (prima-materia#924). Parts:
# chapters XI-XII; chapter XIII; chapters XIV-XV. Shared system terms are typed
# once, by the part that introduces them, and linked from the others. The
# harvests of Stupen' I and II (traditions/transerfing-stupen-1.ttl,
# traditions/transerfing-stupen-2.ttl) are linked, not repeated.
#

#
# prima-materia — Transerfing: Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III:
# Vpered v proshloe! (2004), part 1: chapters XI Energy and XII Frailing.
#
# Two independent extraction passes ran over the text (A 251 records, B 262;
# 15 records of B without counterpart in A: 1 added, 14 covered, 0 not owed);
# a reader of the whole part added 2 records both passes missed (a practice
# and a sequencing of the job search) and reclassified 4 (three to concepts,
# one caution to a condition of failure). Stupen' I and II
# (traditions/transerfing-stupen-1.ttl, -2.ttl) are not restated: 4 records
# whose claim a node there already carries are left out and linked; 29 nodes
# that restate an earlier node with a difference say so in a note.
#
# Shared system terms typed here: pmc:TranserfingEnergiya,
# pmc:TranserfingEnergiyaNamereniya. pmc:TranserfingFreyling already stands in
# Stupen' II (chapter IX) and is linked, not retyped; chapter XII's fuller
# account is pmc:TranserfingFrailingCh12. The shared terms of parts 2 and 3
# (coordination of importance and of intention, transaction, gliding,
# inversion) have no counterpart in these two chapters and are not referenced.
# The energy masters of chapter XI are a third-party ascription; the polemics
# against medical pendulums, drug advertising and weather prognoses are
# cautions, since only the author's side is read.
#
#
# ch. XI Energy, section 'Energy levels'
#

pmc:TranserfingHealthAndAStrongFieldBeforeEffectiveTransurfingCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Health and a strong field before effective Transurfing"@en, "Gesundheit und starkes Feld vor wirksamem Transurfing"@de ;
    skos:definition "Working Transurfing effectively is said to require sound health and a fairly strong energy field; no consequence of skipping is named beyond reduced effectiveness."@en ;
    skos:note "Stated as a precondition, but no node carries the dependent step, so it is entered as a concept."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Energy levels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSignsOfInsufficientEnergyCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Signs of insufficient energy"@en, "Anzeichen zu geringer Energie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Taken as signs that health and energy are lacking: dragging oneself out of bed, reluctance to go to work or study, drowsiness after lunch, longing only for the sofa and television in the evening; depression, stress, boredom, fatigue and apathy; a total lack of wish to do anything indicates a deficit of free energy."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Taken as signs that health and energy are lacking: dragging oneself out of bed, reluctance to go to work or study, drowsiness after lunch, longing only for the sofa and television in the evening; depression, stress, boredom, fatigue and apathy; a total lack of wish to do anything indicates a deficit of free energy; it bears on pmc:TranserfingHighEnergyLevelsCh11."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Energy levels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDroppingExcessPotentialYieldsRegainedVitalityCh11 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Dropping excess potential yields regained vitality"@en, "Abbau überschüssiger Potentiale bringt Lebenskraft zurück"@de ;
    skos:definition "Energy formerly bound up in excess potentials and in pendulums is said to come back once these are dropped, adding to the level of energy before any exercise."@en ;
    skos:note "Added on reconciliation: found by pass B only."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingReducingImportance ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingHighEnergyLevelsCh11 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Energy levels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHighEnergyLevelsCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "High energy levels"@en, "Hohes Energieniveau"@de ;
    skos:definition "Energy level is defined as the capacity to take in and make use of energy, above all free energy; held to be raisable through the chapter's exercises and to be the supply of intention."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Energy levels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingEnergiya a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Two forms of human energy"@en, "Zwei Formen menschlicher Energie"@de ;
    skos:definition "The body runs on physiological energy obtained by digestion and on free energy, said to be the energy of the Cosmos flowing through the body; both together form the energy body. Free energy passes in two currents: an ascending one about one inch ahead of the spine for men and two for women, and a descending one hugging the spine. How much free energy a person has is said to depend on how wide the central meridians are."@en ;
    skos:note "Shared system term of Stupen' III, typed by this part (Russian energiya): life energy in the author's sense, the share drawn from food plus the free cosmic share. Its levels: pmc:TranserfingHighEnergyLevelsCh11."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Energy levels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingEnergyBlocksAndHolesLinkedToIllnessCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Energy blocks and holes linked to illness"@en, "Energieblockaden und Löcher als Krankheitsursache"@de ;
    skos:definition "Disturbed energy flow through blocks and holes is said to show up as bodily illness, and a diseased organ can in turn distort the energy body; which came first is hard to tell."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Energy levels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAcupunctureGivesOnlyShortTermEffectCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Acupuncture gives only short-term effect"@en, "Akupunktur wirkt nur kurzfristig"@de ;
    skos:definition "Acupuncture, acupressure and similar methods can restore circulation and cure energy-caused illness, but their effect is said to be short-lived; lasting health needs care of both the physical and the subtle body."@en ;
    skos:note "Entered as a concept: it judges another method and names nothing within Transurfing to be careful about."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Energy levels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMuscleTensionObstructsEnergyFlowCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Muscle tension obstructs energy flow"@en, "Muskelverspannung hemmt den Energiefluss"@de ;
    skos:definition "Muscle tension is said to impede the invisible currents; a tense person entering a relaxed group shifts its mood silently, the others absorb the negative energy, and balancing forces arise, e.g. the group teases the stiff newcomer until they relax."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Energy levels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingEnergiyaNamereniya a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Free energy as the energy of intention"@en, "Freie Energie als Energie der Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Free energy is held to drive initiative: physiological energy alone cannot sustain vitality, and without free energy a person can still do routine tasks but has no intention and cannot be creative or active; physiological energy goes into executing actions, free energy into forming intention."@en ;
    skos:note "Shared system term of Stupen' III, typed by this part (Russian energiya namereniya); it feeds pmc:TranserfingNamerenie and, through it, pmc:TranserfingVneshneeNamerenie."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Energy levels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. XI Energy, section 'Stress and relaxation'
#

pmc:TranserfingStressNarrowsOrDilatesTheMeridiansCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Stress narrows or dilates the meridians"@en, "Stress verengt oder weitet die Meridiane"@de ;
    skos:definition "Depression and tension are said to block and narrow the central meridians so that free energy slows or stops and intention loses its supply; rarely, stress makes them suddenly widen, enabling exceptional feats, but mostly it cuts a person's resources."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Stress and relaxation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingExceptionalFeatsUnderSuddenMeridianDilationCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Exceptional feats under sudden meridian dilation"@en, "Außergewöhnliche Leistungen bei plötzlicher Meridianweitung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Under stress the meridians can rarely dilate at once, and a person is then said to accomplish things far beyond their normal ability; reported as known but rare, not as trainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Stress and relaxation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPhysicalTensionFollowsMentalTensionCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Physical tension follows mental tension"@en, "Körperliche Spannung folgt seelischer Spannung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Habitual muscle tensing is the body's stress reflex; muscle tension is caused by states such as anxiety, irritation and fear, and stress itself is a consequence of importance, the excess meaning given to what troubles one. The common belief that relaxing removes stress treats the symptom, not the cause."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Stress and relaxation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMuscleRelaxationAloneRelapsesCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Muscle relaxation alone relapses"@en, "Bloße Muskelentspannung fällt zurück"@de ;
    skos:definition "Deliberately relaxing muscles brings only passing relief; if the mental tension is not resolved the body returns to its earlier state. Likewise, carrying importance means one will never improve a situation or act effectively."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Deliberately relaxing muscles brings only passing relief; if the mental tension is not resolved the body returns to its earlier state. Likewise, carrying importance means one will never improve a situation or act effectively; it bears on pmc:TranserfingFreedomFromAndImmunityToStressCh11."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Stress and relaxation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLoweringImportanceYieldsFreedomFromStressCh11 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Lowering importance yields freedom from stress"@en, "Senken der Wichtigkeit bewirkt Stressfreiheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reducing importance is said to relieve stress at once and, as a habit, to make one stress-immune."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingRelievingStressByLoweringImportanceCh11 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingFreedomFromAndImmunityToStressCh11 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Stress and relaxation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingRelievingStressByLoweringImportanceCh11 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Relieving stress by lowering importance"@en, "Stressabbau durch Senken der Wichtigkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "When strongly stressed: wake up, open your eyes, notice that a pendulum has caught onto your importance; identify what the importance concerns; remind yourself that lowering it frees you from the pendulum; consciously drop the excess meaning. Whenever unease arises, ask why and where meaning has been inflated, and let go of attachment to it however important the matter seems; act only after intention has been purified."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingThreeStepRelease: the release of importance (pmc:TranserfingVazhnost) is applied to stress, with the added step of noticing that a pendulum (pmc:TranserfingMayatnik) has caught hold of it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Stress and relaxation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHabitOfHeedingTheInnerVoiceEasesRememberingCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Habit of heeding the inner voice eases remembering importance"@en, "Gewohnheit, auf die innere Stimme zu achten, erleichtert das Erinnern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Someone who habitually attends to the inner voice will find it easy to recall importance at the needed moment; stated as facilitating, not as strictly necessary."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingGuardianForRemembering: the help for remembering in time is a habit of listening to the inner voice, not the Guardian."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Stress and relaxation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPurifiedIntentionBeforeEffectiveActionCh11 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Purified intention before effective action"@en, "Gereinigte Absicht vor wirksamem Handeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Effective action comes only after intention is purified of importance; skipping this means one will not change the situation for the better nor act effectively while laden with importance."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:TranserfingActingPurifiedIntentionX10 ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingRelievingStressByLoweringImportanceCh11 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "No improvement of the situation and no effective action while importance is carried." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Stress and relaxation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFreedomFromAndImmunityToStressCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Freedom from and immunity to stress"@en, "Freiheit von Stress und Stressimmunität"@de ;
    skos:definition "Stress is said to be removable instantly by reducing importance; becoming immune to stress means replacing the habit of getting worked up over trifles with the habit of staying relaxed."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Stress and relaxation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRelaxedStateOfBalanceAndUnityCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Relaxed state of balance and unity with the world"@en, "Entspannter Zustand von Gleichgewicht und Einssein mit der Welt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Relaxation here is not apathy but harmonious interaction with the world, i.e. balance, which presupposes absence of inner and outer importance; the integral feeling of the whole body surface brimming with energy is said to equal relaxation, balance and unity with the world, inducible swiftly in any circumstances."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingStateOfBalance: balance is here also a relaxed bodily state and a felt oneness with the world, reached by an exercise."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Stress and relaxation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLowImportanceBeforeRelaxationCh11 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Low importance before relaxation"@en, "Geringe Wichtigkeit vor Entspannung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Absent or low importance is named the main condition for relaxing; trying to relax with inflated importance is pointless (example: someone afraid of heights on a roof edge cannot stay relaxed)."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingRelaxedStateOfBalanceAndUnityCh11 ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingRelievingStressByLoweringImportanceCh11 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Relaxation attempts are futile while importance stays inflated." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Stress and relaxation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDoNotForceRelaxationWhenImportanceCannotBeCh11 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not force relaxation when importance cannot be lowered"@en, "Entspannung nicht erzwingen, wenn die Wichtigkeit nicht sinkt"@de ;
    skos:definition "If lowering importance is impossible, do not spend energy trying to relax: suppressing feelings while handling a crisis only raises energy use; better to let go and worry freely."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingInducingTheRelaxedStateCh11 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Stress and relaxation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMusclesObeyIntentionNotWordsCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Muscles obey intention, not words"@en, "Muskeln gehorchen der Absicht, nicht Worten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Inducing relaxation needs no verbal autosuggestion, since muscles are governed by intention; awareness of a muscle is mostly enough to release it, and a scan with the inner eye can dissolve contractions."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Stress and relaxation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNeglectedMuscleGroupsSuchAsTheBackCh11 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Neglected muscle groups such as the back"@en, "Vernachlässigte Muskelgruppen wie der Rücken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Because of sedentary living some muscle groups no longer respond to intention; back muscles are hard to control consciously, so back pain tends to develop with age; regular stretching and exercise of the back is called absolutely necessary."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingInducingTheRelaxedStateCh11 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Stress and relaxation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingStretchingAndExercisingTheBackCh11 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Stretching and exercising the back"@en, "Rücken dehnen und trainieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Stretch and train the back on a regular basis, called indispensable however commonplace it sounds, because the back muscles barely answer conscious control and otherwise tend to ache with age."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the reader of the whole part: missed by both passes."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Stress and relaxation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingInducingTheRelaxedStateCh11 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Inducing the relaxed state"@en, "Herbeiführen des entspannten Zustands"@de ;
    skos:definition "Without hurry, quickly sweep the body with the inner eye and release tensions; place attention on the whole skin surface at once; picture the skin as a membrane rapidly warming from inside (or tingling, or with electric discharges, as you like) and actually feel the skin; then picture energy shimmering across the whole surface like the colours on a soap bubble. Do not try to imitate any special sensation and do not strain; perform it casually yet decisively."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Stress and relaxation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDoNotSimulateSensationsCh11 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not simulate sensations"@en, "Keine Empfindungen vortäuschen"@de ;
    skos:definition "No need to fake special sensations or to make an effort at all; experiences differ from person to person."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingInducingTheRelaxedStateCh11 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Stress and relaxation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRelaxationExerciseYieldsBalanceAndOnenessCh11 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Relaxation exercise yields balance and oneness"@en, "Entspannungsübung bewirkt Gleichgewicht und Einssein"@de ;
    skos:definition "The exercise is said to produce relaxed balance and felt unity with the world."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingInducingTheRelaxedStateCh11 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingRelaxedStateOfBalanceAndUnityCh11 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Stress and relaxation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRelaxedStateComesInstantlyAfterAFewRepetitionsCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Relaxed state comes instantly after a few repetitions"@en, "Entspannter Zustand stellt sich nach wenigen Wiederholungen sofort ein"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: the integral sense of the whole surface overflowing with energy marks the state; after a few repetitions it is reached at once and soon becomes as effortless as crossing one's arms."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingInducingTheRelaxedStateCh11."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Stress and relaxation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. XI Energy, section 'Energy vampires'
#

pmc:TranserfingAccessToCosmicEnergyAndWhyVampirismCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Access to cosmic energy and why vampirism is easier"@en, "Zugang zur kosmischen Energie und warum Vampirismus leichter ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Cosmic energy is everywhere but not distributed toward humans; to draw it consciously one must deliberately widen the meridians and pull the flow in. Energy already assimilated by a human body has a specific frequency and is easier to take; tuning to someone's frequency, like a radio circuit tuned to one station, suffices to take it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Energy vampires'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDeliberateRechargingFromTheCosmosCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Deliberate recharging from the Cosmos"@en, "Bewusstes Aufladen aus dem Kosmos"@de ;
    skos:definition "Humans are said to be in principle able to recharge intentionally from the Cosmos by widening the meridians, though this ability is still only rudimentary."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Energy vampires'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingThreeTypesOfEnergyVampireCh11 a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Three types of energy vampire"@en, "Drei Typen von Energievampiren"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author sorts energy vampires into three types: the stealthy one, who tunes in through innocent questions, eye contact, touching, hand-holding or pushy talk, adapting to temperament (a good psychologist, sociable but not charming, persistently intrusive); the manipulator, who plays on guilt and finds people who hand themselves over to another's judgement or seek advice, needing only to touch their worry to open them; the provocateur, coarse and aggressive, attacking the aura by anything from veiled bullying to open aggression to make the donor lose composure and pour out any emotion."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingManipulators: the manipulator now appears as one of three kinds of energy vampire, tuning in through the donor's guilt."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Energy vampires'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingVampirismIsUnconsciousCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Vampirism is unconscious"@en, "Vampirismus geschieht unbewusst"@de ;
    skos:definition "People become vampires without knowing it: they notice that certain situations lift them and keep recreating them; donor and vampire seek each other out to meet mutual needs."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Energy vampires'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSignOfHavingBeenDrainedCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sign of having been drained"@en, "Anzeichen, ausgesaugt worden zu sein"@de ;
    skos:definition "If after a conversation one feels exposed, vulnerable, weak or shaky, one may assume one's energy was taken."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: If after a conversation one feels exposed, vulnerable, weak or shaky, one may assume one's energy was taken; it bears on pmc:TranserfingProtectionFromVampiresAndManipulationCh11."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Energy vampires'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPendulumCh11 a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Pendulum"@en, "Pendel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pendulums are held to take the largest share of a person's free energy, drawing it via the importance meridian, and unlike a vampire to do so continuously for as long as the person emits at the pendulum's frequency; they are called freeloaders that hook into their prey; one not swaying with them cannot be drained."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingMayatnik: here the pendulum is the chief consumer of free energy, drawing it through the importance meridian without pause for as long as one resonates, unlike the brief raid of a vampire."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "pendulum" ;
    pm:nameRole "energy-feeding structure that hooks into importance" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Energy vampires'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLowEnergyInvitesIntrusionCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Low energy invites intrusion"@en, "Niedrige Energie lädt zu Übergriffen ein"@de ;
    skos:definition "When worried or low in awareness and self-confidence, others and animals sense the weakness: a dog singles you out to bark at, a street beggar to pester; a vampire can take much and one slips easily into trouble."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Energy vampires'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingObsessiveWatchfulnessAgainstVampiresCh11 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Obsessive watchfulness against vampires"@en, "Zwanghafte Wachsamkeit gegenüber Vampiren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Do not suspect a vampire in everyone: being obsessively cautious itself opens access to your biofield."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingGuardingAgainstNegativeEnergeticInfluenceCh11 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Energy vampires'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingGuardingAgainstNegativeEnergeticInfluenceCh11 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Guarding against negative energetic influence"@en, "Schutz vor negativem energetischem Einfluss"@de ;
    skos:definition "Strengthen the energy body, monitor your importance level, cultivate awareness so as to stay conscious when someone tries to draw you into a game or trap, keep importance low so that tuning to your frequency is hard, and watch for guilt feelings; inner emptiness leaves nothing to hook into."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingEmptiness: emptiness toward hooks is joined with strengthening the energy body, low importance and watchfulness over guilt."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Energy vampires'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingProtectiveMeasuresYieldProtectionFromVampiresCh11 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Protective measures yield protection from vampires"@en, "Schutzmaßnahmen bewirken Schutz vor Vampiren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Energy-body strengthening, low importance and awareness are said to protect against negative influence."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingGuardingAgainstNegativeEnergeticInfluenceCh11 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingProtectionFromVampiresAndManipulationCh11 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Energy vampires'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingManipulatorsGiveUpAfterFailedAttemptsCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Manipulators give up after failed attempts"@en, "Manipulatoren geben nach Fehlversuchen auf"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: most manipulator vampires leave you in peace after one or two vain attempts to hook in."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingGuardingAgainstNegativeEnergeticInfluenceCh11."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Energy vampires'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingProtectionFromVampiresAndManipulationCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Protection from vampires and manipulation"@en, "Schutz vor Vampiren und Manipulation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Being hard to tune into and unhookable, with a strong aura said to give dependable protection against unwanted interference."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Energy vampires'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. XI Energy, section 'The Protective Shield'
#

pmp:TranserfingSensingTheAuraCh11 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Sensing the aura"@en, "Die Aura spüren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Feel the surface of the whole body as when lowering yourself into a hot bath; do not 'try', simply do it. Picture energy slowly flowing from the body's centre and spilling onto the surface to form a ball, and imagine being enclosed by this ball of the energy body."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'The Protective Shield'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWorksFirstTimeWhenNotTryingCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Works first time when not trying"@en, "Gelingt beim ersten Mal ohne Bemühen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: whoever plunges straight in without assuming effort is needed first will manage it at the first go without practice."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingSensingTheAuraCh11."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'The Protective Shield'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAuraSensingExerciseYieldsManagementOfTheEnergyCh11 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Aura sensing exercise yields management of the energy body"@en, "Aura-Übung bewirkt Lenkung des Energiekörpers"@de ;
    skos:definition "Imagining the energy ball is said to begin control of the energy body and later bring a bodily sense of it."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingSensingTheAuraCh11 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingSensingAndManagingTheEnergyBodyAuraCh11 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'The Protective Shield'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSensingAndManagingTheEnergyBodyAuraCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sensing and managing the energy body (aura)"@en, "Spüren und Lenken des Energiekörpers (Aura)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Imagining the aura is the first step to managing the energy body; with time a physical sense of it is said to develop."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'The Protective Shield'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingExtrasensoryPerceptionSeeingAurasCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Extrasensory perception, seeing auras"@en, "Außersinnliche Wahrnehmung, Aurasehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Psychics are said to see auras and their defects; everyone is said to be born with extrasensory abilities that lie dormant through disuse and can be woken instantly or over long practice, depending on the power of intention."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingSeeingAurasCh9: extrasensory perception is now said to be inborn in everyone and wakeable by exercises according to the strength of intention."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'The Protective Shield'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLatentAbilitiesAwakenedByIntentionCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Latent abilities awakened by intention"@en, "Schlummernde Fähigkeiten durch Absicht geweckt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Dormant abilities are held to be awakenable at once or gradually by exercises; it all depends on how powerful one's intention is; full power of intention is hard to gain, but enough to keep energy healthy suffices here."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'The Protective Shield'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAWeakAuraInvitesEnergeticAttackCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A weak aura invites energetic attack"@en, "Schwache Aura lädt zu energetischem Angriff ein"@de ;
    skos:definition "A weak aura always leaves one exposed to assault on the energy field."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: A weak aura always leaves one exposed to assault on the energy field; it bears on pmc:TranserfingProtectionFromVampiresAndManipulationCh11."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'The Protective Shield'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFountainExerciseYieldsHealthyEnergyLevelsCh11 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Fountain exercise yields healthy energy levels"@en, "Fontänenübung bewirkt gesundes Energieniveau"@de ;
    skos:definition "Regular performance of the exercise is said to build and keep healthy energy levels, and meridians to be developed by energy exercises."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingEnergyFountainsAndProtectiveSphereCh11 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingHighEnergyLevelsCh11 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'The Protective Shield'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingEnergyFountainsAndProtectiveSphereCh11 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Energy fountains and protective sphere"@en, "Energiefontänen und Schutzsphäre"@de ;
    skos:definition "Stand relaxed. Inhaling, imagine energy rising from the ground, entering at the perineum, travelling up in front of the spine and leaving through the head into the sky; exhaling, imagine energy coming down from the sky, entering the head, passing down the spine and out into the ground; imagining suffices. Then run both currents at once, side by side, never crossing, each running in its own channel; at first link them to breathing, later free them from it; you may speed them by imagination. Let the rising flow leave the crown and fall around you like a fountain, the falling flow leave below the feet and turn the other way, giving two fountains; merge their spray into an enveloping sphere. Then feel the skin surface and expand that feeling out to the sphere as if inflating a balloon, fixing the sphere. Stay relaxed and do not strain to feel the energy; practise attention to the currents from time to time."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'The Protective Shield'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPhysicallyFeelingTheCentralCurrentsCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Physically feeling the central currents"@en, "Körperliches Spüren der zentralen Ströme"@de ;
    skos:definition "With time sensitivity grows and one learns to feel the energy moving, tangibly though less immediately than touch."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'The Protective Shield'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNoStrainingInTheFountainExerciseCh11 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "No straining in the fountain exercise"@en, "Kein Anstrengen bei der Fontänenübung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Keep relaxed and avoid tension from trying hard to feel energy physically; do not worry at first about not sensing the central meridians, which are unfelt like any healthy organ."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingEnergyFountainsAndProtectiveSphereCh11 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'The Protective Shield'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAttentionToCurrentsYieldsFeelingThemCh11 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Attention to currents yields feeling them"@en, "Aufmerksamkeit auf die Ströme bewirkt ihr Spüren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Regularly turning attention to the energy currents is said to bring a bodily sense of them before long."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingEnergyFountainsAndProtectiveSphereCh11 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingPhysicallyFeelingTheCentralCurrentsCh11 ;
