#
# ch. XI Energy, section 'Increasing Your Energy Levels'
#

pmc:TranserfingFreeEnergyCannotBeStoredCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Free energy cannot be stored"@en, "Freie Energie lässt sich nicht speichern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Raising energy is not stockpiling: only physiological energy is stored as calories through food and rest; free energy from the Cosmos cannot be kept, it is present without limit everywhere in the field, and high energy depends chiefly on meridian width."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Increasing Your Energy Levels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingInnerVersusOuterIntentionAndEnergyCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Inner versus outer intention and energy"@en, "Innere gegenüber äußerer Absicht und Energie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Outer intention does not fight or alter the world but simply selects what it needs, as in a shop of alternatives without haggling; it needs no stored energy since that is superabundant; immediate needs are, however, met only by inner intention."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingVneshneeNamerenie: added here is that outer intention needs no stock of energy, since energy is present in excess everywhere."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Increasing Your Energy Levels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNoAttemptToStockpileEnergyCh11 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "No attempt to stockpile energy"@en, "Nicht versuchen, Energie anzuhäufen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Building energy reserves in order to impose inner intention on the world is futile and very costly; it is like filling one's cheeks with water while swimming in a lake in case the lake runs dry; one should not aim at being an energy bundle."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingHighEnergyLevelsCh11 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Increasing Your Energy Levels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWholeEnergyOfTheUniverseAtOnesDisposalCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Whole energy of the universe at one’s disposal"@en, "Die gesamte Energie des Universums verfügbar"@de ;
    skos:definition "Feeling oneself part of the Universe is said to place its entire energy at one's disposal and, by a light touch of outer intention, to achieve personal goals quickly that inner intention could never reach."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Increasing Your Energy Levels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingMergingWithUniversalEnergyCh11 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Merging with universal energy"@en, "Verschmelzen mit der Energie des Universums"@de ;
    skos:definition "Let energy flow through you as two opposing currents, optionally pictured as counter-flowing fountains; picture yourself as a drop in the ocean; let your consciousness feel itself an inseparable part of the Universe; expand the energy sphere and dissolve it into the surrounding space while remembering that in form you remain a distinct particle; aim for a continuous energetic feeling of oneness rather than a single act."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Increasing Your Energy Levels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMergingYieldsUniversalEnergyAndSwiftGoalAttainmentCh11 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Merging yields universal energy and swift goal attainment"@en, "Verschmelzen bewirkt universelle Energie und raschen Zielerfolg"@de ;
    skos:definition "Merging with universal energy is said to give access to its energy and fast realization of personal goals via outer intention."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingMergingWithUniversalEnergyCh11 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingWholeEnergyOfTheUniverseAtOnesDisposalCh11 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Increasing Your Energy Levels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCloggedBodyAndChronicStressRestrictMeridiansCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Clogged body and chronic stress restrict meridians"@en, "Verschlackter Körper und Dauerstress verengen die Meridiane"@de ;
    skos:definition "Two main limits on free energy: a toxic body and continual stress; then brief surges of energy are followed by long recovery, and life shrinks to bare subsistence."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Two main limits on free energy: a toxic body and continual stress; then brief surges of energy are followed by long recovery, and life shrinks to bare subsistence; it bears on pmc:TranserfingHighEnergyLevelsCh11."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Increasing Your Energy Levels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMeridiansAtrophyWithLoweredIntentionCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Meridians atrophy with lowered intention"@en, "Meridiane verkümmern bei gesenkter Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Meridians are exercised when life demands intention at full strength; once main goals are reached the bar drops, the meridians narrow and waste with age, intention fades and life turns burdensome; this can be remedied without forcing new conquests."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Increasing Your Energy Levels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingEnergyExercisesYieldDevelopedMeridiansCh11 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Energy exercises yield developed meridians"@en, "Energieübungen bewirken entwickelte Meridiane"@de ;
    skos:definition "Meridians can be developed by energy exercises, the more so the more one tunes into the central currents."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingEnergyFountainsAndProtectiveSphereCh11 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingDevelopedCentralMeridiansAndTheirBenefitsCh11 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Increasing Your Energy Levels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDevelopedCentralMeridiansAndTheirBenefitsCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Developed central meridians and their benefits"@en, "Entwickelte zentrale Meridiane und ihre Vorteile"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tuning into the central currents and subtle body is said to bring: balance and harmony with one's surroundings; greater sensitivity to environmental change and easy going with the flow; connection to the information field as a boundless source of creativity; access to cosmic energy; radiating harmonious energy that surrounds one with prosperity and success; above all functioning where heart and mind meet, so the ability to direct outer intention grows and wishes come true faster and easier."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Increasing Your Energy Levels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingSwitchingOnAndBalancingTheFountainsCh11 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Switching on and balancing the fountains during the day"@en, "Fontänen tagsüber einschalten und ausgleichen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Now and then during the day switch on the fountains and strengthen them by mental picturing without effort. Balance the currents so they meet at the body's midpoint; from there picture them radiating through the sphere until the subtle body feels clearer, sensing both currents and the whole energy body together. If the head grows heavy, the ascending flow dominates: shift attention downward and reinforce that current slightly."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Increasing Your Energy Levels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHeavyHeadSignalsUnbalancedCurrentsCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Heavy head signals unbalanced currents"@en, "Schwerer Kopf zeigt unausgeglichene Ströme"@de ;
    skos:definition "A heavy feeling in the head during the exercise means the rising current is overpowering the falling one."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: A heavy feeling in the head during the exercise means the rising current is overpowering the falling one; it bears on pmp:TranserfingSwitchingOnAndBalancingTheFountainsCh11."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Increasing Your Energy Levels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCurrentEmphasisYieldsControlOfCentreOfGravityCh11 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Current emphasis yields control of centre of gravity"@en, "Betonung eines Stroms bewirkt Schwerpunktsteuerung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Concentrating on one current is said to shift energy and gravity centre accordingly."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingShiftingTheEnergyCentreForSportCh11 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingControlOfEnergyCentreAndCentreOfGravityCh11 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Increasing Your Energy Levels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingShiftingTheEnergyCentreForSportCh11 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Shifting the energy centre for sport"@en, "Verlagern des Energiezentrums im Sport"@de ;
    skos:definition "Concentrate on the descending current to lower the energy centre and with it the physical centre of gravity, for leg stability as in skiing; concentrate on the ascending current to raise it for high jumps."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Increasing Your Energy Levels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingControlOfEnergyCentreAndCentreOfGravityCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Control of energy centre and centre of gravity"@en, "Steuerung von Energie- und Körperschwerpunkt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Shifting the energy centre is said to move the bodily centre of gravity; some energy masters reportedly stand so rooted on the descending current that no one can move them, others leap to incredible heights on the ascending one."@en ;
    skos:note "The rooted and leaping energy masters are the author's ascription to others."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Increasing Your Energy Levels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingAttendingToTheCentralMeridiansDuringExerciseCh11 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Attending to the central meridians during exercise"@en, "Aufmerksamkeit auf die zentralen Meridiane beim Sport"@de ;
    skos:definition "During any physical training, now and then turn inner sight to the zone directly ahead of the spine and picture the rising current going up and the falling one going down; be patient when movements seem to clash with the visualization."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Increasing Your Energy Levels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingOverdiligenceDoesNotPayCh11 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Overdiligence does not pay"@en, "Übereifer zahlt sich nicht aus"@de ;
    skos:definition "Do not try too hard; excessive diligence never pays off."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingAttendingToTheCentralMeridiansDuringExerciseCh11 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Increasing Your Energy Levels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSkillOfFeelingMeridiansAndMatchingMovementCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Skill of feeling meridians and matching movement"@en, "Fertigkeit, Meridiane zu spüren und Bewegung abzustimmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: regular running of the meridians gradually builds the skill of feeling them, and in time any movement can easily be matched with the sense of energy flow."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingAttendingToTheCentralMeridiansDuringExerciseCh11."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Increasing Your Energy Levels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAttentionDuringExerciseYieldsFeelingTheMeridiansCh11 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Attention during exercise yields feeling the meridians"@en, "Aufmerksamkeit beim Sport bewirkt Spüren der Meridiane"@de ;
    skos:definition "Regular attention to the meridians during exercise is said to develop the ability to feel them."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingAttendingToTheCentralMeridiansDuringExerciseCh11 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingPhysicallyFeelingTheCentralCurrentsCh11 ;
