    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Increasing Your Energy Levels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingStrengthTrainingAttentionYieldsHigherEnergyCh11 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Strength-training attention yields higher energy"@en, "Aufmerksamkeit beim Krafttraining bewirkt höhere Energie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Attending to the meridians during weight training is said to raise energy significantly; alternating contraction and release compresses then releases energy through the meridians like springs."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingMeridianAttentionInStrengthTrainingCh11 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingHighEnergyLevelsCh11 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Increasing Your Energy Levels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingMeridianAttentionInStrengthTrainingCh11 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Meridian attention in strength training"@en, "Meridian-Aufmerksamkeit beim Krafttraining"@de ;
    skos:definition "In the effort phase of a lift attend to the muscles; on the counter-movement as muscles relax, move attention to the central meridians and hold the relaxed point one to two seconds to feel energy move. Pull-up example: hold breath at the start, complete the pull, breathe out; on the way down breathe in, relax, shift attention to the meridians, imagine energy flowing both ways, hang with straight relaxed arms one to two seconds and feel the flow as if just released; do not speed it in relaxation. In press-ups, with hands planted and elbows flexed, while exhaling picture forcefully pushing the energy; breathe as is comfortable, usually holding or exhaling on effort and inhaling on relaxation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Increasing Your Energy Levels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDoNotHurryTheFlowDuringRelaxationCh11 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not hurry the flow during relaxation"@en, "Fluss in der Entspannung nicht beschleunigen"@de ;
    skos:definition "When muscles are relaxed do not try to accelerate the energy; let the currents run freely."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingMeridianAttentionInStrengthTrainingCh11 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Increasing Your Energy Levels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingEnergeticInfluenceAndCharismaCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Energetic influence and charisma"@en, "Energetische Ausstrahlung und Charisma"@de ;
    skos:definition "Higher energy is said to raise one's power of influence and enrich the quality of one's energy, useful in persuading; people treat one better because they subconsciously sense and partly benefit from the overflowing fountains; people called magnetic or charismatic are such sources."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Increasing Your Energy Levels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRaisingEnergyYieldsInfluenceCh11 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Raising energy yields influence"@en, "Energiesteigerung bewirkt Ausstrahlung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Increasing energy through the exercises is said to increase influence and goodwill from others."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingEnergyFountainsAndProtectiveSphereCh11 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingEnergeticInfluenceAndCharismaCh11 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Increasing Your Energy Levels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAgainstTechniquesOfEnergeticDominationCh11 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Against techniques of energetic domination"@en, "Gegen Techniken energetischer Beherrschung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Techniques for dominating others energetically exist but violate Transurfing's principle of the right to choose without the right to change things; pressuring the world is ineffective and provokes counter-pressure."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingEnergeticInfluenceAndCharismaCh11 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Increasing Your Energy Levels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGivingAwayExcessEnergyIsHarmlessCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Giving away excess energy is harmless"@en, "Abgabe überschüssiger Energie ist unschädlich"@de ;
    skos:definition "Most people do not feed deliberately as pendulums do; they just bathe in one's surplus; the small excess given away only works in one's favour, so worrying about it is needless."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Increasing Your Energy Levels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingTurningOnTheFountainsBeforeAnImportantMeetingCh11 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Turning on the fountains before an important meeting"@en, "Fontänen vor einem wichtigen Treffen einschalten"@de ;
    skos:definition "While waiting for an important meeting, drop importance and activate the central meridians until they flow as fountains; then fewer clever words and arguments are needed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Increasing Your Energy Levels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFountainsBeforeAMeetingYieldGoodwillCh11 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Fountains before a meeting yield goodwill"@en, "Fontänen vor einem Treffen bewirken Wohlwollen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Letting free energy pass through you makes it available to others, who feel well disposed without knowing why."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingTurningOnTheFountainsBeforeAnImportantMeetingCh11 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingEnergeticInfluenceAndCharismaCh11 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Increasing Your Energy Levels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. XI Energy, section 'The Energy of Intention'
#

pmc:TranserfingThoughtProgrammedEnergyRealizesAlternativesCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Thought-programmed energy realizes alternatives"@en, "Gedankenprogrammierte Energie verwirklicht Alternativen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The central currents are said to be programmed by one's thoughts and to leave the body with those parameters; the programmed energy gathers in the matching sector of the alternatives space and makes that alternative materialize, but only if heart and mind are united, otherwise the thought energy acts like radio interference. Basic actions need only inner intention; realizing a potential alternative needs outer intention, whose power is proportional to energy level: total commitment plus high energetic potential."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingThoughtMaterialisesSector: the carrier is now the central currents shaped by thought, and the shaping holds only when heart and mind agree (pmc:TranserfingEdinstvoDushiIRazuma)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMeridianTrainingAndCleansingYieldIntentionEnergyCh11 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Meridian training and cleansing yield intention energy"@en, "Meridiantraining und Reinigung bewirken Absichtsenergie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Energy levels and thus outer intention are said to rise through central-meridian training and bodily cleansing."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingEnergyFountainsAndProtectiveSphereCh11 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingIncreasedEnergyOfIntentionCh11 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingInitialIntentionBeforeRaisingIntentionEnergyCh11 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Initial intention before raising intention energy"@en, "Anfängliche Absicht vor Steigerung der Absichtsenergie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Some starting intention is needed in order to raise intention energy; no consequence stated."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:TranserfingVisualizingTheWideningChannelsCh11 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingNamerenie ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingVisualizingTheWideningChannelsCh11 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Visualizing the widening channels"@en, "Visualisieren der sich weitenden Kanäle"@de ;
    skos:definition "During the energy exercise switch on the fountains and repeat inwardly the affirmation that your channels widen and your intention energy grows; picture it as a process improving day by day (today better than yesterday, tomorrow better than today)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAffirmationVisualizationYieldsIntentionEnergyCh11 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Affirmation visualization yields intention energy"@en, "Affirmationsvisualisierung bewirkt Absichtsenergie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Visualizing the widening is said to make intention self-supporting and raise energy steadily."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingVisualizingTheWideningChannelsCh11 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingIncreasedEnergyOfIntentionCh11 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingIncreasedEnergyOfIntentionCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Increased energy of intention"@en, "Gesteigerte Absichtsenergie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Wider channels and rising intention energy, so that intention sustains itself and energy keeps climbing; it powers outer intention."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingZealBlocksTheFlowDistractedEffortIsWastedCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Zeal blocks the flow; distracted effort is wasted"@en, "Eifer blockiert den Fluss; zerstreute Mühe ist vergeudet"@de ;
    skos:definition "Intention to improve the biofield must be free of importance and desire potentials: eagerness and gusto in boosting the flow produce the opposite, a block; doing the exercises with maximum effort while the mind dreams elsewhere wastes time and energy. Intention needs focus on the process, not zeal."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Intention to improve the biofield must be free of importance and desire potentials: eagerness and gusto in boosting the flow produce the opposite, a block; doing the exercises with maximum effort while the mind dreams elsewhere wastes time and energy. Intention needs focus on the process, not zeal; it bears on pmp:TranserfingVisualizingTheWideningChannelsCh11, pmp:TranserfingEnergyFountainsAndProtectiveSphereCh11."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. XI Energy, section 'The Step of Intention'
#

pmc:TranserfingAgeingAsAnInducedTransitionCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Ageing as an induced transition"@en, "Altern als induzierter Übergang"@de ;
    skos:definition "From the Transurfing standpoint ageing is held to be the longest induced transition, driven by a script taught from birth (health declines, the body withers, death) and confirmed by experience; physiology is only one part, the share of the transition is unknown but its existence matters; birthday wishes for health in fact signal decline and are small swings of a destructive pendulum. A thought experiment: a newborn raised among people living about three centuries would be expected to live as long."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'The Step of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHowTheIllnessGameUnfoldsCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "How the illness game unfolds"@en, "Wie das Krankheitsspiel abläuft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sharing feelings of lost vigour finds eager partners; talking about illness makes one emit at the destructive pendulum's frequency, i.e. accept its game. It answers with prods of fatigue or malaise, one worries and concludes one is unwell, it takes the energy and prods harder, a doctor confirms, and by the crisis the pendulum has taken all it can and leaves, unless the transition has cast its victim onto an invalid's life line. Even everyday language ('I was ill', not 'I was healing') shows cure treated as a by-product of the Illness game."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingStagesOfIllness: the spiral is traced for ageing and talk of poor health rather than for an epidemic, ending in recovery or on a line of invalidity."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'The Step of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDoNotRefuseTreatmentOfDevelopedIllnessCh11 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not refuse treatment of developed illness"@en, "Behandlung fortgeschrittener Krankheit nicht verweigern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Turning down possible cure for an illness already advanced is called irresponsible and reckless and offers no exit from the game; the point is to avoid entering the game at all."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingDefeatingAndStillingTheIllnessPendulumCh11 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'The Step of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingDefeatingAndStillingTheIllnessPendulumCh11 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Defeating and stilling the illness pendulum at the start"@en, "Das Krankheitspendel am Anfang besiegen und beruhigen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The game begins when one willingly accepts the symptoms. Counter the pendulum's first push by not taking the symptoms seriously, calmly turning away and forgetting them on the spot; if that fails, still its swing with basic preventive measures; if illness comes, play the Healing game rather than the Illness game."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingFirstProd: the first push is here the acceptance of symptoms, and the counter-moves are named defeating the pendulum and stilling its swing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'The Step of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingIllnessGameVersusHealingGameCh11 a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Illness game versus Healing game"@en, "Krankheitsspiel gegenüber Heilungsspiel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Two opposed games: Illness game = passive suffering, chatting about ailments, whining, demanding care and pity, treating malaise as essential to oneself, parading ill health, eagerly gathering disease information; the player is a passive victim emitting at the destructive pendulum's frequency and is drawn into the vortex. Healing game = active interest in cures, efforts at healthy living, humour toward the illness, attention on feeling better, striving for health, contact with like-minded people; the player is an active creator who moves to healthy life lines. A third, impure variant is the game of being ill and waiting to be cured by others."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'The Step of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingPlayingTheHealingGameCh11 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Playing the Healing game"@en, "Das Heilungsspiel spielen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Take an active interest in possible cures, work at a healthy lifestyle, treat the illness with humour, keep attention on feeling better, aim at health, and associate with like-minded people; check that you play it sincerely, not under duress."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'The Step of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHealingGameYieldsShiftToHealthyLinesCh11 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Healing game yields shift to healthy lines"@en, "Heilungsspiel bewirkt Wechsel auf gesunde Linien"@de ;
    skos:definition "Playing the Healing game as active creator is said to shift one onto healthy life lines."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingPlayingTheHealingGameCh11 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingShiftOntoHealthyLifeLinesCh11 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'The Step of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingShiftOntoHealthyLifeLinesCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Shift onto healthy life lines"@en, "Wechsel auf gesunde Lebenslinien"@de ;
    skos:definition "As active master of one's life one is said to steer one's fate and move to life lines of health; radiating at the frequency of healthy lines."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'The Step of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingInsincereHealingGameEqualsTheIllnessGameCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Insincere healing game equals the illness game"@en, "Unaufrichtiges Heilungsspiel gleicht dem Krankheitsspiel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Knowing one should live healthily but slipping back through laziness and old habits, following rules only from duress, is an unclean game; energetically it equals the Illness game, since impure, insincere intention gives the same results."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Knowing one should live healthily but slipping back through laziness and old habits, following rules only from duress, is an unclean game; energetically it equals the Illness game, since impure, insincere intention gives the same results; it bears on pmp:TranserfingPlayingTheHealingGameCh11."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'The Step of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAbandonSelfCoercionCh11 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Abandon self-coercion"@en, "Selbstzwang aufgeben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Whoever plays the coerced game should give up self-coercion, because it frightens the subconscious, which will prevail in the end."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingPlayingTheHealingGameCh11 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'The Step of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSelfCoercedDietingBackfiresCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Self-coerced dieting backfires"@en, "Erzwungene Diät schlägt zurück"@de ;
    skos:definition "Dieting by self-torture while loathing one's figure is a tainted game: hating the weight emits at the frequency of lines where the figure matches that feeling; coercion brings at best small temporary results, frightens the subconscious into resistance, and ends with the diet dropped and more weight gained than before."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingDwellingOnFlaws: the mechanism is applied to dieting under self-coercion, with the subconscious added as the force that undoes it."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Dieting by self-torture while loathing one's figure is a tainted game: hating the weight emits at the frequency of lines where the figure matches that feeling; coercion brings at best small temporary results, frightens the subconscious into resistance, and ends with the diet dropped and more weight gained than before; it bears on pmc:TranserfingShiftOntoHealthyLifeLinesCh11."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'The Step of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLifestyleChangeFromConvictionBeforeHealthyLinesCh11 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Lifestyle change from conviction before healthy lines"@en, "Lebensstilwechsel aus Überzeugung vor gesunden Linien"@de ;
    skos:definition "Health and beauty require changing lifestyle, dropping old habits and taking new ones out of conviction rather than necessity, with strong, pure motivation and intention; doing as before means one can neither emit at the frequency of healthy lines nor move onto them. Such change is said to need intention and not much time."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingShiftOntoHealthyLifeLinesCh11 ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingJoiningTheHealthyLifestyleCampCh11 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "No radiation at, and no transition to, healthy life lines." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'The Step of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. XI Energy, section 'Illness Pendulums'
#

pmc:TranserfingIllnessPendulumsAndMedicalPendulumsCh11 a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Illness pendulums and medical pendulums"@en, "Krankheitspendel und medizinische Pendel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Illness pendulums are held to be among the strongest pendulums: diseases and epidemics themselves, plus the opposing medical pendulums (clinics, sanatoriums, research bodies, factories, pharmacies, schools). Their declared goal is fighting disease, their true task is to keep and recruit adherents by persuading people they are ill and must take medicine; they feed on the negative energy of illness and are easily recognized by luring with information about diseases and cures."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "illness pendulum; medical pendulum" ;
    pm:nameRole "destructive pendulums feeding on illness-related energy" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Illness Pendulums'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHeldByAnIllnessPendulumHealthCannotReturnCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Held by an illness pendulum, health cannot return"@en, "Im Griff des Krankheitspendels kehrt die Gesundheit nicht zurück"@de ;
    skos:definition "Nobody gripped by a pendulum of illness or of medicine can regain the carefree health of youth; with age everyone grows more susceptible; once one emits at its frequency one loses energy, becomes dependent and slides onto illness-laden life lines."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Nobody gripped by a pendulum of illness or of medicine can regain the carefree health of youth; with age everyone grows more susceptible; once one emits at its frequency one loses energy, becomes dependent and slides onto illness-laden life lines; it bears on pmc:TranserfingShiftOntoHealthyLifeLinesCh11."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Illness Pendulums'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCuttingTiesWithPendulumsBeforeRegainingHealthCh11 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Cutting ties with pendulums before regaining health"@en, "Bindungen an Pendel kappen vor Rückgewinnung der Gesundheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Every pendulum tie has to be severed to win back former health; otherwise one stays in their grip and cannot recover youthful health."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingShiftOntoHealthyLifeLinesCh11 ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingCuttingTiesWithIllnessPendulumsCh11 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Former health cannot be reclaimed while held by the pendulum." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Illness Pendulums'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCuttingTiesYieldsReturnToHealthCh11 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Cutting ties yields return to health"@en, "Bindungen kappen bewirkt Rückkehr zur Gesundheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Severing pendulum ties is said to allow former health to be reclaimed."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingCuttingTiesWithIllnessPendulumsCh11 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingShiftOntoHealthyLifeLinesCh11 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Illness Pendulums'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingCuttingTiesWithIllnessPendulumsCh11 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Cutting ties with illness pendulums"@en, "Bindungen an Krankheitspendel kappen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Block all information produced by illness pendulums; decline to take part in their games (defeating the pendulum); if seriously ill, play the Healing game, looking after the whole body (stilling its swing)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Illness Pendulums'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCovertProgrammingByMedicineAdvertisingCh11 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Covert programming by medicine advertising"@en, "Verdeckte Programmierung durch Arzneiwerbung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Drug adverts are said to plant a double program in semi-conscious viewers: buy the medicine and life falls into place, and more insidiously, you are like these attractive successful people who all have a health problem, i.e. you are predisposed, already sick or soon will be."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingIllnessPendulumsAndMedicalPendulumsCh11 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Illness Pendulums'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHealthPrognosesInWeatherForecastsCh11 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Health prognoses in weather forecasts"@en, "Gesundheitsprognosen im Wetterbericht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Forecasts listing which ailments magnetic storms or pressure changes will aggravate are said to program destructive expectations, especially in the elderly, who prepare beforehand to suffer; such factors occur almost daily."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingIllnessPendulumsAndMedicalPendulumsCh11 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Illness Pendulums'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAvoidIllnessTalkWithFriendsAndRelativesCh11 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Avoid illness talk with friends and relatives"@en, "Krankheitsgespräche mit Freunden und Verwandten meiden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Conversations about ailments and medicine, rather than strengthening health, make participants emit at illness-pendulum frequency, an energy as contagious as germs; avoid such company or illness frequencies will creep up on you."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingIllnessPendulumsAndMedicalPendulumsCh11 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Illness Pendulums'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingIgnoringOrMockingIllnessInformationCh11 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Ignoring or mocking illness information"@en, "Krankheitsinformation ignorieren oder verspotten"@de ;
    skos:definition "When an illness pendulum lures with disease and treatment information, let it pass without taking it seriously (defeat); or meet it with healthy laughter and a few jibes (stilling its swing)."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingParodyOrIgnoring: the same pair of moves, ignoring to defeat and laughter to still, is applied to news about diseases and cures."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Illness Pendulums'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingIllnessPendulumWithdrawsCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Illness pendulum withdraws"@en, "Krankheitspendel zieht sich zurück"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: ignored, the pendulum loses heart and leaves you; laughed at, it flees in the other direction."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingIgnoringOrMockingIllnessInformationCh11."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Illness Pendulums'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFreedomFromIllnessPendulumsIsShortLivedCh11 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Freedom from illness pendulums is short-lived"@en, "Freiheit von Krankheitspendeln ist kurzlebig"@de ;
    skos:definition "Parting with illness pendulums brings full freedom but not for long, since people tend to join some pendulum and will again risk their illnesses; leaving the limbo requires siding with recovery pendulums."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingCuttingTiesWithIllnessPendulumsCh11 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Illness Pendulums'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRecoveryPendulumsCh11 a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Recovery pendulums"@en, "Genesungspendel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pendulums said to govern everything concerned with strengthening body and spirit; becoming their adherent protects against illness pendulums."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "recovery pendulum" ;
    pm:nameRole "benign pendulum of health and strengthening" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Illness Pendulums'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingJoiningTheHealthyLifestyleCampCh11 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Joining the healthy-lifestyle camp"@en, "Anhänger eines gesunden Lebensstils werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Join the recovery pendulums by adopting and consistently keeping a healthy lifestyle, caring for oneself instead of fighting disease."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingUsingPendulums: the harmless pendulums to join are named as those of recovery and healthy living."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Illness Pendulums'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHealthyLifestyleYieldsHealthyLinesAndProtectionCh11 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Healthy lifestyle yields healthy lines and protection"@en, "Gesunder Lebensstil bewirkt gesunde Linien und Schutz"@de ;
    skos:definition "Consistent self-care is said to make one emit at healthy-line frequency and leave no room for illness."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingJoiningTheHealthyLifestyleCampCh11 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingShiftOntoHealthyLifeLinesCh11 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Illness Pendulums'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHealingIllnessVersusCaringForHealthCh11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Healing illness versus caring for health"@en, "Krankheit heilen gegenüber Gesundheit pflegen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Two contrasting life styles: one built on curing illness, tied to inner intention; one on looking after health, tied to outer intention; the choice is one's own. The summary adds that inner intention is fixed on being ill and recovering, outer on healthy living."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XI Energy, section 'Illness Pendulums'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. XII Frailing, section 'Intention in Relationships'
#

pmc:TranserfingIntentionToGiveYieldsReceivingCh12 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Intention to give yields receiving"@en, "Absicht zu geben bewirkt Empfangen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Substituting giving for receiving is said to bring what was relinquished; the chapter motto states the same."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingReplacingTheIntentionToReceiveWithTheIntentionCh12 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingReceivingWhatOneLetGoCh12 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Intention in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingOuterIntentionInRelationshipsCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Outer intention in relationships"@en, "Äußere Absicht in Beziehungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Problems and achievements arise from relationships. Outer intention is elusive and not subject to will, but can be set going implicitly: if one releases one's own inner intention, outer intention is said to activate others' inner intention so that it works independently in one's favour. Using others' inner intention means not obstructing them from doing what they truly want; conflicts arise from clashing inner intentions and are solved by finding common ground."@en ;
    skos:note "Inner and outer intention: pmc:TranserfingVnutrenneeNamerenie, pmc:TranserfingVneshneeNamerenie."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Intention in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSelfWorthAsTheRootOfInnerIntentionCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Self-worth as the root of inner intention"@en, "Selbstwert als Kern der inneren Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Self-worth, tied to inner importance, is held to drive most people's intentions in a pendulum world; the soul's needs account for only a small, underdeveloped share, drowned by the constant need to uphold self-esteem."@en ;
    skos:note "Inner importance: pmc:TranserfingVazhnost."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Intention in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDoNotChangeOthersOrYourselfCh12 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not change others or yourself"@en, "Weder andere noch sich selbst ändern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Against the common advice to change yourself if changing others fails: neither change others nor yourself; any such effort is ineffective, harmful inner intention. Instead allow others to realize their inner intention, which stirs outer intention."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingVnutrenneeNamerenie ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Intention in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPressuringAPartnerBackfiresCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Pressuring a partner backfires"@en, "Druck auf den Partner schlägt zurück"@de ;
    skos:definition "Example: a woman pressing a reluctant partner to marry builds excess potential from strong desire and importance, turns love into a dependent relationship ('if you loved me...'), and balanced forces are said to take the partner away."@en ;
    skos:note "Excess potential and balancing forces: pmc:TranserfingIzbytochnyPotentsial, pmc:TranserfingUravnoveshivayushchieSily."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Example: a woman pressing a reluctant partner to marry builds excess potential from strong desire and importance, turns love into a dependent relationship ('if you loved me...'), and balanced forces are said to take the partner away; it bears on pmp:TranserfingRealizingTheOthersInnerIntentionCh12."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Intention in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingOwnNeedsMetThroughOthersFulfilmentCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Own needs met through others’ fulfilment"@en, "Eigene Bedürfnisse erfüllt durch die Erfüllung anderer"@de ;
    skos:definition "Turning inner into outer intention is said to fulfil one's own aims and similar needs almost of their own accord; the 'open window' lies where one usually does not look."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Intention in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingRealizingTheOthersInnerIntentionCh12 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Realizing the other’s inner intention"@en, "Die innere Absicht des anderen verwirklichen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Drop attachment to getting what you want from the other; ask what the focus of their inner intention is (e.g. what a man seeks in marriage: to be loved, valued, respected, admired); then redirect your own inner intention to helping fulfil theirs, which turns it into outer intention. If you think the person does not deserve this, ask why you are with them; no self-change is needed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Intention in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingServingTheOthersIntentionYieldsOwnFulfilmentCh12 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Serving the other’s intention yields own fulfilment"@en, "Dienst an der Absicht des anderen bewirkt eigene Erfüllung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Directing energy to meeting the other's needs is said to realize one's own goal and needs."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingRealizingTheOthersInnerIntentionCh12 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingOwnNeedsMetThroughOthersFulfilmentCh12 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Intention in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAimingToSeemUnaffectedDoesNotWorkCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Aiming to seem unaffected does not work"@en, "Das Ziel, ungekünstelt zu wirken, scheitert"@de ;
    skos:definition "Setting oneself the goal of acting unaffected fails; trying to make people interested in one's own person is useless, being an expression of inner intention; while trying to draw attention one thinks only of oneself."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Setting oneself the goal of acting unaffected fails; trying to make people interested in one's own person is useless, being an expression of inner intention; while trying to draw attention one thinks only of oneself; it bears on pmc:TranserfingNaturalEaseInCompanyCh12."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Intention in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingEliminatedImportanceBeforeUnaffectednessCh12 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Eliminated importance before unaffectedness"@en, "Beseitigte Wichtigkeit vor Ungezwungenheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Unaffectedness is attainable only by removing importance; since that is not instant, attention-shifting is offered as the workaround."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingNaturalEaseInCompanyCh12 ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingReducingImportance ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Natural, unaffected behaviour is not reached." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Intention in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingShiftingAttentionFromSelfToOthersCh12 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Shifting attention from self to others"@en, "Aufmerksamkeit vom Selbst auf andere lenken"@de ;
    skos:definition "At a party or in talk: remember others are busy with themselves; activate the Guardian and stop playing at raising your own worth; play at raising others' significance; show interest, listen, observe, go with the flow without fawning; talk about what interests them, including themselves."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Intention in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAttentionToOthersYieldsNaturalEaseCh12 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Attention to others yields natural ease"@en, "Aufmerksamkeit für andere bewirkt Ungezwungenheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once attention moves from self to others, excess importance fades automatically and natural behaviour follows."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingShiftingAttentionFromSelfToOthersCh12 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingNaturalEaseInCompanyCh12 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Intention in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNaturalEaseInCompanyCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Natural ease in company"@en, "Natürliche Ungezwungenheit in Gesellschaft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Behaving naturally and freely because the excess potential of self-importance has faded."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Intention in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingOthersSeekOnesAcquaintanceCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Others seek one’s acquaintance"@en, "Andere suchen die Bekanntschaft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: once inner intention becomes outer, people at once become interested in meeting you."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingShiftingAttentionFromSelfToOthersCh12."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Intention in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAttractingOthersInterestAndGoodwillCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Attracting others’ interest and goodwill"@en, "Interesse und Zuneigung anderer gewinnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Others become keen to know one and are won over, sensing their own worth confirmed beside one; said to work with subtle, irresistible force."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Intention in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAttentionToOthersYieldsTheirInterestCh12 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Attention to others yields their interest"@en, "Aufmerksamkeit für andere bewirkt deren Interesse"@de ;
    skos:definition "Showing interest in others fulfils their inner intention, so they become interested in the one who fulfilled it."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingShiftingAttentionFromSelfToOthersCh12 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingAttractingOthersInterestAndGoodwillCh12 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Intention in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPeopleJudgeFitByTheirOwnFeltWorthCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "People judge fit by their own felt worth"@en, "Menschen beurteilen Passung nach dem eigenen Wertgefühl"@de ;
    skos:definition "Except toward celebrities, people regard one as a possible business partner, friend or lover and judge how well one fits a script where they feel fulfilled, i.e. liked, interesting, respected, valued; one's merits and faults matter little; dazzling qualities can even hinder, as others fear fading beside them, and many stars are lonely."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Intention in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingShowInterestSincerelyNotAsTechniqueCh12 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Show interest sincerely, not as technique"@en, "Interesse aufrichtig zeigen, nicht als Technik"@de ;
    skos:definition "Interest must be sincere; the other must not sense a learned manipulative technique or a hidden agenda; someone whose goodwill you want at least deserves sincerity."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingShiftingAttentionFromSelfToOthersCh12, pmp:TranserfingLettingThePartnerBeTheInterestingOneCh12 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Intention in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingLettingThePartnerBeTheInterestingOneCh12 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Letting the partner be the interesting one"@en, "Den Gesprächspartner interessant sein lassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Instead of displaying cleverness and name-dropping, set the task of letting the partner appear interesting: tune into their frequency, listen attentively, ask questions, show interest in their chosen topic and their life; set your own personality aside so theirs can shine."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Intention in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHoursOfConversationAndAWonOverPartnerCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Hours of conversation and a won-over partner"@en, "Stundenlanges Gespräch und gewonnener Partner"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: such a conversation can run for hours with the partner mostly talking; at the end they are sure they met a fascinating confidant and fine person, and become an eager admirer."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingLettingThePartnerBeTheInterestingOneCh12."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Intention in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLettingOthersShineYieldsWhatWasSacrificedCh12 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Letting others shine yields what was sacrificed"@en, "Andere glänzen lassen bewirkt das Geopferte"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sacrificing the spotlight for another's personality is said to return the very thing sacrificed."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingLettingThePartnerBeTheInterestingOneCh12 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingAttractingOthersInterestAndGoodwillCh12 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Intention in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingGainingAnUninterestedPersonsAttentionCh12 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Gaining an uninterested person’s attention"@en, "Aufmerksamkeit einer desinteressierten Person gewinnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "For someone not interested, e.g. in a business proposal: put yourself and the proposal aside, give them full attention, take real interest in all they are engaged in and take time to talk; only then will they attend to your matter."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Intention in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingReplacingTheIntentionToReceiveWithTheIntentionCh12 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Replacing the intention to receive with the intention to give"@en, "Die Absicht zu empfangen durch die Absicht zu geben ersetzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Universal principle when wanting something from someone: give it instead of waiting for it. For respect, treat them with respect and show they matter to you; for compassion and gratitude, share in others' problems and care sincerely; to be found attractive, show others you find them attractive; for help, help others; for mutual love, drop possessiveness and dependent relationships and love without expecting return."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Intention in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingReceivingWhatOneLetGoCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Receiving what one let go of"@en, "Das Losgelassene empfangen"@de ;
    skos:definition "One is said inevitably to receive the very thing one stopped trying to get; love given without expectation is called rare and irresistible."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Intention in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingArrangingThingsSoOthersWantToHelpCh12 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Arranging things so others want to help"@en, "Die Dinge so fügen, dass andere helfen wollen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rather than force (requires power) or persuasion: define the other's needs and lacks (money, power, respect, pride in work, children's welfare, prestige, leadership, recognition: all forms of self-worth); work out how your task would raise their self-worth; present it in that light; let them feel more valued and appreciate them generously. Wake up, step out of your own interests; while helping fulfil their inner intention, mention your need casually in passing, or not at all."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Intention in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingStrivingForSelfWorthIsLegitimateCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Striving for self-worth is legitimate"@en, "Streben nach Selbstwert ist berechtigt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Everyone seeks more self-worth in their own way; nobody should be judged for it; worse is someone who stops developing and wants nothing, which is rare."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Intention in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLinkingTasksToSelfWorthYieldsWillingCooperationCh12 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Linking tasks to self-worth yields willing cooperation"@en, "Verknüpfen von Aufgaben mit Selbstwert bewirkt freiwillige Mitwirkung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Guided by this principle one easily prompts others to act; outer intention merely wishes things to go one's way."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingArrangingThingsSoOthersWantToHelpCh12 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingOthersActInOnesInterestOfTheirOwnCh12 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Intention in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingSellingByFindingWhatTheBuyerWantsCh12 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Selling by finding what the buyer wants"@en, "Verkaufen durch Erkunden der Käuferwünsche"@de ;
    skos:definition "Do not think how to sell; think what the buyer wishes to buy, as buyers want to choose, not be sold to; take a genuine interest (e.g. recommend a doctor or treatment to a customer with rheumatism) and the purchase follows; the principle is called infallible though the example is simplified."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Intention in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingBuyerFocusYieldsSalesCh12 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Buyer-focus yields sales"@en, "Käuferorientierung bewirkt Verkäufe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Genuine interest in the buyer is said to make them buy from you."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingSellingByFindingWhatTheBuyerWantsCh12 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingOthersActInOnesInterestOfTheirOwnCh12 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Intention in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingOthersActInOnesInterestOfTheirOwnCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Others act in one’s interest of their own accord"@en, "Andere handeln von selbst im eigenen Interesse"@de ;
    skos:definition "People are said to act for one while pursuing their own concerns, often without one even hinting at one's need; things unfold by themselves, called the magic of outer intention."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Intention in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingIssuingAChallengeToInduceInnerIntentionCh12 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Issuing a challenge to induce inner intention"@en, "Eine Herausforderung stellen, um innere Absicht zu wecken"@de ;
    skos:definition "To induce another's inner intention, consider how doing what you need would raise their self-worth and frame it as a challenge, to a person or group: asking who is best, appealing to professional honour (not losing face), or to inner importance (showing what they are made of)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Intention in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAcceptedChallengeYieldsCommitmentCh12 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Accepted challenge yields commitment"@en, "Angenommene Herausforderung bewirkt Einsatz"@de ;
    skos:definition "Someone accepting the challenge in terms of self-worth carries out your will as their own, with commitment."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingIssuingAChallengeToInduceInnerIntentionCh12 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingOthersActInOnesInterestOfTheirOwnCh12 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Intention in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. XII Frailing, section 'The Flow of Relationships'
#

pmc:TranserfingTheMasterpieceStanceFailsThreeWaysCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The masterpiece stance fails three ways"@en, "Die Meisterwerk-Haltung scheitert dreifach"@de ;
    skos:definition "Assuming people must buy because the product is a masterpiece is flawed: it rests on inner importance, so one lacks the indifference to judge it; inner intention aims at selling while buyers do not see a masterpiece and care nothing for another's wish to sell; and it centres on the product rather than customer needs, yielding perfect products nobody needs."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Assuming people must buy because the product is a masterpiece is flawed: it rests on inner importance, so one lacks the indifference to judge it; inner intention aims at selling while buyers do not see a masterpiece and care nothing for another's wish to sell; and it centres on the product rather than customer needs, yielding perfect products nobody needs; it bears on pmc:TranserfingVnutrenneeNamerenie."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'The Flow of Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingOuterIntentionGoesWithTheFlowOfAlternativesCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Outer intention goes with the flow of alternatives"@en, "Äußere Absicht folgt dem Alternativenfluss"@de ;
    skos:definition "The outer-intention stance determines what people want, lack, need and are moved by; it follows the flow of alternatives. The mind idealizes its abilities, is absorbed in creation and seeks control, but demand follows its own course and is costly to steer; the mind cannot forecast market trends and need not: it is enough to keep pace with the flow and note small shifts."@en ;
    skos:note "The flow of alternatives is pmc:TranserfingTechenieVariantov."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'The Flow of Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingInventionsAheadOfTheirTimeRarelyPayCh12 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Inventions ahead of their time rarely pay"@en, "Erfindungen vor ihrer Zeit zahlen sich selten aus"@de ;
    skos:definition "Demand need not be invented: nearly all premature inventions are never implemented or profitable; staking income on a personal masterpiece ahead of its time likely loses, barring a rare brilliant winner-takes-all case. Only ventures serving customers' present demand are said to be assured of success."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingTrackingDemandWithTheFlowCh12 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'The Flow of Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingTrackingDemandWithTheFlowCh12 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Tracking demand with the flow"@en, "Nachfrage mit dem Fluss verfolgen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Do not try to make people want your product, which is near impossible; going with the flow, keep track of what customers want and which of their needs are already covered, and note small changes in the course of demand."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'The Flow of Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSuccessGuaranteedByTheAlternativesFlowCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Success guaranteed by the alternatives flow"@en, "Durch den Alternativenfluss gesicherter Erfolg"@de ;
    skos:definition "The flow is said to hold all answers and to be the sole guarantor of success; heeding it lets many obstacles pass one by."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'The Flow of Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMaterialRealizationMovesThroughTheAlternativesSpaceCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Material realization moves through the alternatives space"@en, "Materielle Verwirklichung wandert durch den Alternativenraum"@de ;
    skos:definition "Near-simultaneous discoveries by different people are taken as showing how material realization moves through the alternatives space; whatever must arise has its time, as with Leonardo's long-unbuilt inventions."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'The Flow of Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFollowingTheFlowYieldsSuccessCh12 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Following the flow yields success"@en, "Dem Fluss folgen bewirkt Erfolg"@de ;
    skos:definition "Remembering the flow as a gift for the mind and making use of it is said to let many obstacles pass untouched."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingTrackingDemandWithTheFlowCh12 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingSuccessGuaranteedByTheAlternativesFlowCh12 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'The Flow of Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNeverCriticiseOrBlameCh12 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Never criticise or blame"@en, "Niemals kritisieren oder beschuldigen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Criticism springs from inner intention and amounts to fighting the outside world: people always take offence whether fair or not, nobody is convinced they are wrong, one creates excess potential and suffers oneself; dominance through it means taking the manipulator's role; it knocks people off balance and off their course. Abandon criticism and blame."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingModerateCriticism: criticism of others is now ruled out altogether, not only kept moderate."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingVnutrenneeNamerenie ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'The Flow of Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingEncouragingInsteadOfCriticisingCh12 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Encouraging instead of criticising"@en, "Ermutigen statt kritisieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Accept others' shortcomings and emphasize their positive qualities in every case; encouragement nudges them toward a good direction without breaking their flow, injures no right or pride, and aligns their wishes with yours."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'The Flow of Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGuardianAsInnerWitnessCh12 a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Guardian as inner witness"@en, "Wächter als innerer Zeuge"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Guardian is held to be the inner witness: unless dozing, it always finds a reason behind the conduct of someone one wanted to judge and keeps one from plunging into the game of dispute; switched on when waking up."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingInnerGuardian: as inner witness it now also supplies a reason for another's conduct before one judges it, and keeps one out of quarrels."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Guardian" ;
    pm:nameRole "inner witness" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'The Flow of Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingEncouragementYieldsAlignedInterestsCh12 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Encouragement yields aligned interests"@en, "Ermutigung bewirkt gleichgerichtete Interessen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Encouraging people is said to make interests coincide and the situation to unfold favourably."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingEncouragingInsteadOfCriticisingCh12 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingAlignedInterestsAndWillingAlliesCh12 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'The Flow of Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAlignedInterestsAndWillingAlliesCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Aligned interests and willing allies"@en, "Gleichgerichtete Interessen und bereitwillige Verbündete"@de ;
    skos:definition "Others' desires run parallel to one's own; they become allies rather than opponents, grateful and well disposed, and the situation develops to one's benefit."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'The Flow of Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCriticismSetsHeartAgainstMindCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Criticism sets heart against mind"@en, "Kritik stellt das Herz gegen den Verstand"@de ;
    skos:definition "Coercion reaches only the mind; the heart does what it wants or obstructs the mind; criticism turns the heart into the mind's enemy, encouragement into its ally; encouragement creates, criticism destroys. Good managers build enthusiasm instead of fault-finding."@en ;
    skos:note "Heart and mind stand for pmc:TranserfingDusha and pmc:TranserfingRazum."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'The Flow of Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingWatchingDisputesAsASpectatorCh12 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Watching disputes as a spectator"@en, "Streit als Zuschauer beobachten"@de ;
    skos:definition "To avoid being drawn in, wake up and switch on the inner Guardian; step back and observe as a spectator; in a group debate descend mentally into the auditorium and watch; argue only when the issue is critical and your interests leave no retreat; otherwise let others flail; you may offer the solution you see but never force it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'The Flow of Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSpectatorStanceYieldsOverviewCh12 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Spectator stance yields overview"@en, "Zuschauerhaltung bewirkt Überblick"@de ;
    skos:definition "Watching instead of insisting is said to reveal unseen solutions."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingWatchingDisputesAsASpectatorCh12 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingSeeingSolutionsDisputantsMissCh12 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'The Flow of Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSeeingSolutionsDisputantsMissCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Seeing solutions disputants miss"@en, "Lösungen sehen, die Streitenden entgehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "As judicious onlooker, having flown back from the window pane, one is said to see a solution none of the disputants would think of."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'The Flow of Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWinningAnArgumentIsADefeatCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Winning an argument is a defeat"@en, "Einen Streit zu gewinnen ist eine Niederlage"@de ;
    skos:definition "Arguing to the end makes enemies; a won debate never pays and may benefit the opponent; the loser, even if formally conceding, privately keeps counter-arguments and carries a silent, subconscious wound to self-worth that eventually brings trouble, and never acknowledges the winner's new standing."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingReliefOverWinning: the cost of a won argument is placed in the loser's wounded self-worth, which goes on hurting unseen."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Arguing to the end makes enemies; a won debate never pays and may benefit the opponent; the loser, even if formally conceding, privately keeps counter-arguments and carries a silent, subconscious wound to self-worth that eventually brings trouble, and never acknowledges the winner's new standing; it bears on pmp:TranserfingWatchingDisputesAsASpectatorCh12."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'The Flow of Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNeverInjureAnothersSelfEsteemCh12 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Never injure another’s self-esteem"@en, "Niemals das Selbstwertgefühl anderer verletzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Showing someone one is better than them reliably turns them against one; avoid wounding self-esteem like the plague, treat it as taboo, following the slogan not to make idols nor create enemies; this spares endless problems whose cause stays hidden."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingSelfWorthAsTheRootOfInnerIntentionCh12 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'The Flow of Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingMeetingAnArguerHalfWayCh12 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Meeting an arguer half-way"@en, "Dem Streitenden auf halbem Weg entgegenkommen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Recognize that an opponent is defending their self-worth; agree with the point they are reaching for, giving them what they want; then state your own view calmly without insisting or proving."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'The Flow of Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAgreeingYieldsSuperiorOutcomesCh12 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Agreeing yields superior outcomes"@en, "Zustimmung bewirkt überlegene Ergebnisse"@de ;
    skos:definition "This both goes with the flow and implements outer intention, with results said to surpass any clever intellectual device."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingMeetingAnArguerHalfWayCh12 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingAlignedInterestsAndWillingAlliesCh12 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'The Flow of Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAFirstNoEndsPersuasionCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A first “no” ends persuasion"@en, "Ein erstes Nein beendet das Überzeugen"@de ;
    skos:definition "If the first reply to one's opening is no, convincing that person of anything is out of the question; they have turned another way and will not go with the flow with their partner."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: If the first reply to one's opening is no, convincing that person of anything is out of the question; they have turned another way and will not go with the flow with their partner; it bears on pmp:TranserfingOpeningAConversationInAgreementCh12."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'The Flow of Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingOpeningAConversationInAgreementCh12 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Opening a conversation in agreement"@en, "Ein Gespräch in Zustimmung eröffnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Set an agreeing tone from the start: open so that the first word your partner says is yes; never begin with a sensitive issue; any topic will do as long as they agree; later steer smoothly toward contentious points, both moving by inertia in the same direction."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'The Flow of Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingAdmittingAMistakeBeforeBeingBlamedCh12 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Admitting a mistake before being blamed"@en, "Einen Fehler eingestehen, bevor man beschuldigt wird"@de ;
    skos:definition "When fairly expecting blame, do not arm yourself to defend; step forward and own the mistake first, agreeing in advance with the accuser's line; this realizes their wish to set you right and enlarges them, while your voluntary step keeps your self-esteem intact."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'The Flow of Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTheAccuserTurnsGenerousCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The accuser turns generous"@en, "Der Ankläger wird großzügig"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: the person ready to deliver just wrath is likely to become magnanimous and grateful, and one's own integrity is kept."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingAdmittingAMistakeBeforeBeingBlamedCh12."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'The Flow of Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSelfJustificationFeedsPendulumsCh12 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Self-justification feeds pendulums"@en, "Selbstrechtfertigung nährt Pendel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Defending and justifying one's mistakes is rowing against the tide and hands energy to pendulums; the urge comes from heightened inner importance. Grant yourself the right to err, and acknowledge mistakes instead of justifying them; relief follows at once. Others' remarks hurt only where inner importance is raised."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingRefusingGuilt: self-justification is traced to inflated inner importance and said to pass energy to pendulums."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingAdmittingAMistakeBeforeBeingBlamedCh12 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'The Flow of Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingTellingOthersTheyWereRightCh12 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Telling others they were right"@en, "Anderen sagen, dass sie recht hatten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Drop importance, accept that a critic or adviser was right, or at least keep it in mind, and tell them aloud they were right, though not obliged to; when someone proves right while others keep silent, say so openly, acting as witness of their good sense."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'The Flow of Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAcknowledgingOthersYieldsAlliesCh12 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Acknowledging others yields allies"@en, "Anerkennung anderer bewirkt Verbündete"@de ;
    skos:definition "Openly granting that someone was right is said to win their favour: they are relieved of defending themselves, feel grateful and see one as ally, mostly subconsciously; many allies can be found this way."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingTellingOthersTheyWereRightCh12 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingAlignedInterestsAndWillingAlliesCh12 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'The Flow of Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMindfulnessEasesWitnessingOthersRightnessCh12 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Mindfulness eases witnessing others’ rightness"@en, "Achtsamkeit erleichtert das Bezeugen fremder Richtigkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "With practised mindfulness, taking the role of witness to others' right-mindedness becomes easy and even fun; the stated advantage is conscious awareness, absence of importance and readiness to give attention, while others sleep."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:TranserfingTellingOthersTheyWereRightCh12 ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingConstantAwareness ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:presentationOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'The Flow of Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. XII Frailing, section 'Attuning to Fraile'
#

pmc:TranserfingWithoutAttunementNoMutualUnderstandingCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Without attunement no mutual understanding"@en, "Ohne Einstimmung kein gegenseitiges Verständnis"@de ;
    skos:definition "If two people fail to adjust to each other, no mutual understanding arises and their talk stays empty words."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: If two people fail to adjust to each other, no mutual understanding arises and their talk stays empty words; it bears on pmp:TranserfingFrailingSpeakingWithinTheOthersInterestsCh12."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Attuning to Fraile'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFrailingCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fraile and frailing"@en, "Fraile und Frailing"@de ;
    skos:definition "Fraile is the Transurfing term for each person's unique set of personal characteristics; frailing means attuning to them, and the quality of communication depends directly on grasping the partner's fraile. 'Attuning to the partner's frequency' is admitted to be a customary phrase of a deliberately oversimplified model; the physical mechanism is said not to matter. Later the author calls the split between intention-directed and flow-directed relationships purely relative: it all comes down to frailing."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingFreyling: fraile is here the unique set of personality traits met in contact with others, and frailing the act of attuning to someone else's; the frequency picture is called a deliberately simplified model."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Attuning to Fraile'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFullAttentionBeforeAttuningToFraileCh12 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Full attention before attuning to fraile"@en, "Volle Aufmerksamkeit vor der Einstimmung auf Fraile"@de ;
    skos:definition "Giving full attention is called the most important element; without its power attunement cannot even begin, yet people commonly forget this and attend only to their own thoughts."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:TranserfingFrailingSpeakingWithinTheOthersInterestsCh12 ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingShiftingAttentionFromSelfToOthersCh12 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Attunement to the other cannot even start." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Attuning to Fraile'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingFrailingSpeakingWithinTheOthersInterestsCh12 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Frailing: speaking within the other’s interests"@en, "Frailing: im Rahmen der Interessen des anderen sprechen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Consciously focus attention on the partner's interests and shift inner sight from yourself to them; place their intention at the base of the conversation and build your concern on top (e.g. ask for August leave by explaining you want to return fit for September's rising workload rather than complaining of your needs); ask each time how fulfilling your wish benefits the 'donkey' (show the carrot); listen attentively; for an indifferent person talk of what interests them and forget your own topic for a while; put yourself in their shoes; once attuned, move smoothly to your issue."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Attuning to Fraile'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAttunementAndRapportWithAnotherCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Attunement and rapport with another"@en, "Einstimmung und Gleichklang mit einem anderen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Being on the other's wavelength so that requests are heard at their own frequency and they do what one needs; by frailing one achieves what ordinary inner-intention methods never could."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Attuning to Fraile'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFrailingYieldsRapportAndComplianceCh12 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Frailing yields rapport and compliance"@en, "Frailing bewirkt Gleichklang und Entgegenkommen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Speaking in the language of the other's interests is said to attune to their thought energy; finding the answer to the donkey question makes them do what is needed."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingFrailingSpeakingWithinTheOthersInterestsCh12 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingAttunementAndRapportWithAnotherCh12 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Attuning to Fraile'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingUsingThePersonsNameCh12 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Using the person’s name"@en, "Den Namen der Person verwenden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Use the partner's name frequently in conversation; it is called the easiest key to their wavelength, a password signalling friendly intent and recognition of their worth."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Attuning to Fraile'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingUsingNamesYieldsAttunementCh12 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Using names yields attunement"@en, "Namensnennung bewirkt Einstimmung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Calling someone by name often is said to have an effect on attunement."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingUsingThePersonsNameCh12 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingAttunementAndRapportWithAnotherCh12 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Attuning to Fraile'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAWallOfFormalityOrDistrustBlocksAttunementCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A wall of formality or distrust blocks attunement"@en, "Eine Mauer aus Förmlichkeit oder Misstrauen verhindert Einstimmung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Everyone guards self-worth with a protective field; attunement is impossible while the partner sits behind formality or distrust."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Everyone guards self-worth with a protective field; attunement is impossible while the partner sits behind formality or distrust; it bears on pmp:TranserfingFrailingSpeakingWithinTheOthersInterestsCh12."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Attuning to Fraile'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingDissolvingBarriersByShowingGladLikingCh12 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Dissolving barriers by showing glad liking"@en, "Barrieren durch offene Freude auflösen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Use disarming directness, showing you are not shielding your own worth nor ready to pounce, so they lower their screen; most effective is to show sincere liking as pets do: be visibly glad to see the person, smile, greet warmly, use their name, listen attentively; avoid the coolness of an aquarium fish."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Attuning to Fraile'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingShowingGladnessYieldsFellowFeelingCh12 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Showing gladness yields fellow-feeling"@en, "Gezeigte Freude bewirkt Zuneigung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Subconsciously the partner concludes they matter because someone is glad to see them, and finds that person pleasant and attractive."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingDissolvingBarriersByShowingGladLikingCh12 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingAttunementAndRapportWithAnotherCh12 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Attuning to Fraile'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAttentionMustBeGenuineNotEtiquetteCh12 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Attention must be genuine, not etiquette"@en, "Aufmerksamkeit muss echt sein, nicht Etikette"@de ;
    skos:definition "Habitual 'how are you' and smiles worn like an accessory make dialogue sterile and off-putting; attention and participation must be real."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingDissolvingBarriersByShowingGladLikingCh12 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Attuning to Fraile'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingResonatingWithThePersonsForteCh12 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Resonating with the person’s forte"@en, "Mit der Stärke der Person in Resonanz gehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Find what the person is truly passionate about, keen on, or proud of, their resonant string, discuss it and let them express themselves; called the most effective way to connect."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Attuning to Fraile'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCatchingTheForteYieldsEasyWinningOverCh12 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Catching the forte yields easy winning over"@en, "Die Stärke treffen bewirkt leichtes Gewinnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once the thread of the forte is caught, winning the person is said to be easy."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingResonatingWithThePersonsForteCh12 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingAttunementAndRapportWithAnotherCh12 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Attuning to Fraile'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingAskingASmallFavourCh12 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Asking a small favour"@en, "Um einen kleinen Gefallen bitten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ask the person for help with some difficulty or for a small service; you lower your importance and raise theirs, showing you need them and letting them express themselves."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Attuning to Fraile'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAskingFavoursYieldsGoodwillCh12 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Asking favours yields goodwill"@en, "Um Gefallen bitten bewirkt Wohlwollen"@de ;
    skos:definition "If they can render the service they feel needed with you and one wins their favour, remembered for life."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingAskingASmallFavourCh12 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingAttractingOthersInterestAndGoodwillCh12 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Attuning to Fraile'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSelfWorthAsMostCherishedPossessionCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Self-worth as most cherished possession"@en, "Selbstwert als höchstes Gut"@de ;
    skos:definition "After life itself, people are said to value nothing more than self-worth; degradation wounds most deeply; the hunger for power is the final, extreme stage of the struggle for self-worth. The author concedes he may seem to exaggerate this."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Attuning to Fraile'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCriticismAsAntifrailingCh12 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Criticism as antifrailing"@en, "Kritik als Antifrailing"@de ;
    skos:definition "Every form of criticism hits self-worth and is called antifrailing; never say directly to someone that they are wrong, even when sure; neutrality protects their self-worth and shields one from balanced forces."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingFrailingCh12 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Attuning to Fraile'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDoNotTouchOthersNegativeSlidesCh12 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not touch others’ negative slides"@en, "Negative Dias anderer nicht berühren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Negative slides, pictures of what people dislike in themselves hanging on importance's film and projected onto others, are open wounds; handing a projection back provokes a stormy reaction and a likely worst enemy; leave them alone and do not explain them."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingSlayd ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Attuning to Fraile'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLoveAsPerfectFrailingCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Love as perfect frailing"@en, "Liebe als vollkommenes Frailing"@de ;
    skos:definition "Being in love is the most perfect attunement to another's fraile; its origin cannot be explained. Mutual love requires renouncing possession and giving unconditionally; once flowered it can be kept unless it becomes a relation of dependence, but nothing can make one fall in love."@en ;
    skos:note "Fraile: pmc:TranserfingFreyling."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Attuning to Fraile'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. XII Frailing, section 'Energy in Relationships'
#

pmc:TranserfingAnothersUnexplainedGoodwillAndCooperationCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Another’s unexplained goodwill and cooperation"@en, "Unerklärliches Wohlwollen und Entgegenkommen anderer"@de ;
    skos:definition "The other becomes well disposed apparently without reason, does what one asks or eases the problem, and feels comfortable in one's presence."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Energy in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingBeneficialVisualizationYieldsGoodwillCh12 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Beneficial visualization yields goodwill"@en, "Wohltuende Visualisierung bewirkt Wohlwollen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pleasing the person in one's mind is said to deliver an energetic treat like a feel-good film, producing goodwill."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingVisualisingFulfilmentYieldsWinningCooperation: the effect is now explained energetically, as a treat of energy the other feels without knowing its source."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingVisualisingFulfilment ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingAnothersUnexplainedGoodwillAndCooperationCh12 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Energy in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAComfortingWaveFeltByTheOtherCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A comforting wave felt by the other"@en, "Eine wohltuende Welle beim anderen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: if fraile and needs were guessed right, the person feels a sudden soothing wave without knowing its source and feels at ease with you."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingVisualisingFulfilment."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Energy in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSincerityAndHeartMindUnityInVisualizationCh12 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Sincerity and heart-mind unity in visualization"@en, "Aufrichtigkeit und Einheit von Herz und Verstand bei der Visualisierung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The visualization must be done sincerely with heart and mind united; genuine goodwill makes the effect substantial; no consequence of omission named."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:TranserfingVisualisingFulfilment ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingEdinstvoDushiIRazuma ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Energy in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCharmAsUnionOfHeartAndMindCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Charm as union of heart and mind"@en, "Charme als Einheit von Herz und Verstand"@de ;
    skos:definition "Abundant free energy is said to make a person charming, magnetic and charismatic; one's energetic force scales with the free energy one runs and the strength of the heart-mind link; thought programs free energy, more purely the closer heart and mind; charm is mutual love of heart and mind, the radiance of their union; such people live by their own credo, are happy and love themselves without narcissism."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingRadiantCharmBeautyHarmonyCh9: charm is now also tied to the amount of free energy one runs, which spills over as fountains others feel."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Energy in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTurningToTheHeartYieldsCharmCh12 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Turning to the heart yields charm"@en, "Hinwendung zum Herzen bewirkt Charme"@de ;
    skos:definition "Following the heart toward one's goal is said to make one charming and outwardly more attractive."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingTurningToOnesHeartCh12 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingCharmAndChangedAppearanceCh12 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Energy in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingTurningToOnesHeartCh12 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Turning to one’s heart"@en, "Sich dem eigenen Herzen zuwenden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Turn toward your heart, give yourself love, and start walking toward your deepest goal."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingSelfLoveBeforeRadiatingCharmCh9: self-love is here made the practice that yields charm and a changed appearance on the target life line."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Energy in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCharmAndChangedAppearanceCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Charm and changed appearance"@en, "Charme und verändertes Aussehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Personal qualities change, the body grows more attractive, the face softer, the smile enchanting; on the target life line one's appearance, as part of that sector's scenery, matches the energy radiated when one sees one's own perfection (compare photos from dark periods)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Energy in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMeridianTrainingYieldsInfluenceCh12 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Meridian training yields influence"@en, "Meridiantraining bewirkt Einfluss"@de ;
    skos:definition "Training the meridians and raising energy is said to build an uncommon power to sway people and win their goodwill."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingEnergyFountainsAndProtectiveSphereCh11 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingEnergeticInfluenceAndCharismaCh11 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Energy in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingFloodingAGroupWithOnesFountainsCh12 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Flooding a group with one’s fountains"@en, "Eine Gruppe mit den eigenen Fontänen fluten"@de ;
    skos:definition "To be the life of the party, drop importance and switch on the fountains. In a group discussion, where everyone's thought energy sways around one theme, turn on the fountains and let them flood the group; feel your field widen until it takes in every participant."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Energy in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGroupFountainsYieldWeightOfOnesWordsCh12 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Group fountains yield weight of one’s words"@en, "Gruppenfontänen bewirken Gewicht der eigenen Worte"@de ;
    skos:definition "One's remarks are said to carry more weight and others feel the power of one's thoughts; abundant free energy always draws interest and goodwill."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingFloodingAGroupWithOnesFountainsCh12 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingEnergeticInfluenceAndCharismaCh11 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Energy in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingVisualizationPlusFountainsOneToOneCh12 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Visualization plus fountains one to one"@en, "Visualisierung und Fontänen im Zweiergespräch"@de ;
    skos:definition "In a one-to-one talk mentally run a beneficial visualization for the person while your energy fountains run at the same time."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Energy in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCombinedTechniqueYieldsAdvantageInNegotiationsCh12 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Combined technique yields advantage in negotiations"@en, "Kombinierte Technik bewirkt Vorteil in Verhandlungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Said to create the most favourable impression and a large advantage wherever charm or strength is needed: negotiations, exams, job interviews, personal relationships; called an effective, tolerant way of attunement, unlike vampires who pull painful strings."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingVisualizationPlusFountainsOneToOneCh12 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingAnothersUnexplainedGoodwillAndCooperationCh12 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Energy in Relationships'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. XII Frailing, section 'Pardon'
#

pmp:TranserfingPardoningOneselfForShortcomingsCh12 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Pardoning oneself for shortcomings"@en, "Sich die eigenen Mängel vergeben"@de ;
    skos:definition "When you know of shortcomings or missing knowledge that might hinder your goal, accept them and yourself as you are; permit yourself flaws as a luxury; before an event where you must excel (interview, exam, performance, contest, date) let go, take off the cloak of inner importance, grant yourself absolution, and concentrate on your strengths rather than hiding weaknesses."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Pardon'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSelfPardonYieldsReliefAndFreedEnergyCh12 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Self-pardon yields relief and freed energy"@en, "Selbstvergebung bewirkt Erleichterung und freie Energie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Self-acceptance is said to give relief and calm and to release the energy of intention."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingPardoningOneselfForShortcomingsCh12 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingReliefAndReleasedIntentionEnergyCh12 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Pardon'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingConcealedShortcomingsSurfaceAtTheCriticalMomentCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Concealed shortcomings surface at the critical moment"@en, "Verborgene Mängel zeigen sich im entscheidenden Moment"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hiding shortcomings makes them show at the critical moment; failing to accept oneself always appears as obstacles: guilt or inadequacy builds excess potential that balanced forces aggravate, outer intention realizes one's fears, what one blocks enters the script (the one feared question is asked, the one unknown skill demanded), and worst, one tenses or freezes at the key moment."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Hiding shortcomings makes them show at the critical moment; failing to accept oneself always appears as obstacles: guilt or inadequacy builds excess potential that balanced forces aggravate, outer intention realizes one's fears, what one blocks enters the script (the one feared question is asked, the one unknown skill demanded), and worst, one tenses or freezes at the key moment; it bears on pmc:TranserfingReliefAndReleasedIntentionEnergyCh12."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Pardon'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFreeEnergySpentOnGuardingShortcomingsCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Free energy spent on guarding shortcomings"@en, "Freie Energie verbraucht durch das Bewachen von Mängeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Free energy is consumed in sustaining the importance potential, fighting balanced forces and controlling slipping situations; the more importance given to flaws, the harder balanced forces resist and the stronger the flow presses, until intention energy is exhausted, like carrying a squealing piglet that, once released, frees all the energy spent holding it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Pardon'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFeelingOfAWeightLiftedCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Feeling of a weight lifted"@en, "Gefühl einer abgenommenen Last"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: you will notice how much freer and easier you feel, as if a great load had been taken from your shoulders."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingPardoningOneselfForShortcomingsCh12."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Pardon'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingReliefAndReleasedIntentionEnergyCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Relief and released intention energy"@en, "Erleichterung und freigesetzte Absichtsenergie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Inner calm and lightness as excess potential vanishes and intention's energy is set free for other uses."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingFreedEnergy: what is freed is the energy of intention, and the occasion is accepting one's shortcomings before a demanding event."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Pardon'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFightingOnesOwnShortcomingsIsInnerIntentionCh12 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Fighting one’s own shortcomings is inner intention"@en, "Kampf gegen eigene Mängel ist innere Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Struggling against one's flaws is the fly beating on the window pane; eliminating excess potential and freeing energy is the real advantage."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingStopTheFlyBeforeFreedom: the fly at the glass now stands for the fight against one's own shortcomings."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingPardoningOneselfForShortcomingsCh12 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Pardon'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingShiftingFromWorryIntoActionCh12 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Shifting from worry into action"@en, "Vom Grübeln ins Handeln wechseln"@de ;
    skos:definition "If importance cannot be dropped, at least loosen the grip of control and move from worrying to doing: start acting in whatever way you can, regardless of initial effectiveness, and permit yourself to act badly."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingIdleWorry: the remedy is spelled out: loosen control and start doing, allowing oneself to do it badly."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Pardon'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingActionDissipatesImportanceAndFreesIntentionCh12 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Action dissipates importance and frees intention"@en, "Handeln löst Wichtigkeit auf und befreit die Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "While acting, the importance potential is said to dissipate, intention energy to be released and things to turn out well."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingShiftingFromWorryIntoActionCh12 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingReliefAndReleasedIntentionEnergyCh12 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Pardon'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. XII Frailing, section 'Job Hunting'
#

pmc:TranserfingStagesOfTheJobSearchCh12 a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "Stages of the job search"@en, "Stufen der Stellensuche"@de ;
    skos:definition "The job search is laid out in order: settle on the job, write the CV as the first link of the transfer chain, send it out and let offers come, then prepare for and hold the interview."@en ;
    skos:note "Only the step from choice to CV carries a stated order (pmc:TranserfingChoiceOfJobBeforeCVAndInterviewCh12); no consequence of skipping a stage is named, so no further pm:Presupposing pairs are entered. Transfer chain: pmc:TranserfingTransferChainCh8."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the reader of the whole part: missed by both passes."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmp:TranserfingChoosingTheRightJobCh12 ;
    rdf:_2 pmp:TranserfingWritingTheCVFromTheEmployersSideCh12 ;
    rdf:_3 pmp:TranserfingLettingTheWorkFindYouCh12 ;
    rdf:_4 pmp:TranserfingPreparingTheInterviewAroundTheEmployerCh12 ;
    pm:seriesStatement "First the job is chosen, then the CV is written as the opening link, then it is sent out with no pressure, and only then is the interview prepared and held." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Job Hunting'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingChoosingTheRightJobCh12 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Choosing the right job"@en, "Die richtige Stelle wählen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Decide which job is yours using the earlier goals-and-doors method; keep in mind the genuine right to choose and that potential is limited only by intention and the importance attached; ignore prestige, means and shortcomings and ask only whether the job is truly for you."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingChoosingDoorX10: the method of goals (pmc:TranserfingTsel) and doors (pmc:TranserfingDver) is applied to choosing a job, with prestige, means and shortcomings set aside."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Job Hunting'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPendulumsBreedAnxietyAboutVacanciesCh12 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Pendulums breed anxiety about vacancies"@en, "Pendel erzeugen Angst um freie Stellen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Doubts about a vacancy are exploited by pendulums, which arrange anxiety, disappointment, even despair; stay aware and keep affirming one's right of choice and that an order once placed will be delivered sooner or later; intention acts instantly in dreams, but material realization is inert like tar and needs time, patience and unshakeable conviction."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingChoosingTheRightJobCh12 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Job Hunting'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingSlideOfChoosingWithoutCaringHowCh12 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Slide of choosing without caring how"@en, "Dia der Wahl ohne Sorge um das Wie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Recommended slide: you choose the kind of job; how it will be found is none of your business; in the alternatives space anything is possible whatever pendulums say; just choose and hold firm intention to receive the order. If finances do not permit waiting, take what is available, then with at least minimum income place the order for the best and await it calmly."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingNoWayMakeOneselfBelieveImpossibleX10: the picture of ordering and waiting is given as a slide (pmc:TranserfingSlayd) for job hunting."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Job Hunting'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingSlideForTensionAtALikedJobCh12 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Slide for tension at a liked job"@en, "Dia bei Anspannung in einer geschätzten Arbeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "If you like your work but feel tense or inhibited, carry a mental slide of yourself doing it well with pleasure and fulfilment."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Job Hunting'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPersistingTensionMeansInnerDiscomfortCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Persisting tension means inner discomfort"@en, "Anhaltende Anspannung bedeutet inneres Unbehagen"@de ;
    skos:definition "If the tension does not fade with time, it signals inner discomfort, and looking for another job is advised."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: If the tension does not fade with time, it signals inner discomfort, and looking for another job is advised; it bears on pmp:TranserfingSlideForTensionAtALikedJobCh12."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Job Hunting'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingChoiceOfJobBeforeCVAndInterviewCh12 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Choice of job before CV and interview"@en, "Stellenwahl vor Lebenslauf und Gespräch"@de ;
    skos:definition "The job must first be decided, then intention directed, before writing the CV and preparing interviews; the CV is the first link of the transfer chain."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:TranserfingWritingTheCVFromTheEmployersSideCh12 ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingChoosingTheRightJobCh12 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Job Hunting'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTheJobOfferIsNotTheGoalCh12 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "The job offer is not the goal"@en, "Nicht das Angebot der Stelle zum Ziel machen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Focusing on being offered the job is a mistake; wondering whether one will be picked inevitably builds scenarios of defeat."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingTargetSlideOfTheJobAlreadyWonCh12 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Job Hunting'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingTargetSlideOfTheJobAlreadyWonCh12 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Target slide of the job already won"@en, "Zieldia der bereits gewonnenen Stelle"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once the job is chosen, run a slide of the goal already achieved: you, already hired, with the application behind you, not the act of being offered it; meanwhile do your part rather than sitting idle. Respect the transfer chains, whose opening link is the CV, where inner intention is to be focused."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingSystematicallyRunningTargetSlideX10: the target slide shows the job already held, not the moment of being chosen."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Job Hunting'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingWritingTheCVFromTheEmployersSideCh12 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Writing the CV from the employer’s side"@en, "Den Lebenslauf aus Sicht des Arbeitgebers schreiben"@de ;
    skos:definition "List all skills but name only the one position applied for, chosen boldly; present yourself well without exaggeration but keep every thought on the employer's problems and needs, putting yourself in their place: read many vacancies in your field, note the repeated duties and qualities, take those that fit you and adapt, in effect writing in what the employer expects; use the employer's wording rather than your own fine phrases; imagine drafting the ideal employee's template; list extra skills but stress the required ones. Before publishing online, search the CVs of competitors as if you were the recruiter, to see their strengths and weaknesses and what to change in yours."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Job Hunting'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingApplyingForSeveralPositionsAtOnceCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Applying for several positions at once"@en, "Bewerbung auf mehrere Stellen zugleich"@de ;
    skos:definition "Offering oneself for many roles signals desperation to the employer; several simultaneous goals thin intention from a firm core to a shapeless amoeba; taking on too much concentrates excess potentials and one ends with nothing."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Offering oneself for many roles signals desperation to the employer; several simultaneous goals thin intention from a firm core to a shapeless amoeba; taking on too much concentrates excess potentials and one ends with nothing; it bears on pmp:TranserfingWritingTheCVFromTheEmployersSideCh12."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Job Hunting'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingObtainingTheJobMeantForOneCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Obtaining the job meant for one"@en, "Die für einen bestimmte Stelle erhalten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Getting precisely the chosen position, however scarce such jobs are, as long as one allows oneself to have it and leaves the 'how' to outer intention; going to work as to a celebration."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Job Hunting'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingThePerfectCandidateLosesToTheFittingOneCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The perfect candidate loses to the fitting one"@en, "Der perfekte Bewerber verliert gegen den passenden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Inner intention displays a brilliant specialist, yet a more modest one wins because they fit the employer's picture better; 'perfect' becomes the enemy of good; the mind cannot predict demand and sells itself as a masterpiece while the market sets other criteria."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Inner intention displays a brilliant specialist, yet a more modest one wins because they fit the employer's picture better; 'perfect' becomes the enemy of good; the mind cannot predict demand and sells itself as a masterpiece while the market sets other criteria; it bears on pmp:TranserfingWritingTheCVFromTheEmployersSideCh12."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Job Hunting'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingEmployerFocusedCVYieldsTheJobCh12 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Employer-focused CV yields the job"@en, "Arbeitgeberorientierter Lebenslauf bewirkt die Stelle"@de ;
    skos:definition "A CV tuned to the employer's criteria is said to give a large advantage toward the chosen job."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingWritingTheCVFromTheEmployersSideCh12 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingObtainingTheJobMeantForOneCh12 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Job Hunting'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingLettingTheWorkFindYouCh12 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Letting the work find you"@en, "Die Arbeit einen finden lassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Send the CV to various companies without hammering on doors: recommend yourself without pressure and let them choose; publish it in several media; shift weight from hunting for work to making your presence known on the market; never send to the same address twice; as an exclusive specialist use recruiting agencies and wait calmly for results; no quick answer should be expected."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Job Hunting'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingBurningDesireDelaysTheOrderCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Burning desire delays the order"@en, "Brennender Wunsch verzögert die Bestellung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Delivery time depends on how purified the intention is; flaming desire makes balanced forces interfere in many ways; orders are often filled just when hope is lost; the more indifferent one is, the sooner it is fulfilled, since lack of desire frees one to act instead of fearing failure."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Delivery time depends on how purified the intention is; flaming desire makes balanced forces interfere in many ways; orders are often filled just when hope is lost; the more indifferent one is, the sooner it is fulfilled, since lack of desire frees one to act instead of fearing failure; it bears on pmp:TranserfingLettingTheWorkFindYouCh12."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Job Hunting'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingPreparingTheInterviewAroundTheEmployerCh12 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Preparing the interview around the employer"@en, "Vorbereitung des Gesprächs um den Arbeitgeber herum"@de ;
    skos:definition "At invitation, watch your intention: clear the target slide, forget yourself and attend wholly to the employer's inner intention. Study the company's promotional material: what it is proud of, how it sets itself apart; bring these up in the interview. Sense its resonant frequency or spirit: regulated or loose ethics, formal or informal communication, enthusiasm and initiative versus discipline, team versus individual creativity."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Job Hunting'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSeenAsTheirKindOfPersonCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Seen as “their kind of person”"@en, "Als „einer von ihnen“ gesehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: grasping the company's spirit even at interview means being regarded as their type of person."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingPreparingTheInterviewAroundTheEmployerCh12."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Job Hunting'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingSelfPardonBeforeTheInterviewCh12 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Self-pardon before the interview"@en, "Selbstvergebung vor dem Vorstellungsgespräch"@de ;
    skos:definition "Before the interview accept your weaknesses and missing skills and walk in calmly; there is no ideal candidate or employer, so drop inner and outer importance; no self-justification is needed; working on flaws stays valid, but in the interview permit yourself imperfection."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Job Hunting'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingControllingNervesByInnerIntentionFailsCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Controlling nerves by inner intention fails"@en, "Nerven mit innerer Absicht zu bändigen scheitert"@de ;
    skos:definition "Insisting to oneself that one is calm does not work; nerves cannot be handled without removing their cause; fighting inner panic can make one freeze stiff like a mummy."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Insisting to oneself that one is calm does not work; nerves cannot be handled without removing their cause; fighting inner panic can make one freeze stiff like a mummy; it bears on pmp:TranserfingGoingToTheInterviewJustToGoThroughCh12."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Job Hunting'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingGoingToTheInterviewJustToGoThroughCh12 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Going to the interview just to go through it"@en, "Zum Gespräch gehen, nur um es zu durchlaufen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Accept beforehand that you may fail, the only effective stress reducer in the hot seat; purify intention of desire; go not to get the job nor even to pass but merely to go through the interview; concentrate on the process, enjoy it as a chance to show yourself well, drop thoughts of failing."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingPurifyingIntentionCh7: accepting defeat in advance is applied to the interview, whose aim shrinks to getting through it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Job Hunting'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingIntentionPurifiedOfDesireBeforeTheInterviewCh12 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Intention purified of desire before the interview"@en, "Vom Wunsch gereinigte Absicht vor dem Gespräch"@de ;
    skos:definition "Purifying intention of desire is called essential, since wanting to be chosen builds excess potential and the more meaning and importance the job has, the lower one's chances."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:TranserfingGoingToTheInterviewJustToGoThroughCh12 ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingPurifyingIntentionCh7 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Chances fall as the importance attached to success rises." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Job Hunting'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingAnsweringWithinTheEmployersConcernsCh12 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Answering within the employer’s concerns"@en, "Im Rahmen der Anliegen des Arbeitgebers antworten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Instead of displaying yourself, show real interest in the employer's issues: answer precisely and briefly without rambling, bring each answer back to their concerns, raise what the company does, is proud of and struggles with, and present your strengths as relevant to solving its problems."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Job Hunting'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingInterviewTechniquesYieldTheJobCh12 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Interview techniques yield the job"@en, "Gesprächstechniken bewirken die Stelle"@de ;
    skos:definition "Interview conducted in the employer's context, with desire purified, is said to put the outcome under one's script."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingAnsweringWithinTheEmployersConcernsCh12, pmp:TranserfingGoingToTheInterviewJustToGoThroughCh12 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingObtainingTheJobMeantForOneCh12 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Job Hunting'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGameRunsToOnesOwnScriptCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Game runs to one’s own script"@en, "Das Spiel läuft nach eigenem Drehbuch"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: if the talk was steered toward the employer's concerns, one can be sure the game follows one's script."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingAnsweringWithinTheEmployersConcernsCh12."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Job Hunting'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRejectionMeansTheJobWasNotMeantCh12 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Rejection means the job was not meant for one"@en, "Ablehnung heißt, die Stelle war nicht vorgesehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "If not selected, the job was clearly not one's own and unknown problems may have been escaped; a post meant for someone else brings trouble; keep searching calmly for one's own job, which work should never cause inner discomfort."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XII Frailing, section 'Job Hunting'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# prima-materia — Transerfing: Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III:
# Vpered v proshloe! (2004), part 2: chapter XIII Coordination, from 'The
# Insecurity Labyrinth' to the SUMMARY.
#
# Two independent extraction passes ran over the text (A 193 records, B 207;
# 7 records of B without counterpart in A: 1 added, 6 covered, 0 not owed);
# a reader of the whole part added 5 records both passes missed (the three
# stages of the will to have as members of its series, knowing free of doubt,
# hope as a kind of knowing). Stupen' I and II (traditions/transerfing-stupen-1.ttl,
# traditions/transerfing-stupen-2.ttl) are not restated: 15 records whose claim
# a node there already carries are left out and linked; 44 nodes that restate
# an earlier node with a difference say so in a note.
#
# Shared system terms typed here: pmc:TranserfingKoordinatsiyaVazhnosti
# (coordination of importance, Transurfing's replacement for confidence) and
# pmc:TranserfingKoordinatsiyaNamereniya (coordination of intention, its main
# principle); the practices are pmp:TranserfingCoordinatingImportanceCh13 and
# pmp:TranserfingCoordinatingIntentionCh13. Linked from part 1:
# pmc:TranserfingEnergiyaNamereniya. The Commandments, Jesus' summary of the law
# and "According to your faith" are quotations the author interprets, so
# textual; nothing in the chapter is claimed as received. His polemics are
# concepts, since only his side is read.
#

#
# ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Insecurity Labyrinth'
#

pmc:TranserfingInsecurityConsumesIntentionCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Insecurity consumes the energy of intention"@en, "Unsicherheit verzehrt die Absichtsenergie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Doubting oneself and lacking confidence are treated as one thing; both weaken inner intention and all but rule out outer intention. Importance (inner and outer), frustration and self-restraint each form an excess potential, and keeping several up at once uses up personal energy, so that in the overwhelmed state intention is said to be missing altogether."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Insecurity Labyrinth'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingStrainSpoilsResultCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Strain to do well spoils the result"@en, "Leistungsdruck verdirbt das Ergebnis"@de ;
    skos:definition "Whatever is done while lacking confidence is said to come out poorly, and the harder one strains to perform well the worse the outcome."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Whatever is done while lacking confidence is said to come out poorly, and the harder one strains to perform well the worse the outcome; it bears on pmc:TranserfingInsecurityConsumesIntentionCh13."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Insecurity Labyrinth'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingOverwhelmIntentionGoneCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Overwhelm: intention gone"@en, "Überwältigung: Absicht erloschen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sign of failure: feeling crushed, unable to move or speak sensibly. Although it looks like intention clamped tight, the text holds that at this point no intention remains, its energy having gone into excess potentials."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: feeling crushed, unable to move or speak sensibly. Although it looks like intention clamped tight, the text holds that at this point no intention remains, its energy having gone into excess potentials; it bears on pmc:TranserfingInsecurityConsumesIntentionCh13."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Insecurity Labyrinth'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPanicForecastsCh13 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Panic forecasts realise the worst"@en, "Panische Prognosen verwirklichen das Schlimmste"@de ;
    skos:definition "Anxious \"what if\" forecasts, mostly gloomy, drain intention and, worse, stress, panic and fear are said to generate the worst expectations, which come true. Anxious insecurity is called pure food for pendulums."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingInsecurityConsumesIntentionCh13 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Insecurity Labyrinth'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGuiltNarrowsMeridiansCh13 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Guilt narrows the meridians and draws manipulators"@en, "Schuldgefühl verengt die Meridiane und zieht Manipulatoren an"@de ;
    skos:definition "Guilt is said to narrow the meridians and to leave enough energy only for weak, hesitant action; a habit of guilt attracts manipulators who feed on the unprotected energy while one keeps explaining oneself."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingManipulators: adds that guilt narrows the meridians and leaves energy only for feeble action, and that endless self-explanation deepens the insecurity."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingManipulators ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Insecurity Labyrinth'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingViciousCircleOfInsecurityCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Vicious circle of insecurity"@en, "Teufelskreis der Unsicherheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Model: more importance and desire deepen insecurity, tighter self-control raises tension, panic tends to justify itself, and guilt ends in the life of a loser."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Insecurity Labyrinth'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWallOfConfidenceCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Head-on attack to build a wall of confidence"@en, "Frontalangriff zum Aufbau einer Selbstsicherheitsmauer"@de ;
    skos:definition "Trying to display strength by forceful decisive impact on the world costs much energy, which goes into excess potentials and resisting the flow; the wall keeps falling and the approach is said to end in failure every time."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Trying to display strength by forceful decisive impact on the world costs much energy, which goes into excess potentials and resisting the flow; the wall keeps falling and the approach is said to end in failure every time; it bears on pmc:TranserfingConfidenceAsTemporaryPotentialCh13."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Insecurity Labyrinth'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingUnfoundedConfidenceCh13 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Unfounded, all-or-nothing confidence"@en, "Grundlose Alles-oder-nichts-Sicherheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Staking everything without a basis is shyness turned inside out; it creates excess potential and usually harms others, and once it measures itself against others it forms dependent relationships. Confidence resting on comparison or contempt is pure excess potential and will be punished by balanced forces sooner or later."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingConfidenceAsTemporaryPotentialCh13 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Insecurity Labyrinth'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingEcstaticConfidenceCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Ecstatic confidence fades"@en, "Euphorische Sicherheit verfliegt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The sudden rush of self-assurance a shy person may feel is called false, since it rests on a brief emotional high that soon passes."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: The sudden rush of self-assurance a shy person may feel is called false, since it rests on a brief emotional high that soon passes; it bears on pmc:TranserfingConfidenceAsTemporaryPotentialCh13."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Insecurity Labyrinth'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDoNotFightInsecurityCh13 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not fight, hide or force insecurity"@en, "Unsicherheit weder bekämpfen noch verbergen noch erzwingen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Fighting insecurity is futile, false courage cannot hide it and the energy spent on the attempt turns against one; artificially summoned courage is wasted, and holding oneself together while falling apart is impossible. Any attempt to develop confidence is called ridiculous."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingFightingOwnWeaknesses: there the target is a shortcoming; here it is insecurity itself, which can be neither fought, hidden nor forced into courage."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingInsecurityConsumesIntentionCh13 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Insecurity Labyrinth'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingConfidenceAsReleasedIntentionCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Confidence as released intention"@en, "Zuversicht als freigesetzte Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Confidence does not grow through decisive deeds; once someone quits fighting and acts, the energy of intention lets go and shifts from excess potentials into carrying out the action. Confidence, like energy, is either there or not and cannot be developed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Insecurity Labyrinth'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAffirmingConfidenceCh13 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Against affirmation and autosuggestion for confidence"@en, "Gegen Affirmation und Autosuggestion zur Selbstsicherheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Repeating affirmations of self-confidence is called naive and fruitless, like treating symptoms rather than the cause; the thought transmission needed to stay on a wave of confidence cannot be sustained."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingAffirmationsFail: applied to self-confidence and set beside treating symptoms instead of the cause."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingConfidenceAsTemporaryPotentialCh13 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Insecurity Labyrinth'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMorningSelfAssuranceCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Morning self-assurance crashes on provocation"@en, "Morgendliche Selbstbeschwörung bricht bei Provokation ein"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced course: a morning declaration of unshakeable confidence gives a brief lift, then a pendulum arranges a provocation and one falls from the wave unnoticed, back into irritation, gloom and fear of the world."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: a morning declaration of unshakeable confidence gives a brief lift, then a pendulum arranges a provocation and one falls from the wave unnoticed, back into irritation, gloom and fear of the world; it bears on pmc:TranserfingAffirmingConfidenceCh13."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Insecurity Labyrinth'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingInsecurityLabyrinthCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The labyrinth without exit"@en, "Das Labyrinth ohne Ausgang"@de ;
    skos:definition "The insecurity labyrinth has no exit; its walls are made of importance and fall once one stops seeking a way out and drops importance. Paradox: to gain self-confidence one must give up wanting it. Confidence is called a pendulum invention, a mirage and a trap for importance, a game the pendulums always win."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Insecurity Labyrinth'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCausesOfInsecurityCh13 a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Two groups of causes of insecurity"@en, "Zwei Gruppen von Ursachen der Unsicherheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Internal causes: fixation on one's own qualities, yielding discontent over shortcomings, inferiority against others, shyness, fear of failing or looking foolish. External causes: overrating outside factors, yielding fears about the gap between modest inner means and the world's demands, feeling tiny in a big city, fear of reality."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Insecurity Labyrinth'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingConfidenceAsTemporaryPotentialCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Confidence is a temporary excess potential"@en, "Selbstsicherheit ist ein vorübergehendes Überschusspotenzial"@de ;
    skos:definition "Confidence is a belief in success, so room for doubt always remains and one negative adjustment of the scenario topples it. It is built on excess potentials and dependency; even self-control is a passing concentration of tension. Confidence is the opposite pole of insecurity, both cost energy and the first is destroyed by balanced forces; both are rooted in dependence on outside factors and spring only from importance."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Insecurity Labyrinth'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Importance'
#

pmc:TranserfingStrugglePostulateCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The pendulum postulate of struggle"@en, "Das Pendelpostulat des Kampfes"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pendulums are said to have imposed the belief that nothing comes free and that one must fight, push and outdo rivals, which requires confidence. Rejecting this scenario, one can take what is one's own calmly, by discovering the will to have it. Freedom of choice threatens pendulums, which would starve if people claimed without struggle. Without struggle, confidence becomes unnecessary."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingAgainstFightingForLuck: the belief in struggle is here a pendulum postulate that also makes confidence seem needed, and freedom of choice is said to threaten pendulums."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Importance'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingStringsOfImportanceCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Puppet strings of importance"@en, "Marionettenfäden der Bedeutsamkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Metaphor: the pendulum leads a person like a puppet; while the strings are taut the person walks confidently like a child at its mother's hand, and when they slacken or jerk the person feels unsure and pulls them tight. It is the person who will not release the strings of importance, held by a dependency that fakes support. Released, the person would walk freely and need only coordination, keeping balance by not creating importance."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingPuppetStrings: not a list of channels but one image: the person, not the pendulum, keeps hold of the strings, like a child at its mother's hand, and once free needs only coordination to keep balance."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Importance'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingInnerEmptinessCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Inner emptiness"@en, "Innere Leere"@de ;
    skos:definition "A state with no excessive meaning attributed to anything, so nothing can hook in and the layer of one's world is not distorted; not a vacuum. Said to be more effective against pendulums than toughness, and to need no energy for a protective field."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en, "Differs from pmp:TranserfingEmptiness: held as a lasting state of attaching excess meaning to nothing, set against toughness and needing no protective field."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Importance'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingInnerCalmCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Inner calm"@en, "Innere Ruhe"@de ;
    skos:definition "A feeling of inner peace said to come from not producing inner importance, leaving nothing that needs proving."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Importance'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingDroppingTheFightForWorthCh13 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Dropping the fight for self-worth"@en, "Den Kampf um Selbstwert aufgeben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: drop any need to demonstrate something to oneself or others; accept what one wanted to prove as a basic truth; do not try to believe in or argue oneself into one's value; simply quit the battle and watch how others respond; once one registers their changed attitude, belief is no longer needed."@en ;
    skos:note "Said to work every time despite being a paradox."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Importance'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSelfWorthCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Self-worth and raised self-esteem"@en, "Selbstwert und gehobenes Selbstwertgefühl"@de ;
    skos:definition "A sense of one's own worth and higher self-esteem, said to be gained the moment the battle for it is dropped, confirmed by the respect of others."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Importance'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAgainstInflatingSelfEsteemCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against psychologists who inflate self-esteem"@en, "Gegen Psychologen, die das Selbstwertgefühl aufblähen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author rejects the common practice of many psychologists of persuading clients that they are better than they think: someone with low self-esteem cannot convince himself of the opposite, doubts about the special qualities creep in, and the result is smugness or deeper despair."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Importance'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRespectFromOthersCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Others begin to show respect"@en, "Andere zeigen mehr Achtung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced sign: after quitting the battle, people around treat one with more respect as if valuing one higher; then one simply knows one's worth, and self-esteem visibly rises while others confirm it."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingDroppingTheFightForWorthCh13."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Importance'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingBattleForWorthDrainsCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The battle for worth drains energy"@en, "Der Kampf um Wert zehrt Energie aus"@de ;
    skos:definition "Struggling for self-worth is said to channel free energy into fighting the flow and into excess potentials that stir balanced forces, producing a knot of problems that cannot be unpicked."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Struggling for self-worth is said to channel free energy into fighting the flow and into excess potentials that stir balanced forces, producing a knot of problems that cannot be unpicked; it bears on pmp:TranserfingDroppingTheFightForWorthCh13."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Importance'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDroppingTheFightYieldsSelfWorthCh13 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Dropping the fight yields self-worth"@en, "Kampfverzicht ergibt Selbstwert"@de ;
    skos:definition "Giving up the struggle for worth is said to produce a growing sense of worth and esteem."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingDroppingTheFightForWorthCh13 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingSelfWorthCh13 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Importance'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGuiltCannotBeSuppressedCh13 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Guilt cannot be suppressed"@en, "Schuld lässt sich nicht unterdrücken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Denying or stamping out guilt is as pointless as artificially lifting self-esteem; with a disposition to guilt the feeling cannot be stifled by inner battle."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingGuilt ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Importance'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingStopJustifyingCh13 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Stop justifying yourself"@en, "Sich nicht mehr rechtfertigen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: do not justify yourself to others except where an explanation of your actions is truly needed; recall that nobody may judge you as long as you harmed no one; do not accept blame publicly; let manipulators fall through emptiness and give them nothing, leaving the \"court\" quietly without slamming the door; with a deep guilt complex it is fine at first to silence conscience temporarily; never ask others to assess your worth."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingRefusingGuilt: adds leaving the court quietly, putting a lid on conscience for a while if the complex runs deep, and never inviting others to rate one's worth."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Importance'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNotJustifyingYieldsFreedomFromGuiltCh13 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Not justifying yields freedom from guilt"@en, "Nicht-Rechtfertigen ergibt Schuldfreiheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "The practice of not justifying oneself is said to clear conscience of guilt."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingStopJustifyingCh13 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingReleaseOfGuilt ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Importance'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGuiltVanishesCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Guilt vanishes"@en, "Schuld verschwindet"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced sign: guilt is said simply to dissolve; one no longer feels a need for protection or to strike first."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingStopJustifyingCh13."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Importance'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGuiltAndLowWorthAsRootsCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Guilt and low worth as roots of inner importance"@en, "Schuld und Minderwert als Wurzeln innerer Bedeutsamkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Guilt together with low self-worth is held to be the main forms of inner importance, all other excess potentials deriving from them; settling these two removes a large share of inner importance."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Importance'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTwoOppressiveOuterImportancesCh13 a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Two most oppressive forms of outer importance"@en, "Zwei drückendste Formen äußerer Bedeutsamkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Dread of the unknown, and being crushed by tasks, both producing panic and stress. Contrasted reactions: the insecure drag their burden, strong personalities storm the fortress with overt confidence; both cost energy (panic versus overcoming obstacles)."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Importance'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingLoweringOuterImportanceByActionCh13 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Lowering outer importance and acting"@en, "Äußere Bedeutsamkeit senken und handeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: deliberately lower outer importance and stop fighting the alternatives flow; do not battle to wipe out importance, since meaning can never be fully removed; loosen the grip and convert anxious energy into energy for doing; start doing in whatever way possible, without insisting or pressing."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingReducingImportance: aimed at outer importance and carried out by turning anxious energy into doing, without trying to wipe importance out."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Importance'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingObstaclesClearCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Obstacles clear, problems shrink"@en, "Hindernisse weichen, Probleme schrumpfen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: perceived obstacles leave the path; excess potential disperses through action, intention is freed and complex problems turn into minor ones."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingLoweringOuterImportanceByActionCh13."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Importance'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingBlindFaithAndTheUnknownCh13 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Blind faith does not cure fear of the unknown"@en, "Blinder Glaube heilt die Angst vor dem Unbekannten nicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Neither blind faith, autosuggestion nor false confidence help with fear of the unknown; one cannot make oneself believe in a distant goal or certain success, so such attempts should be dropped. Faith, especially blind faith, always leaves room for doubt; forced importance is what blinds."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingBlindBeliefOfTheMindCh13 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Importance'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingCoordinatingImportanceCh13 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Coordination"@en, "Koordination"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: enjoy thinking of the goal as though it were already reached; release control over the script; move along the alternatives flow, assisting it by pure intention. Also: lower importance, remember that you set how complex a task is, and let adjustments to the script work for you. Leave the means aside."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Importance'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCoordinatingImportanceYieldsCoordinationCh13 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Coordination practice yields coordination"@en, "Koordinationspraxis ergibt Koordination"@de ;
    skos:definition "Living by the coordination steps is said to bring the state of coordination."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingCoordinatingImportanceCh13 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingKoordinatsiyaVazhnosti ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Importance'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFaithTurnsToKnowledgeCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Faith turns to knowledge"@en, "Glaube wird zu Wissen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: acting in coordination, what one wanted but feared to believe soon shows up around a bend of the current; facts dispel doubt, faith becomes knowledge, and dread of the unknown turns into satisfaction in one's own strength. Things fall into place without excess effort."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingCoordinatingImportanceCh13."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Importance'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHeartMindHarmonyForCoordinationCh13 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Absolute coordination needs harmony of heart and mind"@en, "Absolute Koordination setzt Einklang von Herz und Verstand voraus"@de ;
    skos:definition "Full coordination results from heart-mind harmony; if consciously sure but doubt or gloom sits in the subconscious, coordination stays out of reach."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingKoordinatsiyaVazhnosti ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingEdinstvoDushiIRazuma ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Coordination stays out of reach while doubt or gloom remains in the subconscious." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Importance'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCredoYieldsHeartMindUnityCh13 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Heeding the heart and credo yields heart-mind harmony"@en, "Herz und Credo folgen ergibt Einklang"@de ;
    skos:definition "Listening to the heart and living by one's credo is said to produce harmony of heart and mind."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingLivingByOwnCredoCh13 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingEdinstvoDushiIRazuma ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Importance'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingLivingByOwnCredoCh13 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Living by one's own credo"@en, "Nach dem eigenen Credo leben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: heed the whispers of the heart; love and accept yourself as you are; do not suffer from conscience or guilt; act firmly as heart and mind dictate. Do not shape, change or fight the credo, it already exists; drop inner and outer importance to free it."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingLivingByOwnCredo: the credo is not picked but already there, sealed in importance; it is freed by dropping importance and must not be reworked."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Importance'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCredoCollapsesCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Credo collapses under low self-esteem"@en, "Das Credo zerfällt bei geringem Selbstwert"@de ;
    skos:definition "Attempts to live by one's credo break down when self-esteem is hurt and heart and mind come into conflict."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Attempts to live by one's credo break down when self-esteem is hurt and heart and mind come into conflict; it bears on pmp:TranserfingLivingByOwnCredoCh13."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Importance'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDoNotPolishCredoCh13 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not polish your credo"@en, "Das Credo nicht zurechtfeilen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reworking one's credo like a sculptor chiselling marble is said to yield only fruitless soul-searching, torment and self-doubt; a credo cannot be produced by struggle or effort of will."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingLivingByOwnCredoCh13 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Importance'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCredoFreedCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sensing the credo freed"@en, "Spüren, dass das Credo frei ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: once inner and outer importance are released one immediately feels the credo released and lives by it calmly."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingLivingByOwnCredoCh13."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Importance'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingEndingWorthBattleYieldsCoordinationCh13 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Dropping worth-battle and judgement yields coordination"@en, "Verzicht auf Wertkampf und Fremdurteil ergibt Koordination"@de ;
    skos:definition "Quitting the battle for worth, not letting others judge one, and lowering outer importance are said to give what people usually call true confidence, that is, coordination."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingDroppingTheFightForWorthCh13, pmp:TranserfingStopJustifyingCh13, pmp:TranserfingLoweringOuterImportanceByActionCh13 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingKoordinatsiyaVazhnosti ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Importance'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingKoordinatsiyaVazhnosti a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Coordination (true calm confidence)"@en, "Koordination (wahre, ruhige Zuversicht)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Transurfing's replacement for confidence: a calm inner strength not tied to anything external, needing no confirmation; arising from self-sufficiency and wholeness, a state of total balance with heart and mind united and free of fear, stress, guilt, obligation, dependency and superiority. Held up as the ideal to strive for."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en, "Shared system term of Stupen' III (coordination of importance), typed by this part; Transurfing's replacement for confidence."@en, "Introduced at \"Transurfing offers an alternative\"; defined further in this section."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Importance'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCoordinationBeforeFreedomFromPendulumsCh13 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Coordination before freedom from pendulums"@en, "Koordination vor Freiheit von Pendeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Coordination is said to grant freedom from pendulums."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingFreeOfThePendulumsPower ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingKoordinatsiyaVazhnosti ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:presentationOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Importance'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingPlayingARoleAsIfFilmedCh13 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Playing a role as if filmed"@en, "Eine Rolle spielen, als würde man gefilmt"@de ;
    skos:definition "For burdensome present duties: detach and picture yourself being filmed in a movie; play the part through to the end, at least to the close of the current episode, until passing through the right door."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Importance'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Battle with the Clay Golem'
#

pmc:TranserfingThreeLevelsOfPendulumInfluenceCh13 a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Three levels of pendulum influence"@en, "Drei Ebenen des Pendeleinflusses"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pendulum influence acts on a mental, an emotional and an energetic level."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Battle with the Clay Golem'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingInformationMatrixCh13 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Information networks and the matrix"@en, "Informationsnetze und die Matrix"@de ;
    skos:definition "The rapidly expanding telecommunication web, under the anaesthesia of entertainment and handy gadgets, is said to let a pendulum gather huge numbers of adherents at once; the trend points toward people becoming parts of an informational energy matrix with no notion of their freedom, which shapes worldview rather than using force. Hence pendulum protection is needed."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingMayatnik ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Battle with the Clay Golem'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingImportanceOfZeroImportanceCh13 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Pendulums hook into the importance of zero importance"@en, "Pendel haken sich in die Wichtigkeit der Nullbedeutsamkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Even the great importance one gives to keeping importance at zero can serve a pendulum as a hook."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingVazhnost ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Battle with the Clay Golem'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWarOnPendulumsCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Declaring war on pendulums"@en, "Pendeln den Krieg erklären"@de ;
    skos:definition "Failure condition: whoever earnestly wages war on pendulums, perceives the process as a fight, or challenges the golem even knowingly, is said to be beaten in advance, since a pendulum cannot be defeated in battle."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: whoever earnestly wages war on pendulums, perceives the process as a fight, or challenges the golem even knowingly, is said to be beaten in advance, since a pendulum cannot be defeated in battle; it bears on pmc:TranserfingClayGolemCh13."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Battle with the Clay Golem'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingClayGolemCh13 a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Clay golem"@en, "Lehmgolem"@de ;
    skos:definition "The pendulum as opponent once the encounter is seen as a game: a mere clay golem, harmless as long as one stays aware of the game and refuses its rules; fought with sugar sabres, it shatters or crumbles into emptiness."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "clay golem" ;
    pm:nameRole "the pendulum seen as an opponent in a game, harmless while one keeps to awareness" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Battle with the Clay Golem'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPendulumsStrikeWhenSureCh13 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Pendulums strike when you feel sure"@en, "Pendel lauern, wenn man sich sicher fühlt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pendulums are said to wait for their victim whenever it feels confident and to try every means to unbalance it; one should expect this. They may also provoke gently and softly."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingPendulumsStrikeWhenWillHaveAppearsCh9: the trigger is feeling sure of oneself, and the provocation may come gently."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingMayatnik ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Battle with the Clay Golem'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingBreakingTheGameRulesCh13 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Breaking the rules of the pendulum game"@en, "Die Spielregeln des Pendels brechen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: when provoked (trouble, bad news), wake up, recall what the game is and at once lower importance; deliberately respond in an unexpected, inadequate way rather than per the script; do not take the bait; do not get angry with the game itself; consciously change your attitude to the negative factor instead of fighting your reaction; keep reminding yourself of the rules and keep importance at zero; relax, let yourself lose at times, and if it stops being fun show maximal indifference by losing without caring."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingInappropriateReaction: framed as a game with a clay golem in which a lost round is accepted and one never grows angry with the game itself."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Battle with the Clay Golem'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWakefulnessBeforeBreakingRulesCh13 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Wakefulness before breaking the rules"@en, "Wachheit vor dem Regelbruch"@de ;
    skos:definition "The rules can be broken only while not daydreaming; in non-lucid dreaming the dreamer is a victim of circumstance, and waking people react as automatically. One must come to one's senses in time."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:TranserfingBreakingTheGameRulesCh13 ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingConstantAwareness ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "One reacts by habit and remains at the mercy of circumstance." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Battle with the Clay Golem'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPleasureOfNotTakingTheBaitCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Pleasure of not taking the bait"@en, "Freude, den Köder nicht zu schlucken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced sign: a pleasant feeling on noticing the pendulum straining to provoke while one stays unmoved, from pride and from the energy gained."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingBreakingTheGameRulesCh13."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Battle with the Clay Golem'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingProvocationEnergyCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Taking in the energy of a failed provocation"@en, "Die Energie einer gescheiterten Provokation aufnehmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "When one does not yield to a provocation, one is said to receive the energy the pendulum put into it and to grow stronger; this extra strength is felt as pleasure."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Battle with the Clay Golem'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRuleBreakingYieldsProvocationEnergyCh13 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Rule-breaking yields the provocation's energy"@en, "Regelbruch ergibt die Provokationsenergie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Not taking the bait is said to transfer the pendulum's spent energy to oneself."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingBreakingTheGameRulesCh13 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingProvocationEnergyCh13 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Battle with the Clay Golem'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGolemShattersCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The golem shatters"@en, "Der Golem zerspringt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: breaking the rules while keeping inner balance makes the golem fall apart; with importance at zero the mirrors of importance splinter and the golem is seen to crumble."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingBreakingTheGameRulesCh13."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Battle with the Clay Golem'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLosingTemperCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Losing one's temper turns the game into battle"@en, "Wutausbruch macht das Spiel zum Kampf"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once one starts to lose one's temper, the sugar sabre becomes a real blade; the game can become a fight and result in an induced transition."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Once one starts to lose one's temper, the sugar sabre becomes a real blade; the game can become a fight and result in an induced transition; it bears on pmp:TranserfingBreakingTheGameRulesCh13."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Battle with the Clay Golem'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRoomOfMirrorsCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Room of mirrors"@en, "Spiegelkabinett"@de ;
    skos:definition "Fighting a pendulum is like fighting an unseen opponent among mirrors: what looms is neither the pendulum nor its reflection but one's own importance; while anything carries exaggerated meaning the opponent remains."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Battle with the Clay Golem'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingToughnessFeedsThePendulumCh13 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Toughness feeds the pendulum"@en, "Härte nährt das Pendel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ideals like iron will, steel nerves, endurance and self-control imply defence and readiness to strike back; keeping such a protective field costs huge energy, all of it food for the pendulum. Emptiness is held to be far more effective."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingBreakingTheGameRulesCh13 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Battle with the Clay Golem'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingZeroImportanceNotDefenceCh13 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Zero importance must not become constant defence"@en, "Nullbedeutsamkeit darf nicht zur Daueralarmbereitschaft werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "The aim of zero importance must not turn into permanent combat readiness; one should not give the game itself excess meaning or strive to win at any cost, since a held grip lets the pendulum shake one about like a dog with a stick."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingBreakingTheGameRulesCh13 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Battle with the Clay Golem'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAcceptALostRoundCh13 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Accept a lost round"@en, "Eine verlorene Runde hinnehmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "When a round goes to the pendulum, admit it without stubbornness; losing balance is not wrong, do not punish yourself, the next game is yours."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingBreakingTheGameRulesCh13 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Battle with the Clay Golem'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNoUltimatumsCh13 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "No ultimatums or last-time vows"@en, "Keine Ultimaten, keine Letztes-Mal-Schwüre"@de ;
    skos:definition "Promising that this time is the last or setting oneself an ultimatum is really an ultimatum to the pendulum, a protective wall that turns the game into a battle one will lose."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingBreakingTheGameRulesCh13 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Battle with the Clay Golem'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPendulumImposesThoughtsCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Pendulums impose thoughts"@en, "Pendel zwingen Gedanken auf"@de ;
    skos:definition "A pendulum is said to be able to seize one's thought wave so fully that it literally imposes thoughts; the vow \"just one more and then never again\" is the pendulum speaking, not oneself."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Battle with the Clay Golem'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingIndifferentPartingFromHabitCh13 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Indifferent parting from a harmful habit"@en, "Gleichgültiger Abschied von einer schädlichen Gewohnheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Whenever you catch yourself vowing one last time (cigarettes, alcohol, drugs), wake up, see it as the pendulum talking and shake off the delusion; then part from the habit indifferently rather than with resolve."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Battle with the Clay Golem'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingReleaseFromHabitCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Release from a bad habit"@en, "Loslösung von einer schlechten Gewohnheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Separating from a harmful habit without struggle, through indifference."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Battle with the Clay Golem'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPendulumVoiceYieldsReleaseFromHabitCh13 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Awareness of the pendulum voice yields release from habit"@en, "Erkennen der Pendelstimme ergibt Loslösung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Awareness that the vow is the pendulum speaking is said to help one split from the habit indifferently."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingIndifferentPartingFromHabitCh13 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingReleaseFromHabitCh13 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Battle with the Clay Golem'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingReligionsAsPendulumsCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Organised religions as pendulums"@en, "Organisierte Religionen als Pendel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Against the religions: once God revealed himself, pendulums seized religion; people broke the First Commandment by founding many religions, which are pendulums hiding behind the Lord's name; ministers, themselves adherents, have little effect; religious wars cannot please God. The Second Commandment is read as a ban on serving pendulums."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Battle with the Clay Golem'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingJesusSummaryOfTheLawCh13 a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Jesus"@en, "Jesus"@de ;
    skos:definition "Cited as the teacher who reduced all the commandments to two: love of God with all one's heart, soul and mind, and love of the neighbour as oneself."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingJesusAsExemplarCh7: here Jesus is named as the teacher who reduced the commandments to two, not as the measure of outer intention."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Jesus" ;
    pm:nameRole "teacher whose summary of the law is endorsed" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Battle with the Clay Golem'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCommandmentsReducedToOneCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The commandments reduced to one task"@en, "Die Gebote auf eine Aufgabe zurückgeführt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Interpretation: all the commandments ask only that one love God within oneself and within others without worshipping pendulums."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingTenCommandments: read not as rules of balance but as a single charge: love God in oneself and others without serving pendulums."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Battle with the Clay Golem'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingInformationAwarenessCh13 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Information hygiene against pendulums"@en, "Informationshygiene gegen Pendel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: stay highly aware under mass media; do not let negative news affect you; since every group has its pendulum and adherents often do not know its aims, always ask who needs this and why, and whether you need it; meanwhile actively seek information relevant to your goal."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingLettingInformationPass: adds asking whom a message serves and to what end, and an active search for information bearing on one's own goal."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Battle with the Clay Golem'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTwoWaysOfBreakingRulesCh13 a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Two ways of breaking the rules"@en, "Zwei Wege, die Regeln zu brechen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Either drop importance so the pendulum sinks into the emptiness of one's indifference, or damp its swing by an inadequate reaction; the second serves when lowering importance is hard. Any inadequate reaction to a provocation counts as a gross breach of the game."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'The Battle with the Clay Golem'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Ending the Battle'
#

pmc:TranserfingNoFightForTheGoalCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Freedom of choice: no fight needed"@en, "Wahlfreiheit: kein Kampf nötig"@de ;
    skos:definition "The goal need not be fought for; only the will to have is required. Once one allows oneself to have, one can calmly step toward the goal. The right to choose need not be won, it is already possessed."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingFreedomOfChoice: the freedom is said to consist in needing no fight at all, only the will to have, the right to choose being held already."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Ending the Battle'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSelfImprovementScriptCh13 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "The pendulum script of self-improvement and battle"@en, "Das Pendelskript von Selbstverbesserung und Kampf"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pendulums suggest one is imperfect and must first change oneself, then fight for one's place under the sun; the sole purpose is to drain the victim, since battling oneself and battling the world both hand energy to the pendulum."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingAgainstSelfImprovement: the demand to change oneself first and then fight the world is a pendulum scenario for draining the victim."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingStrugglePostulateCh13 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Ending the Battle'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWarriorAndPilgrimCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Warrior versus Transurfing pilgrim"@en, "Krieger versus Transurfing-Pilger"@de ;
    skos:definition "Warriors, vaguely sensing freedom exists, wrongly think it must be fought for and live in constant tension and discipline, forever postponing the main fight. The Transurfing pilgrim does not fight, knowing freedom is already his. The nearest thing to battle in Transurfing, intending to act impeccably,, which asks for awareness rather than tactics and discipline."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingTheFighter: contrasted with the Transurfing pilgrim, who knows freedom is already his; impeccable action needs awareness, not discipline."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Ending the Battle'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPostponingAsRehearsalCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Postponing turns life into rehearsal"@en, "Aufschub macht das Leben zur Probe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Deferring the permission to have makes the present a rehearsal for a better future that then never arrives, chased like the setting sun; believing one has time to spare is illusory."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Deferring the permission to have makes the present a rehearsal for a better future that then never arrives, chased like the setting sun; believing one has time to spare is illusory; it bears on pmp:TranserfingAllowingOneselfToHaveCh13."@en, "Differs from pmc:TranserfingPostponingDreamLifetimeCh9: deferral turns the present into a rehearsal for a future that never arrives, and the remedy is to admit the future now."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Ending the Battle'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWillToHaveCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The will to have"@en, "Der Wille zu haben"@de ;
    skos:definition "The calm, unemotional intention of taking what undoubtedly belongs to one, as opposed to decisiveness or battling oneself; said to be infinitely stronger than the will to act. Arises from free intention energy and is filled with it; flows from heart-mind unity. Those born rich are said to possess it without thinking."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en, "Differs from pmc:TranserfingWillToHaveCh8: defined as dispassionate intention to take what is one's own, as calm as fetching the post, and called far stronger than the will to act."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Ending the Battle'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingAllowingOneselfToHaveCh13 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Allowing oneself to have"@en, "Sich erlauben zu haben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: bring the future into the present instead of awaiting it; permit yourself to have right now, without conditions or reservations, continually, from today, not by trying but by doing; do not expect instant results; do not think about money or the means; work with slides, focusing on the goal as already achieved; earn the will to have rather than money."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingPermissionHaveCh8: given as a practice: from today, without conditions and all the time, not expecting instant results and not thinking of money."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Ending the Battle'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPermissionYieldsWillToHaveCh13 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Permission to have yields the will to have"@en, "Erlaubnis zu haben ergibt den Willen zu haben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Continually allowing oneself to have is the route given to the will to have."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingAllowingOneselfToHaveCh13 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingWillToHaveCh13 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Ending the Battle'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMiracleOneFineDayCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Something others call a miracle"@en, "Etwas, das andere ein Wunder nennen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: if one keeps permitting oneself to have without expecting quick results, one day an event occurs that others would call miraculous; outer intention finds a way to provide, doors open and the means take care of themselves."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingAllowingOneselfToHaveCh13."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Ending the Battle'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPathOfMeansCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The path of means never yields enough"@en, "Der Weg über die Mittel reicht nie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Fretting over whether the goal is realistic and how to reach it is the path of battle; on it one will never earn enough money."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Fretting over whether the goal is realistic and how to reach it is the path of battle; on it one will never earn enough money; it bears on pmp:TranserfingAllowingOneselfToHaveCh13."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Ending the Battle'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingChoiceAsImmutableLawCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Choice as immutable law"@en, "Wahl als unumstößliches Gesetz"@de ;
    skos:definition "Each person receives what he is willing to have; one's choice is an unalterable law shaping one's reality, and refusing this freedom is also a choice. Willingness to have explains why some take holidays every week while others save for years."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingChosenWorldviewManifests: stated as a law of willingness: each receives what he is ready to have, illustrated by the holidaying couple."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Ending the Battle'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAlternativesSpaceShopCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The alternatives-space shop"@en, "Der Laden des Variantenraums"@de ;
    skos:definition "Allegory: in a supermarket a customer asking for stardom is offered it outright, but keeps objecting (no talent, harsh industry, too good to be true) until the assistant shelves the item. Achieving a goal is a matter of choice, like flying as a passenger: being willing to have is all."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingChoosingDestiny: told as a full dialogue in which the customer talks himself out of the item the assistant offers."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Ending the Battle'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDoNotForcePermissionCh13 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not force the permission to have"@en, "Die Erlaubnis zu haben nicht erzwingen"@de ;
    skos:definition "One can fall into battling oneself for the will to have: never compel yourself to allow, never compel the target slide, avoid tension and pressure, which would turn it into a battle once more; just enjoy exciting thoughts."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingAllowingOneselfToHaveCh13 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Ending the Battle'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingForcefulResolveCh13 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Forceful resolve tightens the grip"@en, "Kraftvoller Entschluss verstärkt den Griff"@de ;
    skos:definition "Acting forcefully, even resolute and confident, creates excess potential; trying to release the grip tightens it, and every effort or diligence worsens excess potential. Importance is the root of effort and compulsive grip, and fighting the grip cannot loosen it."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingAssertivenessMistakenWillHaveCh9: adds that trying to loosen the grip tightens it, since importance underlies every effort."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingWillToHaveCh13 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Ending the Battle'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingLightHeartedResolveCh13 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Light-hearted resolve"@en, "Unbeschwerte Entschlossenheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: relax, loosen control and simply be aware that you are collecting your own, as unexcitedly as buying a newspaper (if one shop lacks it, go to another); drop importance and the grip loosens by itself; exercise the right to choose as calmly as fetching the mail; you are your own examiner, so stop the habitual verdicts that you are unworthy or the goal unrealistic; let go of desire and just think of taking what is already yours."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Ending the Battle'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingImportanceShiftsIntentionZoneCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Importance shifts intention between zones"@en, "Bedeutsamkeit verschiebt die Absicht zwischen den Zonen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Lowering importance moves the pointer of intention from the inner to the outer intention zone; pressure stems from importance and is inner intention at work. Willpower serves to overcome obstacles, but obstacles are born of importance and dissolve when it drops, so willpower is no longer needed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Ending the Battle'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLightHeartedResolveYieldsWillToHaveCh13 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Light-hearted resolve yields the will to have"@en, "Unbeschwerte Entschlossenheit ergibt den Willen zu haben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Calmly taking without pressure is said to turn the urge to push into the will to have, after which outer intention takes over."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingLightHeartedResolveCh13 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingWillToHaveCh13 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Ending the Battle'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingZealToWinChoiceCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Vigorous decisiveness to conquer the right of choice"@en, "Ungestüme Entschlossenheit, das Wahlrecht zu erkämpfen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Being full of zeal to win one's right to choose means holding the deadly grip again: disappointment follows, balanced forces quickly cool the ardour and pendulums, sensing importance, provoke at once. Presented as observable by the reader."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Being full of zeal to win one's right to choose means holding the deadly grip again: disappointment follows, balanced forces quickly cool the ardour and pendulums, sensing importance, provoke at once. Presented as observable by the reader; it bears on pmc:TranserfingWillToHaveCh13."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Ending the Battle'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFailedAttemptsNormalCh13 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Failed attempts at calm will are normal"@en, "Misslungene Versuche ruhigen Willens sind normal"@de ;
    skos:definition "One should not be upset by failed attempts at gaining dispassionate will; habits of feeding pendulums are strong, and in time one learns to tell decisiveness from will."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingLightHeartedResolveCh13 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Ending the Battle'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Release'
#

pmc:TranserfingHeartMindUnityBeforeWillToHaveCh13 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Heart-mind unity before the will to have"@en, "Einklang von Herz und Verstand vor dem Willen zu haben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Acquiring the will to have requires unity of heart and mind; heart-mind conflict is the first obstacle to allowing oneself to have. Thoughts must come from that unity."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingWillToHaveCh13 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingEdinstvoDushiIRazuma ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Intention energy is programmed impurely and the thought stays empty talk of the mind." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Release'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWillToHaveIsNotWantingCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Will to have is not \"I want and I will\""@en, "Wille zu haben ist nicht „ich will und ich werde“"@de ;
    skos:definition "Merely thinking that one wants and will get is mistaken; such thoughts need to carry the energy of intention or they are just mental chatter."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Release'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingBicycleModelOfWillCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Learning to ride a bicycle as model of will"@en, "Radfahrenlernen als Modell des Willens"@de ;
    skos:definition "A beginner on a bicycle produces three excess potentials, doubt, desire and control, which drain intention; the bike falls as long as heart-mind unity and free energy are lacking. When the mind slackens control, unity appears and one suddenly can ride without the mind knowing how; the mind accepts the fact and drops control, the other potentials fade with practice and the challenge becomes pleasure."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Release'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHeartAndMindContrastedCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Heart and mind contrasted"@en, "Herz und Verstand im Gegensatz"@de ;
    skos:definition "The mind thinks about means, controls and tries options, and is willing to have only on condition of clarity and rationality; the heart does not think and is unreservedly willing. Their conflict arises from the mind doubting the goal is realistic; when control weakens the mind's limiting conditions fall away and unity is revealed."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingHeartKnowsNoMeansMindThinksX10: the conflict is traced to the mind doubting the goal is realistic, and unity is said to appear as soon as its control slackens."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Release'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFreeEnergyBeforeWillToHaveCh13 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Freed intention energy before the will to have"@en, "Freigesetzte Absichtsenergie vor dem Willen zu haben"@de ;
    skos:definition "The second obstacle: excess potentials of importance, inner and outer, eat up free energy; intention energy must be released."@en ;
    skos:note "The prior step is free intention energy, pmc:TranserfingEnergiyaNamereniya, typed by part 1 of Stupen' III."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingWillToHaveCh13 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingEnergiyaNamereniya ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "With most free energy bound in excess potential, intention lacks power." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Release'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRightDoorBeforeUnityCh13 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "The right door before heart-mind unity"@en, "Die richtige Tür vor dem Einklang"@de ;
    skos:definition "Heart-mind unity is said to come when one is on the way to one's goal through one's own door; what remains is to find one's innermost aspirations and set off."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingEdinstvoDushiIRazuma ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingDver ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:presentationOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Release'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingEnergyTiedInPotentialCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Ninety-nine percent of energy in excess potential"@en, "Neunundneunzig Prozent der Energie im Überschusspotenzial"@de ;
    skos:definition "Carrying inner and outer importance is said to waste almost all one's energy on sustaining excess potential, leaving none free; laying it down releases intention, the driving force of transition in the alternatives space."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Release'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingDroppingImportanceByActionCh13 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Dropping importance consciously, then by action"@en, "Bedeutsamkeit bewusst ablegen, notfalls durch Handeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: notice what you give excess meaning to and what follows from it; since intellectual renunciation often fails, act, because excess potential dissipates through doing: rotate the target slide mentally, visualise the process, and calmly step by step move toward the goal."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingActDontThink: the action named is inner as well as outer: turning the target slide, visualising the process and stepping toward the goal."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Release'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingIntellectualRenunciationCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Intellectual renunciation of importance often fails"@en, "Verstandesmäßiger Verzicht auf Bedeutsamkeit misslingt oft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Trying to give up importance on the intellectual level alone is said not to succeed reliably."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Trying to give up importance on the intellectual level alone is said not to succeed reliably; it bears on pmp:TranserfingDroppingImportanceByActionCh13."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Release'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRemediesForExcessPotentialsCh13 a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Remedies for the single excess potentials"@en, "Abhilfen gegen die einzelnen Überschusspotenziale"@de ;
    skos:definition "A question-and-answer list pairs each burden with its cure: fear with a safety net or a plan B, anxiety and waiting with action, desire with accepting possible defeat and then acting, low worth with ending the battle for it, irritability with breaking the pendulum's rules, guilt with no longer justifying oneself, resentment with leaving the battle and moving with the current, and, where that fails, permission not to cope."@en ;
    skos:note "Repeated almost item by item in the chapter SUMMARY; the single remedies are entered as their own practices."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Release'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingAcceptingDefeatAgainstDesireCh13 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Against desire: accept defeat and act"@en, "Gegen Begehren: Niederlage einkalkulieren und handeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Since fully giving up desire is nearly impossible, accept beforehand that you may fail and prepare alternative routes, which balances the potential; turn desire into determination to act, so its energy disperses and goes into shaping intention."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingAcceptDefeatFirstCh7: given as a practice that also turns desire into resolve to act, so that its energy goes into shaping intention."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Release'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingActingAgainstWaitingCh13 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Against waiting: act"@en, "Gegen Warten: handeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "The potential of waiting disperses by definition through action; dissolve desire and expectation in doing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Release'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingNotGuardingSelfWorthCh13 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Letting go of guarding self-worth"@en, "Das Verteidigen des Selbstwerts lassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Take your worth as axiomatic, then stop acting to raise it: examine your reflexes when worth feels threatened (demanding attention or respect, needing to be right, taking offence, defending and justifying, entering conflict, acting superior, insisting on leading, belittling others, showing off) and refrain from rushing to defend it, since others sense these reactions subconsciously."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Release'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTreatedDifferentlyCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Treated differently, worth acknowledged"@en, "Anders behandelt, Wert anerkannt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: not reflexively defending one's esteem signals healthy worth; people treat one differently, the mind then recognises its value, and others without exception see it too. Giving it up returns it."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingNotGuardingSelfWorthCh13."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Release'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNotGuardingYieldsSelfWorthCh13 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Not guarding worth yields self-worth"@en, "Nicht-Verteidigen ergibt Selbstwert"@de ;
    skos:definition "Abandoning worth-raising behaviour is said to make one's standing grow."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingNotGuardingSelfWorthCh13 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingSelfWorthCh13 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Release'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingBreakingRulesAgainstIrritationCh13 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Against irritability: break the game rules"@en, "Gegen Reizbarkeit: die Spielregeln brechen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Remember fast that it is a game and break the rules with humour by an inadequate reaction to unpleasant news; conversely, meet good news not limply but with open enthusiasm, radiating at the frequency of the wave of fortune. This upsets the pendulum's rhythm."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingInappropriateReaction: aimed at the habit of irritability, and good news is to be met with open enthusiasm to vibrate with the wave of fortune."@en, "Called the only way to drop the habit of negative reaction."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Release'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingLeavingTheCourtroomCh13 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Leaving the courtroom of guilt"@en, "Den Gerichtssaal der Schuld verlassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Stop justifying yourself; recognise that you alone keep yourself on trial, playing prosecutor, counsel and accused while manipulators profit; walk out of the court, nobody can hold you; the onlookers leave once no defendant is present."@en ;
    skos:note "Called the only way to be rid of guilt."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Release'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCaseClosedCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The case is closed"@en, "Der Fall wird geschlossen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: with time the case closes and guilt feelings are gone."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingLeavingTheCourtroomCh13."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Release'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLeavingCourtroomYieldsFreedomFromGuiltCh13 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Leaving the courtroom yields freedom from guilt"@en, "Verlassen des Gerichtssaals ergibt Schuldfreiheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Leaving the inner court is said to remove guilt."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingLeavingTheCourtroomCh13 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingReleaseOfGuilt ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Release'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingHandlingResentmentCh13 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Handling resentment and indignation"@en, "Umgang mit Groll und Empörung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: shed guilt and recognise your worth, after which such anger is said not to arise; stop battling and move with the current; if you still cannot cope, permit yourself not to cope; until working only for yourself on your own path, allow yourself occasional outbursts and do not demand of yourself to win always; instead of fighting your potentials, act with intention purified through movement."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Release'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingProblemFindersCh13 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Problem-finders pull you against the current"@en, "Problemsucher ziehen gegen die Strömung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Some people only find problems and present them as achievements, expecting others to solve them; starting to solve for them draws a crowd of critics, new problems, advice and demands, provoking resentment."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingHandlingResentmentCh13 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Release'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWorkingForABossCh13 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Working for a boss breeds resentment"@en, "Arbeit für einen Chef nährt Groll"@de ;
    skos:definition "Working for someone else is said to bring regular resentment and indignation inevitably; the remedy is to move onto the path toward one's own goal, so that eventually one works only for oneself. Overvaluing the need to keep importance low only worsens matters."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingHandlingResentmentCh13 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Release'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingIntentionPurifiedByDoingCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Intention is purified by doing"@en, "Absicht reinigt sich im Tun"@de ;
    skos:definition "Achieving the will to have needs concrete action, not speculation; intention is purified in movement, and actions grow more effective in the course of doing."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingWillHavePrevailsWillActPurifiedX10: the purifying is said to happen in movement itself, so that action grows more effective while it is done."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Release'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingThreeStagesOfWillToHaveCh13 a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "Three stages of willingness to have"@en, "Drei Stufen des Willens zu haben"@de ;
    skos:definition "First, inhibition before the unfamiliar: running the target slide, one cannot quite accept it could all be possible. Second, delight close to weightlessness, as the goal enters the comfort zone, restriction falls away and intention energy leaves excess potential. Third, ordinariness, as constant rotation of the slide makes its content feel normal."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingComfortZoneStagesTowardWillHaveCh8: the stages belong to the will to have itself (inhibition, delight, ordinariness) instead of leading up to it."@en, "No consequence of skipping a stage is named, so no pm:Presupposing pairs are entered."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmc:TranserfingInhibitionStageCh13 ;
    rdf:_2 pmc:TranserfingDelightStageCh13 ;
    rdf:_3 pmc:TranserfingOrdinarinessStageCh13 ;
    pm:seriesStatement "The order runs from disbelief through elation to normality: the content of the slide first seems too much to accept, then feels light once it is inside the comfort zone, and at last becomes commonplace through steady rotation." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Release'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingInhibitionStageCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "First stage of the will to have: inhibition"@en, "Erste Stufe des Willens zu haben: Hemmung"@de ;
    skos:definition "At first the unfamiliar situation holds one back: running the target slide, one cannot yet take in that all of it might really be meant for oneself."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Release'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDelightStageCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Second stage of the will to have: delight"@en, "Zweite Stufe des Willens zu haben: Entzücken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Next comes elation close to weightlessness: the goal enters the comfort zone, the sense of restriction drops away and seeing the goal as realistic lifts one; the lightness is put down to intention energy leaving excess potential."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Release'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingOrdinarinessStageCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Third stage of the will to have: ordinariness"@en, "Dritte Stufe des Willens zu haben: Gewöhnlichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "In time, because the slide keeps being turned over in the mind, one thinks oneself into its content and everything in it comes to seem normal."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Release'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingKeepTheWillToActCh13 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Keep the will to act"@en, "Den Willen zu handeln behalten"@de ;
    skos:definition "While importance dissolves and the will to have strengthens, one must not drop the will to act, the intention to keep stepping toward the goal. While one desires, doubts and puzzles over means, the will to have stands on shaky ground."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingWillToHaveCh13 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Release'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingThreeStagesPassedCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Passing all three stages"@en, "Alle drei Stufen durchlaufen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced signs: elation and a real feeling of weightlessness at the second stage; having gone through all three stages means one is surely on the right road."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmc:TranserfingThreeStagesOfWillToHaveCh13 and pmp:TranserfingSystematicallyRunningTargetSlideX10."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Release'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Intention'
#

pmc:TranserfingHillsPitsAndEvenRoadCh13 a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Hills, pits and the even road"@en, "Hügel, Gruben und die ebene Straße"@de ;
    skos:definition "People walk a road flanked by tall hills and deep holes: the confident and determined climb toward glittering prizes set by pendulums and are mostly blown back down by balanced forces; negativists wallow in the pits of their worst expectations. Coordination means walking the even road between."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingExtremesAndRoles: the extremes are climbers after pendulum prizes and negativists in the pits, and coordination is the level road between them."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNegativistDragsOthersCh13 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "A negativist drags others along"@en, "Ein Negativist zieht andere mit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Negativity changes the layer of the negativist's world and pulls those closest, whose layers intersect his, into his misery; weaning him from comfort in self-torment is extremely hard."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingNegativistsPowerCh13 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNegativistsPowerCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The negativist's hidden power"@en, "Die verborgene Macht des Negativisten"@de ;
    skos:definition "The negativist seems powerless but uses a real power: the firm belief that life is awful and worsening is itself the will to have, so his choice materialises and the world meets him halfway. This is taken to show that everyone can shape the script in waking life, not only in dreams."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPositiveMottoOnCloudsCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The positive motto as a walk on clouds"@en, "Das positive Motto als Wolkenwanderung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Simply swapping the negative motto for \"life is wonderful and getting better\" puts one on a walk across clouds: one moment of doubt or a fearful glance down and one stops and falls from a height."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Simply swapping the negative motto for \"life is wonderful and getting better\" puts one on a walk across clouds: one moment of doubt or a fearful glance down and one stops and falls from a height; it bears on pmp:TranserfingCoordinatingIntentionCh13."@en, "Differs from pmc:TranserfingAffirmationsFail: a single motto adopted as a stance, which fails at the first doubt like a fall from the clouds."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingBirthTraumaRootOfNegativityCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Birth trauma as root of negativity"@en, "Geburtstrauma als Wurzel der Negativität"@de ;
    skos:definition "The deep predisposition to negativity is traced to the harsh conventional birth: pain, cold, glare, cut cord, a slap and separation from the mother teach the newborn that life is a battle for survival and lay the base of guilt, fear and powerlessness, giving pendulums their inroad; later falls and scares reinforce it. Positivism, conversely, tends to lift one into castles in the air or into storming fortresses."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingNegativityBias: the bias is traced to the shock of conventional birth, not to survival in ancient times."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingCoordinatingIntentionCh13 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Coordinating intention"@en, "Koordination der Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "A game offered to the controlling mind: whenever something bad happens, the mind must wake up, consciously assess how much importance it is assigning and alter how it relates to the problem. Main principle: choose to regard apparently negative turns of the script as positive. In practice: pause before reacting like an oyster; tell yourself it is only a game with the golem and accept the game; stay positive and act pleased whatever happens; look for the good side of any annoyance and be glad even if none is found; cultivate the habit of rejoicing at setbacks."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRealisingThePositiveCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Realising the positive"@en, "Das Positive verwirklichen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Said to be gainable: success in realising favourable outcomes equal to the success negativists have in realising their worst expectations."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCoordinatingIntentionYieldsRealisedPositiveCh13 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Coordinating intention yields realised positives"@en, "Koordination der Absicht ergibt verwirklichtes Positives"@de ;
    skos:definition "Following the main principle of coordination is said to bring that level of success."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingCoordinatingIntentionCh13 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingRealisingThePositiveCh13 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingKoordinatsiyaNamereniya a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Main principle of coordination"@en, "Hauptprinzip der Koordination"@de ;
    skos:definition "If apparently negative script changes are perceived as positive, their outcome is said to become positive; claimed to work every time, to be tested rather than believed."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingTurningApparentSetbacksFavourableTurnsPerceptionX10: here named the main principle of coordination, said to work every time and grounded in the two branches of each event."@en, "Shared system term of Stupen' III (coordination of intention), typed by this part; the practice is pmp:TranserfingCoordinatingIntentionCh13."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTwoBranchesOfEveryEventCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Two branches of every event"@en, "Zwei Zweige jedes Ereignisses"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rationale for the mind: the world is dual, and as one raises the opposite arm when slipping off a log, each event of a life line has a favourable and an unfavourable branch; choosing one's relation to the event places one on the corresponding branch."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTrailOfTroubleCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Trail of trouble"@en, "Pechsträhne"@de ;
    skos:definition "Irritation from the morning on turns small events into a chain of trouble (\"things come in threes\"): the chain follows from one's attitude, not from the first annoyance. One radiates on the wavelength of the unfavourable branch, the tension potential drains intention, actions become ineffective and bigger irritations follow; tracking negative branches feeds generational decline."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Irritation from the morning on turns small events into a chain of trouble (\"things come in threes\"): the chain follows from one's attitude, not from the first annoyance. One radiates on the wavelength of the unfavourable branch, the tension potential drains intention, actions become ineffective and bigger irritations follow; tracking negative branches feeds generational decline; it bears on pmp:TranserfingCoordinatingIntentionCh13."@en, "Differs from pmc:TranserfingIrritationFollowedByMishap: the chain starts from one's own attitude to a first small annoyance and runs along unfavourable branches."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingInconvenienceTurnsToAdvantageCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Inconvenience turns to advantage"@en, "Ungemach wendet sich zum Vorteil"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: in most cases the annoyance will work in one's favour; where it does not, the positive attitude is said to have shielded one from further misfortune and carried one onto a favourable line."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingCoordinatingIntentionCh13."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAnnoyanceAsDeviationCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Annoyance as deviation from the norm"@en, "Ärger als Abweichung von der Norm"@de ;
    skos:definition "Good fortune and happiness are said to be the norm; annoyances are strong departures from balance that demand extra energy, which one supplies oneself by building obstacles and afterwards surmounting them. The mind automatically views any departure from a script it has signed up to as bad and tries to regain control."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingOriginalScriptJudges: adds that good fortune is the norm and that annoyance costs energy one supplies oneself."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingAgreeingToScriptChangesCh13 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Agreeing to every script change"@en, "Jeder Skriptänderung zustimmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: explain the game to the mind, telling it that it keeps control but that control now means viewing all events as positive; activate the Guardian at the start of the day; hold a rough picture of how the day should go; the moment the scenario shifts, accept and agree to the change and act as if it were exactly what was needed; do not hurry to voice displeasure or fight the situation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSlidingControlCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Gliding control over the scenario"@en, "Gleitende Kontrolle über das Szenario"@de ;
    skos:definition "A dynamic, sliding hold on changes to the scenario: by surrendering control over the script one regains it, now aimed at moving with the alternatives flow, and keeps one's own attitude and therefore the situation in hand."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAgreeingYieldsSlidingControlCh13 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Agreeing to changes yields gliding control"@en, "Zustimmung zu Änderungen ergibt gleitende Kontrolle"@de ;
    skos:definition "Accepting script changes as they come is said to produce this sliding control."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingAgreeingToScriptChangesCh13 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingSlidingControlCh13 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSecretOfCoordinationCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Secret of coordination: loosen and take charge"@en, "Geheimnis der Koordination: loslassen und in die Hand nehmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Coordination consists in releasing the grip of control while at the same time taking matters into one's own hands; a tight grip prevents the situation from unfolding in harmony with the flow."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingProblemsAvoidedCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Problems avoided, things turn out well"@en, "Probleme bleiben aus, alles gerät gut"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: whoever starts practising the coordination principle gets exactly what everyone wants, avoidance of problems and good outcomes."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingAgreeingToScriptChangesCh13."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCoordinationOutperformsOuterIntentionCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Coordination outperforms direct outer intention"@en, "Koordination übertrifft direkte äußere Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "The coordination principle is called more effective than trying to sway events by outer intention: the mind cannot foresee every move, since one's world layer crosses countless others; it need only run the target slide and keep to the principle, and outer intention then delivers the goal."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPracticeDevelopsCoordinationCh13 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Practice, not intellect, develops coordination"@en, "Übung, nicht Verstand, entwickelt Koordination"@de ;
    skos:definition "Coordination grows through practice; understanding the principle intellectually does not suffice, the ability must be continually developed and refined and the Guardian kept active."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingKoordinatsiyaVazhnosti ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingCoordinatingImportanceCh13 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFavourableBranchesCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Moving onto favourable branches"@en, "Auf günstige Zweige wechseln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Coordination is said to be the best way to travel in the alternatives space: perceiving each event as positive, one always passes onto favourable life-line branches and meets the wave of fortune more often."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCoordinatingIntentionYieldsFavourableBranchesCh13 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Coordinating intention yields favourable branches"@en, "Koordination der Absicht ergibt günstige Zweige"@de ;
    skos:definition "Treating every event as positive is said to shift one onto favourable branches."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingCoordinatingIntentionCh13 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingFavourableBranchesCh13 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHeadInTheCloudsCh13 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not drift into the clouds"@en, "Nicht in die Wolken abheben"@de ;
    skos:definition "One must not float off with head in the clouds; what is needed is conscious, deliberate action that keeps balance while riding the wave of fortune, called the essence of Transurfing."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingCoordinatingIntentionCh13 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Coordinating Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Apples Fall to the Sky'
#

pmc:TranserfingReceivingWhatOneIsWillingCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "One receives what one is willing to receive"@en, "Man erhält, was man zu empfangen bereit ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reading the scriptural saying about faith: one gets only as much as one is willing to accept, outer intention executes the order faultlessly, and what one has matches the template of one's worldview and sense of one's place. Knowing the main principles, one can steer fate by free will."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Apples Fall to the Sky'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingBlindBeliefOfTheMindCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The mind's blind belief"@en, "Der blinde Glaube des Verstandes"@de ;
    skos:definition "The mind cannot be convinced before facts, yet it can pretend and can hold blind, fanatical, usually false belief, an intense excess potential from inflating the meaning of a conviction; it then sees and hears nothing else. When the mind crawls into the box where it shut the heart, belief is blind, and outer intention never fills its sail."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Apples Fall to the Sky'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFalseBeliefTrapCh13 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "False belief is a pendulum trap"@en, "Falscher Glaube ist eine Pendelfalle"@de ;
    skos:definition "False belief is said to be a snare set by the pendulum inside the labyrinth of insecurity: it feels like escape but is illusory, with doubts walled off below awareness by a protective wall of faith."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingBlindBeliefOfTheMindCh13 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Apples Fall to the Sky'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFalseAndTrueBeliefCh13 a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "False versus true belief"@en, "Falscher versus wahrer Glaube"@de ;
    skos:definition "Criterion: true belief is knowledge, formed by facts; a belief is false whenever one has to talk oneself into it, by enthusiasm or by compulsion, and it is held up by the mind's control, which keeps every doubt out. Hoping minds refuse to listen."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Apples Fall to the Sky'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingTestingBeliefByDiscomfortCh13 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Testing a belief by inner discomfort"@en, "Einen Glauben am inneren Unbehagen prüfen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: loosen the mind's control and turn attention to the faintest signs of inner unease (the faint rustle of morning stars); if a pang of discomfort shows, stop trying to persuade yourself of the idea you wanted to adopt. In heart-mind unity no self-persuasion is needed."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingDiscomfortAsSign: the sign is used to test a belief one is trying to adopt, not a decision."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Apples Fall to the Sky'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAffirmationsFeedDoubtCh13 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Affirmations strengthen doubt"@en, "Affirmationen stärken den Zweifel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Talking oneself round with positive affirmations such as insisting one will get one's way does not remove doubt; it prepares fertile soil for it. The heart cannot be persuaded, since it does not grasp logic or the mind's language."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingAffirmationsFail: adds that such affirmations make doubt grow, because the heart does not take in logic."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingBlindBeliefOfTheMindCh13 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Apples Fall to the Sky'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHeartKnowsNoHalfTonesCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The heart knows no half tones"@en, "Das Herz kennt keine Zwischentöne"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asked whether the goal will be reached, the heart answers only yes or no, never maybe; the faintest shadow of doubt makes the answer no, and nothing can talk it round. Doubt is partial belief, which the heart turns into a firm no; the heart neither believes nor doubts but knows."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Apples Fall to the Sky'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingReplacingBeliefWithKnowingCh13 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Replacing believing with knowing"@en, "Glauben durch Wissen ersetzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: strike believing out of your template of the world and set knowing in its place; grant yourself the knowing that the wish will be fulfilled; grow used to and accept that knowing, as people got used to telephones and planes; use the slide technique, keeping the knowledge in mind until outer intention turns it into fact; remind rather than convince yourself; whenever doubts and thoughts of means creep in, fish them out at once with the thought that success hinges on your choice, which is made, so there is nothing to hesitate over; do not fight doubts; recall each time that you alone decide."@en ;
    skos:note "Later in the section the author reveals this passage as a demonstration of the belief trap (see the caution on the author leading the reader into the labyrinth)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Apples Fall to the Sky'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLawOfReachingTheGoalCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Law of reaching the goal"@en, "Gesetz des Zielerreichens"@de ;
    skos:definition "Stated law: the goal will be reached when there is the will to have together with the will to act, moving through the right door. With the heart's knowing one can settle the outcome of an event that can go either way."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Apples Fall to the Sky'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDoubtsFadeCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Doubts fade gradually"@en, "Zweifel verblassen allmählich"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: answering each doubt with the reminder of one's own choice makes doubts gradually fade; knowledge free of belief leaves doubt no room."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingReplacingBeliefWithKnowingCh13."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Apples Fall to the Sky'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingKnowingFreeOfDoubtCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Knowing free of doubt"@en, "Wissen ohne Zweifel"@de ;
    skos:definition "A knowing that contains no belief and so leaves doubt no place; held out as reached by meeting each doubt with the reminder that success rests on a choice already made."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Apples Fall to the Sky'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFightingDoubtsCh13 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Fighting doubts guarantees defeat"@en, "Kampf gegen Zweifel sichert die Niederlage"@de ;
    skos:definition "Setting out to eliminate doubts or battle their presence is called a guarantee of defeat; doubts as such do not ensure failure, though the road may get bumpy."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingReplacingBeliefWithKnowingCh13 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Apples Fall to the Sky'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHabitOfForgettingCh13 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "The habit of forgetting"@en, "Die Gewohnheit des Vergessens"@de ;
    skos:definition "Self-warning: new knowledge is quickly forgotten while old habits are deeply rooted; the reader slips back into semiconscious living and must never forget being in charge of his fate."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingRememberingWhatOneKnows: stated as a warning against forgetting and semiconscious living, with the reminder that one is in charge of one's fate."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingReplacingBeliefWithKnowingCh13 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Apples Fall to the Sky'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWalkingOnWaterCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Walking on water"@en, "Auf dem Wasser gehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author supposes that walking on water came naturally to Jesus and claims that others too could do it, were they free of the associated doubt, anxiety and emotion; history is cited as a chain of the improbable becoming normal."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en, "Linked: pmc:TranserfingJesusAsExemplarCh7, where walking on water is the measure of outer intention."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Apples Fall to the Sky'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFreedomFromDoubtBeforeWalkingOnWaterCh13 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Freedom from doubt before walking on water"@en, "Zweifelsfreiheit vor dem Gehen auf dem Wasser"@de ;
    skos:definition "Walking on water is made conditional on being rid of doubt, anxiety and the emotion connected with it."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingWalkingOnWaterCh13 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingKnowingFreeOfDoubtCh13 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:presentationOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Apples Fall to the Sky'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDraggingDoubtsCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Dragging doubts along"@en, "Zweifel mitschleppen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Carrying doubts reliably lowers the odds: of the two life lines, success and failure, wallowing in doubt radiates at the failure line's frequency, and any failure met then stems from circumstances one's own thoughts produced."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Carrying doubts reliably lowers the odds: of the two life lines, success and failure, wallowing in doubt radiates at the failure line's frequency, and any failure met then stems from circumstances one's own thoughts produced; it bears on pmp:TranserfingAskingWhichDoIChooseCh13."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Apples Fall to the Sky'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingAskingWhichDoIChooseCh13 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Asking \"which do I choose?\""@en, "Fragen „was wähle ich?“"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: replace the question whether it will happen with the question whether you choose success or failure; regularly catch the moment you give in to doubt and recall that success is a matter of choice; imagine that from today apples fall upward, until it feels ordinary. One is said to get used to it soon."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Apples Fall to the Sky'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAuthorsBeliefTrapDemonstrationCh13 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "The author's own demonstration of the belief trap"@en, "Die Selbstvorführung der Glaubensfalle durch den Autor"@de ;
    skos:definition "Caution against the book's own preceding method: the author asks the reader to wake up and notice that swapping belief for not-yet-obtained knowledge left the nature of faith unchanged; whoever believed him fell into the trap, which is exactly how pendulums win faith and trust."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingReplacingBeliefWithKnowingCh13 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Apples Fall to the Sky'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingVerifyDoNotBelieveCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Transurfing needs no faith: verify"@en, "Transurfing braucht keinen Glauben: prüfen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Statement on the method's status: only pendulums need others' faith; Transurfing does not aim to convince but to break stereotypes and help the reader leave the box of conditioning and wake into the waking dream, which can then be directed without belief. Do not believe; verify by acting, and knowing follows when it works. The author claims his material is more than speculation."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingTestInsteadOfBelief: adds that only pendulums need others' faith and that the aim is to break stereotypes and wake the reader into the waking dream."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Apples Fall to the Sky'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAgainstUnshakeableFaithCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against the doctrine of unshakeable faith"@en, "Gegen die Lehre vom unerschütterlichen Glauben"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author disputes the common teaching, tied to the scriptural word that it be done according to one's faith, that anything is achievable with unwavering faith in one's strength: doubt cannot be avoided, acquiring faith is futile, persuasion never expels doubt from the heart and only fools the mind, where doubts keep living on."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingFaithBeforeIntentionCh7: there absolute faith is required; here the striving for unshakeable faith is rejected, since doubt cannot be avoided."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Apples Fall to the Sky'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAbsoluteFaithCh13 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Give up striving for absolute faith"@en, "Das Streben nach absolutem Glauben aufgeben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Attempts to attain absolute faith are fruitless and should be dropped."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingBlindBeliefOfTheMindCh13 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Apples Fall to the Sky'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingLivingTheSlideDespiteDoubtCh13 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Living the target slide despite doubt"@en, "Das Zielbild trotz Zweifel leben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: ignore the means; play the target slide and step toward the goal; brush faith aside and live out the slide of life with the goal already reached; take pleasure in the task; treat it as concrete work of deliberately re-tuning the energy you emit toward your best expectations, since your worst ones demonstrably come true; doubts need not be fully discarded. Leave ways and means to outer intention and trust the alternatives flow."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingCalmSlideWorkWhenMeansUnknownCh8: the occasion is doubt, not ignorance of the means; faith is brushed aside and doubt need not be fully discarded."@en, "Said to be real work on energy quality rather than abstract dreaming."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Apples Fall to the Sky'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLivingTheSlideYieldsOuterIntentionCh13 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Living the slide yields outer intention"@en, "Gelebtes Zielbild ergibt äußere Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Running and living the target slide is said to activate outer intention."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingLivingTheSlideDespiteDoubtCh13, pmp:TranserfingSystematicallyRunningTargetSlideX10 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingVneshneeNamerenie ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Apples Fall to the Sky'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingUnexpectedOpeningsCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Unexpected openings appear"@en, "Unerwartete Gelegenheiten tauchen auf"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: opportunities arise in unforeseen ways, one's actions are steered closer to the goal, and apples fall upward once the mind meets the fact and lets go of control."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingLivingTheSlideDespiteDoubtCh13."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Apples Fall to the Sky'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingStrangeUnfoldingCh13 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Circumstances may unfold strangely"@en, "Umstände können sich seltsam entwickeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Events may seem to develop oddly; the mind cannot know which road leads to the goal and should not lecture the chef in his own kitchen, nor crawl back into the Procrustean bed of stereotypes that ordinary means are required."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingLivingTheSlideDespiteDoubtCh13 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Apples Fall to the Sky'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingCelebrationOfLifeInTheHeartCh13 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Carrying a celebration of life"@en, "Ein Fest des Lebens im Herzen tragen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Even while trudging to a hated job through mud and rain, hold a feeling of celebrating life in your heart."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingKeepingTheFestiveFeeling: the festive feeling is carried into an unpleasant present scene, which is said to dissolve because one's energy no longer fits it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Apples Fall to the Sky'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDifficultiesVanishCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Difficulties vanish"@en, "Schwierigkeiten verschwinden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: the difficulties soon disappear because one's energy no longer matches the frequency of that scene."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingCelebrationOfLifeInTheHeartCh13."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Apples Fall to the Sky'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHopeBeforeTransurfingCh13 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Hope before practising Transurfing"@en, "Hoffnung vor dem Praktizieren von Transurfing"@de ;
    skos:definition "Since the labyrinth of faith has no exit, the author aims to inspire hope that its walls will fall when outer intention shows apples falling upward; without that hope Transurfing cannot be practised. With hope the mind feels solid ground and the heart comes alive."@en ;
    skos:note "The text makes the practice of Transurfing as a whole depend on hope; since a tradition is no step, outer intention, through which the chapter expects the walls of the labyrinth to fall, stands as the dependent step. That choice is the compiler's."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingVneshneeNamerenie ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingHopeAsKnowingCh13 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Transurfing cannot be practised at all." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Apples Fall to the Sky'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFightOrCollapseCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fight or collapse in a crisis"@en, "Kampf oder Zusammenbruch in der Krise"@de ;
    skos:definition "Faced with misfortune, people either gear up to battle the situation or give up; both bring stress and depression, give energy to pendulums, erode the core of confidence and push some toward cigarettes, alcohol or drugs, binding them to new pendulums."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Faced with misfortune, people either gear up to battle the situation or give up; both bring stress and depression, give energy to pendulums, erode the core of confidence and push some toward cigarettes, alcohol or drugs, binding them to new pendulums; it bears on pmp:TranserfingFindingSupportInDifficultyCh13."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Apples Fall to the Sky'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingFindingSupportInDifficultyCh13 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Finding support in a difficult situation"@en, "Halt finden in einer schwierigen Lage"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: wake up and see how the situation arose, namely created by a pendulum; recognise the danger lies in one's relation to the problem, not the problem; refuse to grant the problem importance and avoid both tensing for a fight and sinking into despair; take support from knowing the pendulum wants your energy; smile inwardly and tell the pendulum it will not get your energy, that you see its hooks, will not accept the problem's importance, and choose to be free of it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Apples Fall to the Sky'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingInnerSupportCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Inner support without confidence"@en, "Innerer Halt ohne Selbstsicherheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Strength found within when outside support and confidence are gone, resting on the knowledge of what the pendulum is doing; this understanding, like hope, lifts one above the role of puppet or paper boat."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Apples Fall to the Sky'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSeeingThePendulumYieldsInnerSupportCh13 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Seeing the pendulum's aim yields inner support"@en, "Erkennen des Pendelziels ergibt inneren Halt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Becoming aware of the pendulum's design is said to embolden and give heart."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingFindingSupportInDifficultyCh13 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingInnerSupportCh13 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Apples Fall to the Sky'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHopeAsKnowingCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Hope as a kind of knowing"@en, "Hoffnung als eine Art Wissen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hope is counted as knowledge that not everything is lost and a way out exists; grasping how a problem works weighs as much as hope. Where hope appears, apathy lifts and intention energy is freed; with it the mind stands on firm ground and the heart comes alive."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Apples Fall to the Sky'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingMistakesAsCapitalCh13 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Past mistakes as capital"@en, "Fehler der Vergangenheit als Kapital"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: hold that nothing is lost; where an earlier goal is objectively closed, set a new one, possible at any age since everyone has several; treat past mistakes and failures as capital, and after a big failure be glad, being on the path to success."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingCorrectingPastMistakes: mistakes are not undone but treated as capital: a closed goal is replaced by a new one, and failure is welcomed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Apples Fall to the Sky'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingShiningSuccessCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Shining success"@en, "Glänzender Erfolg"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: taking this stance brings brilliant success; experience held worthless will serve on the target life line."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingMistakesAsCapitalCh13."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Apples Fall to the Sky'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSelfReproachCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Self-reproach makes failure repeat"@en, "Selbstvorwürfe lassen Misserfolg wiederkehren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Beating oneself up, whining and complaining after a failure is said to make it recur again and again."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Beating oneself up, whining and complaining after a failure is said to make it recur again and again; it bears on pmp:TranserfingMistakesAsCapitalCh13."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Apples Fall to the Sky'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFlyAtTheWindowpaneCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The fly at the windowpane"@en, "Die Fliege an der Fensterscheibe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Image: a fly drilled to fly straight at its goal beats against the pane beside an open window; so are people who do not see how goals are reached. Knowing an open window exists nearby, even unseen, gives hope, and hope releases the energy of intention; apathy lifts when new hope appears, like the oasis seen by the exhausted."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingStopTheFlyBeforeFreedom: the fly is an image of not seeing how goals are reached, and knowing the open window exists gives hope."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Apples Fall to the Sky'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHopeBeforeActionCh13 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Hope before action and released intention"@en, "Hoffnung vor Handeln und freigesetzter Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hope is said to release the energy of intention and to be needed for starting action; once hope has done its work, awareness of freedom of choice follows."@en ;
    skos:note "The dependent step is released intention energy, pmc:TranserfingEnergiyaNamereniya, typed by part 1 of Stupen' III; taking action follows from it."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingEnergiyaNamereniya ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingHopeAsKnowingCh13 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Apples Fall to the Sky'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFromHopingToIntendingCh13 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "From hoping to intending"@en, "Vom Hoffen zum Beabsichtigen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced endpoint: after hope has done its work one becomes aware of freedom of choice and tells oneself that one neither wants nor hopes but intends (the chapter motto)."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmc:TranserfingHopeBeforeActionCh13."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIII Coordination, section 'Apples Fall to the Sky'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# prima-materia — Transerfing: Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III:
# Vpered v proshloe! (2004), part 3: chapter XIV Forward to the Past and
# chapter XV Letters from the Past, to the closing SUMMARY.
#
# Two independent extraction passes ran over the text (A 166 records, B 162;
# 14 records of B without counterpart in A: 1 added, 12 covered, 1 not owed);
# a reader of the whole part added 5 records both passes missed and refiled
# 4 (the three elements of transaction as a series, their order folded into
# it, the exam story as a case report, the polemic on church donations as a
# concept). Stupen' I and II (traditions/transerfing-stupen-1.ttl, -2.ttl)
# are not restated: 11 records whose claim a node there already carries are
# left out and linked; 30 nodes that restate an earlier node with a
# difference say so in a note.
#
# Shared system terms typed here: pmc:TranserfingTransaktsiya,
# pmc:TranserfingSkolzhenie, pmc:TranserfingInversiya. Linked, typed by other
# parts of Stupen' III: pmc:TranserfingEnergiya (part 1),
# pmc:TranserfingKoordinatsiyaNamereniya, pmc:TranserfingKoordinatsiyaVazhnosti
# (part 2). Readers' letters quoted in chapter XV are third-party ascriptions;
# the author's answers are textual; his student-days stories are first-person
# reports.
#

#
# ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Transaction'
#

pmc:TranserfingTestingOverBeliefTransactionImmediatelyVisibleCh14 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Testing over belief; transaction as immediately visible result"@en, "Prüfen statt Glauben; Transaktion als sofort sichtbares Ergebnis"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author asks readers not to accept Transurfing on faith but to try its principles; outer intention normally acts slowly and almost imperceptibly, whereas the transaction exercise is offered as a way to witness one's own shift through the alternatives space at once, without astral or dream work."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingTestInsteadOfBelief: the call to test rather than believe recurs; new is the claim that transaction lets one see one's shift through the alternatives space at once, whereas outer intention normally works slowly. Statement on how the method is to be validated (personal trial) and on the slow, hardly noticeable working of outer intention."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Transaction'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingTransactionCh14 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Transaction"@en, "Transaktion"@de ;
    skos:definition "A single three-part act: (1) turn the key to switch on the central energy currents; (2) run the target slide, placing yourself inside a scene where the goal is reached, adding touch, sound, smell, for about a minute or longer, eyes resting loosely on the ground a little ahead; (3) once the slide is fairly distinct, raise the eyes and look forward and into the distance with clear, aware sight, without thinking or analysing. Best done relaxed, while walking somewhere familiar, outdoors rather than among plain objects."@en ;
    skos:note "Elements 1-3 named by the author; practised lightly, at odd moments, out of curiosity. Its order of elements is held in pmc:TranserfingThreeElementsOfTransactionCh14; the concept is pmc:TranserfingTransaktsiya."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Transaction'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingClearSightCh14 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Clear sight"@en, "Klarer Blick"@de ;
    skos:definition "Third element of transaction: when the slide stands fairly clear, lift the gaze and take in, with alert awareness and no thinking or analysing, whatever lies ahead and further off, for the few seconds the gust lasts."@en ;
    skos:note "Entered by the reader so that the three elements can be held as a series (pmc:TranserfingThreeElementsOfTransactionCh14)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Transaction'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMeridianFamiliarityBeforeTurningKeyCh14 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Meridian familiarity before turning the key"@en, "Vertrautheit mit den Meridianen vor dem Schlüsseldrehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The first element presupposes recalling the central meridians, known from the energy exercises taught earlier in the book."@en ;
    skos:note "Prior practice lies outside this unit (energy exercises, earlier part)."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:TranserfingTurningTheKeyCh14 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingEnergiya ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Transaction'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingTurningTheKeyCh14 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Turning the key"@en, "Den Schlüssel drehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Scan the body and let muscle tension go; picture energy rising and descending along the spine; imagine two arrows pointing horizontally out of the body's centre, one to the front and one behind, reaching 20-30 cm or further; rotate both together so the front one swings up and the rear one down until both stand parallel to the spine. Can be done standing or walking; no need to form fountains or a sphere; the point is to imagine being filled by the flow. Repeat many times daily, especially whenever an unpleasant or worrying thought is noticed."@en ;
    skos:note "Presupposes familiarity with the central meridians from earlier energy exercises. Not feeling the energy is said not to matter; perception comes with practice."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Transaction'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingBoostedFlowCentralEnergyCh14 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Boosted flow of central energy"@en, "Verstärkter Fluss der zentralen Energieströme"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rapid activation of the rising and descending central currents, felt as an increase in energy flow."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable. The central currents belong to the energy work of chapter XI (pmc:TranserfingEnergiya)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Transaction'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTurningKeyYieldsBoostedEnergyFlowCh14 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Turning the key yields boosted energy flow"@en, "Schlüsseldrehen bewirkt verstärkten Energiefluss"@de ;
    skos:definition "The arrow rotation is said to switch on the central currents like a key."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingTurningTheKeyCh14 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingBoostedFlowCentralEnergyCh14 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Transaction'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingQuickReleaseTensionRelaxedStateCh14 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Quick release of tension and relaxed state"@en, "Rasches Lösen von Anspannung, entspannter Zustand"@de ;
    skos:definition "The ability to enter a relaxed state at will, letting the bodily tension that problems leave in the muscles go, and clearing the energy of intention of the excess potential that weighs one down; brings a sense of lightness."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable. Described as a key to the box of conditioning that oppressive circumstances lock one in."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Transaction'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTurningKeyYieldsReleaseTensionCh14 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Turning the key yields release of tension"@en, "Schlüsseldrehen bewirkt Lösen der Anspannung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Turning the key is said to release tension and free intention energy from excess potential."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingTurningTheKeyCh14 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingQuickReleaseTensionRelaxedStateCh14 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Transaction'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSignsThatKeyWorksCh14 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Signs that the key works"@en, "Zeichen, dass der Schlüssel wirkt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced in advance: an immediate rise in energy flow, a wave of relief as muscles loosen, a feeling of lightness and ease."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingTurningTheKeyCh14."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Transaction'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingKeyDoesNotRemoveImportanceCh14 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "The key does not remove importance"@en, "Der Schlüssel beseitigt keine Bedeutsamkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Self-limiting warning: the exercise eases letting go on the energetic and bodily level but does not by itself free one from importance."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingTurningTheKeyCh14 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Transaction'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingThreeElementsOfTransactionCh14 a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "Three elements of transaction"@en, "Drei Elemente der Transaktion"@de ;
    skos:definition "Author's division of the transaction into key, target slide, clear sight, each with its function (energy boost, strengthening the wind of intention, catching the change)."@en ;
    skos:note "No consequence of skipping an element is named, so no pm:Presupposing pairs are entered; the record of pass A on the order (A-3-015) is folded in here."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmp:TranserfingTurningTheKeyCh14 ;
    rdf:_2 pmp:TranserfingSystematicallyRunningTargetSlideX10 ;
    rdf:_3 pmp:TranserfingClearSightCh14 ;
    pm:seriesStatement "The three elements follow in this order: once the key is turned the slide is run, and only when one sees oneself fairly clearly inside it does one look up with clear sight; each builds on the one before." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Transaction'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSignsSuccessfulTransactionCh14 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Signs of a successful transaction"@en, "Zeichen einer gelungenen Transaktion"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced in advance: for a few seconds the view seems subtly altered, as though a faint new tint had been added; a sense of having met this mood somewhere before, sometimes a distinct feel of a past episode (déjà vu); or conversely the sense that something new has entered the scene that was absent seconds ago. Even an unfamiliar place may carry a flicker of something long forgotten or fresh."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingTransactionCh14. Author stresses these are new subtle tones, moods, meanings, not changes visible without the exercise; 'you will not be disappointed'."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Transaction'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPerceivingShiftsShadeSceneryCh14 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Perceiving shifts of shade in the scenery"@en, "Wahrnehmen von Tönungswechseln der Szenerie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Seeing, for brief moments, the change in hue of the stage set as the layer of one's world moves between sectors and life lines; a viewing window onto one's own movement in the alternatives space."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable. Called a porthole into the alternatives space."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Transaction'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTransaktsiya a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Mechanism of the transaction"@en, "Wirkmechanismus der Transaktion"@de ;
    skos:definition "Material realisation of one's layer normally moves evenly through the alternatives space and so goes unnoticed, like a minute hand; only sharper jumps between life lines show as changed shades. During transaction the slide strengthens the wind of intention, the thought energy departs from the frequencies of the present line, the key amplifies that energy so realisation speeds through sectors, and clear sight wakes one to catch the brief gust."@en ;
    skos:note "Also: déjà vu is common but missed because one accepts situations at face value, i.e. sleeps in a waking dream. Shared system term of Stupen' III, typed by this part; the practice is pmp:TranserfingTransactionCh14."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Transaction'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPractiseTransactionDispassionatelyLightlyCh14 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Practise transaction dispassionately and lightly"@en, "Transaktion gelassen und leicht üben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Do it as routinely as brushing teeth; keep attempts spontaneous, do not strain, do not make the technique important; the less weight it gets, the better it works; practise now and then, for curiosity and pleasure."@en ;
    skos:note "Touches outer intention, which cannot be controlled."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingTransactionCh14 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Transaction'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNotWorkingAtFirstExpectedCh14 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Not working at first is expected"@en, "Anfängliches Nichtgelingen ist zu erwarten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Early attempts may fail, as with learning to cycle; the author says this is no cause for concern and that it will come."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Early attempts may fail, as with learning to cycle; the author says this is no cause for concern and that it will come; it bears on pmp:TranserfingTransactionCh14. Announced non-result framed as non-failure."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Transaction'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTechniqueNotFixedCh14 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Technique not fixed"@en, "Technik nicht festgelegt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author allows that a reader may hit on a quite different technique that works for them and advises doing what feels right."@en ;
    skos:note "Statement on how fixed the method is."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Transaction'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDoNotOverdoTransactionSpeedThingsCh14 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not overdo transaction to speed things up"@en, "Transaktion nicht übertreiben, um zu beschleunigen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Frequent repetition would in principle hasten movement toward the goal, but since it cannot be kept impeccably dispassionate, loading oneself with it creates a strong excess potential of desire."@en ;
    skos:note "Summary restates: one should not drive oneself to do it too often; target slide and visualisation suffice."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingTransactionCh14 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Transaction'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDesireNecessityBlockTransactionCh14 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Desire and necessity block the transaction"@en, "Wunsch und Notwendigkeit blockieren die Transaktion"@de ;
    skos:definition "Wanting quick results or forcing oneself to perform the exercise builds excess potentials that drain intention energy; then no gust of the wind of intention arises and the transaction does not work."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Wanting quick results or forcing oneself to perform the exercise builds excess potentials that drain intention energy; then no gust of the wind of intention arises and the transaction does not work; it bears on pmp:TranserfingTransactionCh14. Desire to see results is strongest early on. Desire and necessity are excess potentials (pmc:TranserfingIzbytochnyPotentsial)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Transaction'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingPausingWhenDesireOrStrainAppearsCh14 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Pausing when desire or strain appears"@en, "Pausieren, sobald Wunsch oder Anstrengung auftaucht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Watch for the wish to see results; on noticing it, or on noticing oneself tensing to perform perfectly or straining to perceive shades, stop and return to the exercise later when the urge has subsided."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Transaction'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTransactionYieldsPerceptionSceneryShadesCh14 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Transaction yields perception of scenery shades"@en, "Transaktion bewirkt Wahrnehmung der Szenerietönung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The transaction is said to let one see the movement of material realisation as changing shades; this is named its only purpose."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingTransactionCh14 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingPerceivingShiftsShadeSceneryCh14 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Transaction'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPrioritySlideWorkOverTransactionCh14 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Priority of slide work over transaction"@en, "Vorrang der Dia-Arbeit vor der Transaktion"@de ;
    skos:definition "Main effort belongs to the target slide and to visualising the current link of the transfer chain; outer intention acts whether or not one sees it, transaction only offers a view of it."@en ;
    skos:note "The slide is pmc:TranserfingSlayd."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Transaction'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Shades in the Scenery'
#

pmp:TranserfingComparingFacesOldPhotographsCh14 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Comparing faces in old photographs"@en, "Gesichter in alten Fotos vergleichen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Leaf through old albums and compare the faces of people (including oneself) photographed at qualitatively different periods, ideally mid-life, ignoring background scenery, hairstyle, ageing and expression; look for a changed countenance or quality that is not linear ageing."@en ;
    skos:note "Backgrounds are unsuitable because places change for natural reasons."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Shades in the Scenery'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPhotoComparisonYieldsRecognitionLineShadesCh14 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Photo comparison yields recognition of line shades"@en, "Fotovergleich bewirkt Erkennen von Linientönungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Comparing period photographs is said to reveal shade differences between life lines."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingComparingFacesOldPhotographsCh14 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingDistinguishingLifeLinesTheirShadeCh14 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Shades in the Scenery'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDistinguishingLifeLinesTheirShadeCh14 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Distinguishing life lines by their shade"@en, "Lebenslinien an ihrer Tönung unterscheiden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Recognising the characteristic hue that one's realisation takes in sectors of differing quality within the alternatives space."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Shades in the Scenery'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPlainSurroundingsShowNoChangeCh14 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Plain surroundings show no change"@en, "Schlichte Umgebung zeigt keine Veränderung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Shades are nearly impossible to catch in simple objects; clear sight aimed at a bed or cupboard reveals nothing, hence practise outdoors."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Shades are nearly impossible to catch in simple objects; clear sight aimed at a bed or cupboard reveals nothing, hence practise outdoors; it bears on pmp:TranserfingTransactionCh14."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Shades in the Scenery'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTimeMovementRealisationLimitsTimeTravelCh14 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Time as movement of realisation; limits of time travel"@en, "Zeit als Bewegung der Realisierung; Grenzen der Zeitreise"@de ;
    skos:definition "Realisation runs through the alternatives space like film through a projector and this motion is experienced as time; moving against or ahead of it on the same line is impossible, as it would break cause and effect; between different lines it is held theoretically possible, though Transurfing does not claim to know how."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Shades in the Scenery'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingForwardPastReturningFormerLifeLinesCh14 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Forward to the past: returning to former life lines"@en, "Vorwärts in die Vergangenheit: Rückkehr auf frühere Lebenslinien"@de ;
    skos:definition "In childhood the heart steers along lines leading to its goals; pendulums and chains of negative branches gradually move one away. Transaction pushes one back toward lines already visited, at a later point in time, so their past flavour bleeds through. Moving toward one's goal is thus a return to how life once felt."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingReturningToABrighterLine: the deferred promise is now explained: transaction moves one back onto lines once travelled, at a later point in time, which is why their former mood shows through. Most people are said never to return to their own path."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Shades in the Scenery'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDoNotMistakeOrdinaryDifferencesShadesCh14 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not mistake ordinary differences for shades"@en, "Gewöhnliche Unterschiede nicht für Tönungen halten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Morning versus evening light on a house, or simply seeing a place for the first time, are not the line contrasts meant; the true sign is the sense that something new has just appeared."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingTransactionCh14 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Shades in the Scenery'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTensionForcingSpoilTransactionCh14 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Tension and forcing spoil the transaction"@en, "Anspannung und Erzwingen verderben die Transaktion"@de ;
    skos:definition "Any tension prevents it from working; forcing a result turns the effort into fruitless strain of inner intention; the mind's urge to control can ruin it."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Any tension prevents it from working; forcing a result turns the effort into fruitless strain of inner intention; the mind's urge to control can ruin it; it bears on pmp:TranserfingTransactionCh14."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Shades in the Scenery'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNoChangeShadeHowReadItCh14 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "No change in shade: how to read it"@en, "Keine Tönungsänderung: wie zu deuten"@de ;
    skos:definition "If nothing is noticed, the present line already matches the quality of the visualisation and the goal lies ahead on it; also, past shades may never show if the route to the goal runs through lines not yet travelled. Over time, regular practice will still show changes occasionally."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: If nothing is noticed, the present line already matches the quality of the visualisation and the goal lies ahead on it; also, past shades may never show if the route to the goal runs through lines not yet travelled. Over time, regular practice will still show changes occasionally; it bears on pmp:TranserfingTransactionCh14. Absence of the sign is reinterpreted rather than counted as failure."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Shades in the Scenery'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNoFearSeeingShadesCh14 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "No fear on seeing the shades"@en, "Keine Angst beim Sehen der Tönungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "When the shifts are actually seen one should not be frightened; the author denies it is mysticism or mere perceptual effect."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingTransactionCh14 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Shades in the Scenery'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingEverydaySignsShiftingPurerLinesCh14 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Everyday signs of shifting to purer lines"@en, "Alltagszeichen des Wechsels auf reinere Linien"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: others start treating one better for no visible reason, some daily problems vanish, everyday features change unexplained; a long-stopped clock may resume running, suggesting a move to purer lines."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingTransactionCh14."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Shades in the Scenery'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingApplianceBreakdownDisturbedLinesCh14 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Appliance breakdown and disturbed lines"@en, "Geräteausfälle und gestörte Linien"@de ;
    skos:definition "Devices failing without cause when owners are stressed are not hit by excess potential directly (too weak and undirected); rather negative emotional energy shifts the person to a line where balance is disturbed, as if the air were dusty or water murky, which sensitive technology registers. Chronically unbalanced people accumulate such failures."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Shades in the Scenery'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDeadClockProvesNothingCh14 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Dead clock proves nothing"@en, "Stehende Uhr beweist nichts"@de ;
    skos:definition "If a clock does not start again, do not worry; it may simply need repair."@en ;
    skos:note "Self-limit on reading signs."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingEverydaySignsShiftingPurerLinesCh14 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Shades in the Scenery'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRegainingLostFreshnessLifeCh14 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Regaining the lost freshness of life"@en, "Wiedergewinnen der verlorenen Frische des Lebens"@de ;
    skos:definition "Recovering the sense of novelty, hope and joy lost while sliding down negative branches; the past itself cannot be restored, its feeling can."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable. Summary: moving toward one's goal refreshes the layer of one's world."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Shades in the Scenery'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMovingTowardGoalViaTransactionYieldsCh14 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Moving toward the goal via transaction yields regained freshness"@en, "Zielbewegung per Transaktion bewirkt wiedergewonnene Frische"@de ;
    skos:definition "Returning to former lines while advancing toward one's goal is said to bring back the earlier feeling of life."@en ;
    skos:note "Text ties the return to former lines to transaction and to goal movement generally (slide work)."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingTransactionCh14 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingRegainingLostFreshnessLifeCh14 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Shades in the Scenery'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Gliding'
#

pmc:TranserfingFreedomEndingBattleCh14 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Freedom is ending the battle"@en, "Freiheit heißt, den Kampf zu beenden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Dependence consists in joining the fight imposed on us; once one wakes from the waking dream, stops being harsh with oneself and stops fighting oneself and the world, nothing restrains one; the fight goes on without one's participation. Joining the battle is itself a choice, and one always receives what one chooses."@en ;
    skos:note "Compared to the brevity of the Emerald Tablet's secret. Answer to the riddle of pmc:TranserfingGuardianOfTheReserve (Stupen' I), whose naming is not repeated here."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Gliding'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWorldMirrorRelationshipCh14 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The world as mirror of one's relationship"@en, "Die Welt als Spiegel der eigenen Haltung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The world returns one's stance: discontent makes it turn away, fighting makes it fight back, ending the fight makes it come to meet one. Unlike a mirror, the world's answer may lag by days or months."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingWorldMirrorsAttitude: besides the return of one's stance, the world's answer is said to lag behind by days or months, unlike a glass mirror. Lag stated in ch. XV."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Gliding'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPendulumsCh14 a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Pendulums"@en, "Pendel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Personified forces that from birth assign a place, impose a worldview template and game rules, give a role and enclose one in conditioning, while falsely proclaiming one independent; they hang one on puppet strings and push for ever harder fighting under the rule that one should fight and copy them; their aim is to hide true freedom. No person can defeat a pendulum in battle."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingMayatnik: here pendulums are cast as assigning a place, a template and a role from birth while falsely declaring one free, under the rule that one should fight and copy them."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "pendulum(s)" ;
    pm:nameRole "controlling collective energy structures" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Gliding'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDroppingImportanceBeforeFreedomCh14 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Dropping importance before freedom"@en, "Bedeutsamkeit ablegen vor Freiheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Real freedom requires giving up importance; until one stops clinging to its strings, no other option than fighting exists."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingReducingImportanceYieldsFreeOfThePendulumsPower: where Stupen' I gives a yielding, here giving up importance is set as a necessity for the freedom of choice (pmc:TranserfingFreedomOfChoice), without which only fighting remains."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingFreedomOfChoice ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingEndingBattleCh14 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "no choice other than the battle exists" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Gliding'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDoNotFightImportanceOrEmotionsCh14 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not fight importance or emotions"@en, "Nicht gegen Bedeutsamkeit oder Gefühle kämpfen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Strings of importance cannot be torn off at once and one should not set out to eradicate complexes, since that starts another battle; they fall away when fighting stops. Trying to control one's emotions is itself fighting oneself."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingChangeAttitudeNotEmotion: new is that strings of importance and complexes must not be attacked head-on either, since that opens another battle; they drop away once the fight ends."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingEndingBattleCh14 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Gliding'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingEndingBattleCh14 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Ending the battle"@en, "Den Kampf beenden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Wake up from the dream and consciously alter one's relationship to the pendulum's game without self-reproach; stop giving surplus meaning to anything inner or outer; drop whatever importance can be dropped consciously, and transform the rest through action: turn the target slide, visualise the process, step calmly toward the goal; count refusing the game as action; let oneself and the world be as they are; break the pendulum's rules, watching from the auditorium rather than the stage."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingEndingWarWithSelf: the war is widened from self-reproach to the battle with the world, and the remedy adds dropping importance, transforming the rest through action, and counting refusal of the game as action."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Gliding'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDepthWakingDreamFollowsImportanceCh14 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Depth of the waking dream follows importance"@en, "Tiefe des Wachtraums folgt der Wichtigkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Everyone plays a role mechanically, as if asleep; how deeply one sleeps grows with the weight one lends to the props of the game, and that weight keeps one captive. Mostly it is enough to wake and deliberately alter one's relationship."@en ;
    skos:note "Reconciled from pass B (offset 27600)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Gliding'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingExpectSetbacksAtStartCh14 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Expect setbacks at the start"@en, "Anfangs mit Rückschlägen rechnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Accumulated problems do not vanish at a stroke; pendulum provocations, obstacles and disappointments are to be expected early; do not lose heart."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingEndingBattleCh14 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Gliding'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingEuphoriaSelfImportanceInviteBlowCh14 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Euphoria and self-importance invite a blow"@en, "Euphorie und Selbstwichtigkeit ziehen einen Schlag nach sich"@de ;
    skos:definition "Feeling enlightened and highly confident about controlling events creates excess potential that balanced forces answer, in proportion to the high; do not fancy oneself the director of others in one's life play; since a very powerful force is in hand, the least lapse from integrity and impeccability has noticeable consequences."@en ;
    skos:note "Proper attitude: like a right to buy a paper at any stand, nothing to get excited about."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingVneshneeNamerenie ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Gliding'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNoHarmfulUseNoBlackMagicCh14 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "No harmful use; no black magic"@en, "Keine schädigende Anwendung; keine schwarze Magie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Transurfing could be turned against people one wants revenge on, but doing so brings grave consequences; even justified retribution is to be avoided. Whoever sends negativity first receives a warning sign; continuing brings punishment. We are guests: free to choose, not entitled to change anyone."@en ;
    skos:note "Self-warning against misuse of its own method."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingVneshneeNamerenie ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Gliding'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingKeepQuietAboutWhatYouIntendCh14 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Keep quiet about what you intend to get"@en, "Über das Angestrebte schweigen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Do not brag to friends and family; confidence should turn into silent inner certainty; act with humility."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingTsel ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Gliding'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAnnouncingGoalLowersChancesCh14 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Announcing the goal lowers the chances"@en, "Ankündigen des Ziels senkt die Chancen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Declaring aloud that one will obtain what one lacks creates excess potential, balanced forces move to cancel it, and the likelihood of success drops markedly."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Declaring aloud that one will obtain what one lacks creates excess potential, balanced forces move to cancel it, and the likelihood of success drops markedly; it bears on pmc:TranserfingKeepQuietAboutWhatYouIntendCh14."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Gliding'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNoEuphoriaAfterSuccessCh14 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "No euphoria after success"@en, "Keine Euphorie nach dem Erfolg"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rejoicing after reaching the goal is fine, but without excess or euphoria, or balanced forces take the gain away."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingPrideSuccessCreatesExcessPotentialCh9: the warning concerns euphoria after the goal is reached, which is said to lead balanced forces to take the gain away."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingTsel ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Gliding'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingIntentionCelebrationCh14 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Intention of celebration"@en, "Absicht des Festes"@de ;
    skos:definition "Turn joy into an intention to celebrate: choose to perceive even the presently disappointing life as a celebration, whatever happens."@en ;
    skos:note "Rests on the principle of coordination."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Gliding'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingQuietDelightLifeThatBecomesCelebrationCh14 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Quiet delight and a life that becomes a celebration"@en, "Stille Freude und ein Leben, das zum Fest wird"@de ;
    skos:definition "A steady quiet joy from knowing one is moving toward the goal, which even balanced forces cannot dim; by coordination, life perceived as a celebration turns into one."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Gliding'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingIntentionCelebrationYieldsQuietDelightCh14 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Intention of celebration yields quiet delight"@en, "Absicht des Festes bewirkt stille Freude"@de ;
    skos:definition "Perceiving life as celebration is said to make it one and to keep quiet delight near."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingIntentionCelebrationCh14 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingQuietDelightLifeThatBecomesCelebrationCh14 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Gliding'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingEndingBattleYieldsFreedomCh14 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Ending the battle yields freedom"@en, "Kampfende bewirkt Freiheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Turning away from the fight is said to tear the strings and give true freedom without losing their support."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingEndingBattleCh14 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingFreedomOfChoice ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Gliding'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingGlidingCh14 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Gliding on the alternatives flow"@en, "Gleiten auf dem Variantenfluss"@de ;
    skos:definition "Trust that the choice will be fulfilled; tune thoughts to the target line so the flow is turned toward the goal; go with the flow, keep balance, follow the principle of coordination; sail with unity of heart and mind, steer by choice."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Gliding'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSkolzhenie a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Unhindered movement toward the goal"@en, "Ungehinderte Bewegung zum Ziel"@de ;
    skos:definition "No force is said to be able to stop one on the way to the goal; one is no longer a paper boat or puppet but glides borne by outer intention's wind."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable. Shared system term of Stupen' III, typed by this part: gliding, with unity of heart and mind as sail and choice as helm; the practice is pmp:TranserfingGlidingCh14."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Gliding'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGlidingYieldsUnhinderedMovementCh14 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Gliding yields unhindered movement"@en, "Gleiten bewirkt ungehinderte Bewegung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Going with the flow in balance and coordination is said to make one unstoppable toward the goal."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingGlidingCh14 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingSkolzhenie ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XIV Forward to the Past, section 'Gliding'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'A Run of Bad Luck'
#

pmc:TranserfingReaderLookingGoodDidNotPreventCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Reader: looking for the good did not prevent bad runs"@en, "Leser: Gutes suchen verhinderte Pechsträhnen nicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "A reader reports that despite trying to see good in everything, happy periods (job, graduation) were repeatedly followed by losses and dark spells, while complaining sometimes seemed to bring help, contrary to the theory."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: A reader reports that despite trying to see good in everything, happy periods (job, graduation) were repeatedly followed by losses and dark spells, while complaining sometimes seemed to bring help, contrary to the theory; it bears on pmp:TranserfingHabitOfPleasure. Author answers that the reader's own expectation that the good could not last chose the outcome."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'A Run of Bad Luck'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingBadLuckChosenReadingChangeCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Bad luck is a chosen reading of change"@en, "Pech ist eine gewählte Deutung von Veränderung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Knowing that a happy time cannot last is a programme the world carries out; what follows good is never bad but something better, which the mind paints dark because it departs from its script; the world then makes this negative stance physical. The mind counts as failure whatever its script lacks and as success only what it imagined beforehand, from inflated self-importance and social stereotypes."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingBadStreakAfterLuck: the run of bad luck is no longer ascribed to a pendulum's hook but to one's own expectation that good times end, which the world carries out."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'A Run of Bad Luck'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSuccessCannotBePlannedMindCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Success cannot be planned by the mind"@en, "Erfolg ist vom Verstand nicht planbar"@de ;
    skos:definition "The mind cannot foresee outcomes or design an algorithm of success; great success arrives unannounced precisely when the mind is distracted and loosens control of the script; no one, the author included, knows a recipe for a given situation. Transurfing gives no recipe; one chooses and then stays out of the way of realisation, the recipe writing itself."@en ;
    skos:note "Includes warning: distrust anyone claiming to know the recipe."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'A Run of Bad Luck'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDistrustClaimedRecipesSuccessCh15 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Distrust claimed recipes for success"@en, "Angeblichen Erfolgsrezepten misstrauen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Do not believe anyone who says they know what will work in a particular situation, the author included."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingNoUniversalRecipe: turned into a warning against anyone, the author included, who claims to know what will work in a given case."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingSuccessCannotBePlannedMindCh15 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'A Run of Bad Luck'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRealisingChoiceWithoutKnowingHowCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Realising a choice without knowing the how"@en, "Eine Wahl verwirklichen, ohne das Wie zu kennen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Getting what one has chosen as the alternatives flow runs toward it, without needing to know the route; circumstances become as one evaluates them."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'A Run of Bad Luck'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingCoordinationIntentionAfterChoosingCh15 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Coordination of intention after choosing"@en, "Koordination der Absicht nach der Wahl"@de ;
    skos:definition "Having chosen, keep the mind from obstructing the alternatives flow with control; hold the stance that the intention is being fulfilled, everything works toward it and unfolds as it should; read present circumstances as wholly positive; tell oneself that events are going as they ought."@en ;
    skos:note "Also applied in the section on regaining a partner and 'Gliding'. Applies pmc:TranserfingKoordinatsiyaNamereniya, the coordination of intention principle."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'A Run of Bad Luck'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRejectingComingEventsManifestsNegativityCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Rejecting coming events manifests negativity"@en, "Ablehnen kommender Ereignisse lässt Negatives eintreten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Each 'bad run' is a missed chance to make good luck better: when the mind refuses or condemns the events under way, the negativity materialises fully."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Each 'bad run' is a missed chance to make good luck better: when the mind refuses or condemns the events under way, the negativity materialises fully; it bears on pmp:TranserfingCoordinationIntentionAfterChoosingCh15."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'A Run of Bad Luck'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPastMistakesTurnOutServeGoalCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Past mistakes turn out to serve the goal"@en, "Frühere Fehler erweisen sich als zielführend"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: if one sets a goal and keeps to coordination, one will find that all earlier errors and setbacks worked toward it."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingCoordinationIntentionAfterChoosingCh15. Differs from pmc:TranserfingCorrectingPastMistakes: the deferred claim now reads: under coordination one finds that all earlier errors served the goal. Also: without those mistakes the goal would still be reached in another form; goals are unlimited."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'A Run of Bad Luck'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCoordinationIntentionYieldsRealisationChoiceCh15 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Coordination of intention yields realisation of choice"@en, "Koordination der Absicht bewirkt Verwirklichung der Wahl"@de ;
    skos:definition "Relying on coordination after choosing is said to let the flow carry the choice into reality; evaluating circumstances positively makes them so."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingCoordinationIntentionAfterChoosingCh15 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingRealisingChoiceWithoutKnowingHowCh15 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'A Run of Bad Luck'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'The Game of Partners'
#

pmc:TranserfingReaderImprovementsMarriageOnlyTemporaryCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Reader: improvements in marriage only temporary"@en, "Leser: Besserungen in der Ehe nur vorübergehend"@de ;
    skos:definition "A husband reports that repeated attempts to improve his marriage helped only briefly; oddly, when angry and ready to end it whatever the cost, the relationship improved for a while."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: A husband reports that repeated attempts to improve his marriage helped only briefly; oddly, when angry and ready to end it whatever the cost, the relationship improved for a while; it bears on pmc:TranserfingPolarisationCouplesCh15. Author reads the letting go as weakening polarisation: balanced forces quieten and the pendulum withdraws."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'The Game of Partners'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPolarisationCouplesCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Polarisation in couples"@en, "Polarisierung in Paaren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Most separations stem from refusing to accept each other; annoyance signals missing awareness, as in a non-lucid dream. Those asleep in waking form dependent relationships, creating polarisation; balanced forces pair opposites to even out differences, and pendulums sensing the polarity prompt the partner, usually unwittingly, to irritate further so as to feed on it. Letting go weakens polarisation. Similar characters are said to be less compatible than opposites, who can live in harmony."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingOppositesUnited: adds that similar characters clash more than opposites, that pendulums prompt the partner to irritate, and that letting go weakens the polarisation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'The Game of Partners'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAtLeastPartnerMustWatchFromCh15 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "At least one partner must watch from the auditorium"@en, "Mindestens ein Partner muss aus dem Zuschauerraum schauen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Avoiding the repeated dramatic break-ups needs at least one partner to observe the joint life from outside the play."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingAcceptingSelfPartnerTheyAreCh15 ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingStepIntoTheAuditoriumCh7 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "conflicts and staged separations continue" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'The Game of Partners'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingChildrenLucidDreamersCanChangeScriptCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Children and lucid dreamers can change the script"@en, "Kinder und Klarträumer können das Drehbuch ändern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Children at play remember it is a game and so act as spectator and actor at once, able to alter the plot; lucid dreamers control events for the same reason. Adults lose this, sink into their games as into deep sleep, become puppets of pendulums, and life just happens to them."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'The Game of Partners'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingPlayingCouplesRolesLikeChildrenCh15 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Playing the couple's roles like children"@en, "Die Paarrollen wie Kinder spielen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Step off the stage and into the audience seats and watch the shared life as a play; adopt the roles the partners have given each other and play them lightly, for fun; whenever the partner does something irritating, act out one's own role in an exaggerated, grotesque, humorous way."@en ;
    skos:note "At least one partner must take the spectator's view."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'The Game of Partners'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPlayfulRolePlayYieldsAcceptanceCh15 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Playful role-play yields acceptance"@en, "Spielerisches Rollenspiel bewirkt Annahme"@de ;
    skos:definition "Playing the roles humorously is said to make conflict dynamics transparent and lead to acceptance."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingPlayingCouplesRolesLikeChildrenCh15 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingAcceptingSelfPartnerTheyAreCh15 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'The Game of Partners'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAcceptingSelfPartnerTheyAreCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Accepting self and partner as they are"@en, "Sich und den Partner annehmen, wie sie sind"@de ;
    skos:definition "Seeing plainly how conflicts arise from waking sleep and how many quarrels are invented, and thereby being able to accept oneself and others unchanged; like children and lucid dreamers, being able to change the script because one knows it is a game."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'The Game of Partners'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Charity'
#

pmc:TranserfingAgainstBuyingAbsolutionThroughChurchDonationsCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against buying absolution through church donations"@en, "Gegen Ablasskauf durch Kirchenspenden"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author denies that giving money to the church saves the soul or clears karma; this idea is said to come from adherents of pendulums, not of God; the religion pendulum is not God, the church is needed by the pendulum, and seeing a donation as a solution is an attempt to bargain with God."@en ;
    skos:note "Dispute with a tradition (church practice of donations for absolution)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Charity'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCharitySincereGivingVersusDealCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Charity: sincere giving versus deal"@en, "Wohltätigkeit: aufrichtiges Geben versus Handel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Charity can dissolve the excess potential of stagnant surplus money; it is a good deed only when sincere; support given without love, for self-image, is a deal: it may raise reputation but brings the soul nothing. Loving oneself sincerely is better than loving others insincerely, and self-love is called essential."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingMaskOfTheBenefactor: adds that charity can discharge the potential of stagnant surplus money and that giving without love is a deal that does nothing for the soul."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Charity'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDoNotTakeHelpingOthersWithoutCh15 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not take on helping others without genuine wish"@en, "Helfen nicht ohne echten Antrieb übernehmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Do not load oneself with an obligation to help if not truly moved; pursue one's own wealth without shame; ignore pendulum supporters pushing 'spiritual' values, since a truly spiritual person forces nothing on anyone."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingAltruismCompensationSpiritualEmptinessX10: put as a direct warning against loading oneself with helping without a real wish, and as permission to pursue one's own wealth."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingCharitySincereGivingVersusDealCh15 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Charity'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingDefineGoalStepTowardItIgnoreCh15 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Define the goal, step toward it, ignore the how"@en, "Ziel bestimmen, darauf zugehen, das Wie außer Acht lassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ask what one truly wants, what would make life an unbroken celebration; set that as goal; take steps toward it without working out the means; let soul and mind go together."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Charity'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingOpeningDoorsAppearanceMeansCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Opening of doors and appearance of means"@en, "Sich öffnende Türen und auftauchende Mittel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Means appear by themselves and previously locked doors open when soul and mind move jointly toward the goal."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable. Differs from pmc:TranserfingSeeingTrueNatureThingsLockedDoorsX10: locked doors open here because soul and mind go together toward the goal, and the means appear of themselves."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Charity'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGoalDirectedSteppingYieldsOpenDoorsCh15 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Goal-directed stepping yields open doors"@en, "Zielgerichtetes Gehen bewirkt offene Türen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Moving toward the defined goal with soul and mind united is said to bring the means and open doors."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingDefineGoalStepTowardItIgnoreCh15 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingOpeningDoorsAppearanceMeansCh15 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Charity'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPersistentLossesSuggestWrongDoorCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Persistent losses suggest a wrong door"@en, "Anhaltende Verluste deuten auf eine falsche Tür"@de ;
    skos:definition "A reader trading currency for two years with constant losses is pointed to his own results as the answer to whether this is his door: those who move toward their deepest goal by the door that is theirs find soul and mind both pleased."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: A reader trading currency for two years with constant losses is pointed to his own results as the answer to whether this is his door: those who move toward their deepest goal by the door that is theirs find soul and mind both pleased; it bears on pmc:TranserfingDver. Reader's experience is thirdParty; the inference rule is the author's."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Charity'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Esoteric Knowledge'
#

pmc:TranserfingTransurfingNotInventedKnowledgeResidesAlternativesCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Transurfing not invented; knowledge resides in the alternatives space"@en, "Transurfing nicht erfunden; Wissen liegt im Variantenraum"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author says Transurfing was not made up, so its laws cannot be simplified or remade; esoteric knowledge can be neither invented nor learned from another, it lies in a commonly reachable place he calls the alternatives space; others may name it differently without changing it."@en ;
    skos:note "Answer to a reader who suspected Transurfing is itself a pendulum or utopia. Statement on fixity of the laws."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Esoteric Knowledge'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingBasicGroundingBeforeDrawingFromCh15 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Basic grounding before drawing from the alternatives space"@en, "Grundwissen vor dem Schöpfen aus dem Variantenraum"@de ;
    skos:definition "Only after establishing a basic foundation in a field can one obtain further material directly from the alternatives space."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:TranserfingDrawingKnowledgeFromSoulInsteadBooksCh15 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingBasicGroundingInFieldCh15 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Esoteric Knowledge'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingBasicGroundingInFieldCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Basic grounding in a field"@en, "Grundlage in einem Fachgebiet"@de ;
    skos:definition "A foundation built by reading widely in a subject, such as psychology or the esoteric, up to the point where further reading adds nothing."@en ;
    skos:note "Entered by the reader as the prior step of pmc:TranserfingBasicGroundingBeforeDrawingFromCh15."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Esoteric Knowledge'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingClingingWiseKeepsConfusedCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Clinging to the wise keeps one confused"@en, "Am Wort der Weisen hängen hält verwirrt"@de ;
    skos:definition "While the mind stays fixed on the words of others it remains confused and stuck as an eternal student; critics and students direct intention toward valuing others' work."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: While the mind stays fixed on the words of others it remains confused and stuck as an eternal student; critics and students direct intention toward valuing others' work; it bears on pmp:TranserfingDrawingKnowledgeFromSoulInsteadBooksCh15."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Esoteric Knowledge'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAccessInformationFieldCreatingNewCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Access to the information field; creating the new"@en, "Zugang zum Informationsfeld; Neues schaffen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The soul, unlike the mind, reaches an information field holding data on past and future and every masterpiece and discovery; the mind receives this as intuition and inspiration; through unity of heart and mind one can get answers to all questions, make discoveries and create genuinely new work."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable. Author denies the soul simply knows everything already."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Esoteric Knowledge'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingDrawingKnowledgeFromSoulInsteadBooksCh15 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Drawing knowledge from the soul instead of books"@en, "Wissen aus der Seele statt aus Büchern schöpfen"@de ;
    skos:definition "After building a basic grounding in a field, stop and set aside what others wrote; boldly rely on oneself; turn the mind's attention to the soul; accept that all knowledge is open to one; seek answers within; walk one's own path and claim individuality; tell oneself one is unique and knows everything; put a question to oneself and await a reply; keep the power of intention with the heart, shifting it from others to self."@en ;
    skos:note "Soul and mind are pmc:TranserfingDusha and pmc:TranserfingRazum."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Esoteric Knowledge'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTurningSoulYieldsAccessKnowledgeCh15 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Turning to the soul yields access to knowledge"@en, "Hinwendung zur Seele bewirkt Wissenszugang"@de ;
    skos:definition "Redirecting intention from others to oneself is said to make knowledge accessible and lead to discoveries and masterpieces."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingDrawingKnowledgeFromSoulInsteadBooksCh15 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingAccessInformationFieldCreatingNewCh15 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Esoteric Knowledge'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAnswerPosedQuestionArrivesCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The answer to a posed question arrives"@en, "Die Antwort auf eine gestellte Frage kommt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: after asking oneself, the answer will certainly come, at once or after days or months depending on the question's complexity."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingDrawingKnowledgeFromSoulInsteadBooksCh15. Deadline-like window: up to months."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Esoteric Knowledge'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingImmersionOthersProblemsHarmsCh15 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Immersion in others' problems harms"@en, "Eintauchen in fremde Probleme schadet"@de ;
    skos:definition "The belief that one must let others' cares touch one in order to help is called a pendulum stereotype; immersion makes one as powerless as those affected; deep emotional sympathy only does more harm."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingHelpingParticipatingSpectatorCh15 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Esoteric Knowledge'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingParticipatingSpectatorYieldsProblemSolvingCh15 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Participating spectator yields problem-solving"@en, "Teilnehmender Zuschauer bewirkt Problemlösung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Detached spectatorship is said to be the only way to find solutions."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingHelpingParticipatingSpectatorCh15 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingSolvingOwnOthersProblemsMasterySituationCh15 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Esoteric Knowledge'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingHelpingParticipatingSpectatorCh15 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Helping as a participating spectator"@en, "Helfen als teilnehmender Zuschauer"@de ;
    skos:definition "Do not sink emotionally into others' problems; help with detachment (not coldness), without distressing oneself or deep emotional sympathy, and only when asked; step down into the auditorium, take the participating spectator's role, play one's part for fun."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingParticipatingWitnessCh7: applied to helping others: with detachment rather than coldness, without deep emotional sympathy, and only when asked. Detachment = absence of importance, not of compassion."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Esoteric Knowledge'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSolvingOwnOthersProblemsMasterySituationCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Solving one's own and others' problems; mastery of the situation"@en, "Eigene und fremde Probleme lösen; Herr der Lage sein"@de ;
    skos:definition "Seeing a problem clearly and solving it objectively, being puppeteer rather than puppet of the situation."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Esoteric Knowledge'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingAbandoningGuiltDutyCh15 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Abandoning guilt and duty"@en, "Schuld und Pflicht ablegen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Distinguish spontaneous compassion from a guilt-driven duty to give; drop the guilt; acknowledge one's freedom, that one owes nobody anything; claim one's right to knowledge and to giving answers oneself."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingGuiltDutySlogansUsedPendulumsX10: turned into a practice: tell spontaneous compassion from guilt-driven duty, drop the guilt and claim one's right to knowledge. Duty is called a form of importance."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Esoteric Knowledge'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNotFreeImportanceTormentedDoubtCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Not free of importance: tormented by doubt"@en, "Nicht frei von Bedeutsamkeit: von Zweifel gequält"@de ;
    skos:definition "Without freedom from importance one remains tortured by doubts."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Without freedom from importance one remains tortured by doubts; it bears on pmp:TranserfingAbandoningGuiltDutyCh15."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Esoteric Knowledge'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAbandoningGuiltYieldsFreeCompassionCh15 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Abandoning guilt yields free compassion"@en, "Schuld ablegen bewirkt freies Mitgefühl"@de ;
    skos:definition "Freedom from duty and importance is said to permit empathy without torment."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingAbandoningGuiltDutyCh15 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingFreeCompassionWithoutSelfTormentCh15 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Esoteric Knowledge'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFreeCompassionWithoutSelfTormentCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Free compassion without self-torment"@en, "Freies Mitgefühl ohne Selbstqual"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once free of importance, one is right in oneself and can sympathise and empathise without doubt or torment."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Esoteric Knowledge'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'How to Win Back the One You Love'
#

pmc:TranserfingInnerIntentionCannotWinBackDepartedCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Inner intention cannot win back a departed partner"@en, "Innere Absicht holt keinen gegangenen Partner zurück"@de ;
    skos:definition "If the partner left by choice, direct actions aimed at getting them back or influencing them will very likely fail; even if they succeed, the returned person would be changed. Only outer intention can do it; and if the person does not love one, it is impossible."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: If the partner left by choice, direct actions aimed at getting them back or influencing them will very likely fail; even if they succeed, the returned person would be changed. Only outer intention can do it; and if the person does not love one, it is impossible; it bears on pmc:TranserfingVnutrenneeNamerenie."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'How to Win Back the One You Love'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSelfWorthCommonCoreRelationalNeedsCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Self-worth as common core of relational needs"@en, "Selbstwert als gemeinsamer Kern von Beziehungsbedürfnissen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Inner intention seeks to influence the world directly, outer intention lets the world come halfway. All the varied needs partners seek (love, sex, respect, closeness, fun) share one element: protecting and confirming self-worth; inner intention in relationships always aims at that."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'How to Win Back the One You Love'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingFrailingGivePartnerAimHisInnerCh15 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Frailing: give the partner the aim of his inner intention"@en, "Frailing: dem Partner das Ziel seiner inneren Absicht geben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Drop the intention to receive, whatever it targets; identify what the partner's inner intention seeks (confirmation of his worth); do not judge him for it; turn one's efforts to fulfilling it. One's own inner intention thereby becomes outer intention."@en ;
    skos:note "First principle of Frailing (from earlier in the book): replacing the intention to receive with that of giving returns what was relinquished. Applies the first principle of Frailing (pmc:TranserfingFreyling)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'How to Win Back the One You Love'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingReceivingFromPartnerAllWishedMoreCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Receiving from the partner all one wished and more"@en, "Vom Partner alles Gewünschte und mehr erhalten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Making the partner happy while receiving what one had let go of, instantly; described as real magic without spells or potions."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'How to Win Back the One You Love'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFrailingYieldsReceivingWhatWasRelinquishedCh15 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Frailing yields receiving what was relinquished"@en, "Frailing bewirkt Erhalt des Losgelassenen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Replacing receiving with giving is said to work so well that it feels like magic."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingFrailingGivePartnerAimHisInnerCh15 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingReceivingFromPartnerAllWishedMoreCh15 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'How to Win Back the One You Love'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLostRelationshipsRarelyReturnCheckMotiveCh15 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Lost relationships rarely return; check the motive"@en, "Verlorene Beziehungen kehren selten zurück; Motiv prüfen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Restoring what is lost is as hard as stepping twice into one river; Frailing is better applied before a relationship suffers; before acting, examine whether one wants the person or merely to repair wounded self-esteem."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingFrailingGivePartnerAimHisInnerCh15 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'How to Win Back the One You Love'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAuthorsAdviceFallibleIntuitionThenHarmlessCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Author's advice is fallible; intuition, then a harmless principle"@en, "Rat des Autors ist fehlbar; erst Intuition, dann ein unschädliches Prinzip"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author gives specific solutions only in clear cases and calls his view subjective and fallible; lacking an answer he consults intuition, and failing that recommends a Transurfing principle because it cannot hurt; he offers tools, not detailed instructions."@en ;
    skos:note "Statement on how fixed and tested the method's application is."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'How to Win Back the One You Love'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGoalsVersusAccompanyingAttributesCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Goals versus accompanying attributes"@en, "Ziele versus Begleitattribute"@de ;
    skos:definition "Career, stability and high pay are not goals but attributes that come of themselves once the true goal (what turns life into a celebration) is reached. Public stereotypes form from visible end results and hide the path, which runs through many setbacks; hence the myth that abundance belongs to a chosen few."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'How to Win Back the One You Love'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingChasingAttributesInsteadGoalCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Chasing attributes instead of the goal"@en, "Attributen statt dem Ziel nachjagen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Substituting an attribute for the goal achieves nothing, like a moth at a bulb; following stereotypes brings at best mediocre success at great effort."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Substituting an attribute for the goal achieves nothing, like a moth at a bulb; following stereotypes brings at best mediocre success at great effort; it bears on pmc:TranserfingTsel. Differs from pmc:TranserfingOutcomeChasingFalseGoalX10: the false target is an accompanying attribute (career, pay) taken for the goal; at best it brings mediocre success at great cost."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'How to Win Back the One You Love'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMakingFittingDecisionCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Making the fitting decision"@en, "Die passende Entscheidung treffen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Arriving at decisions arising where heart and mind act as one; needed to move toward great success unwavering whatever others say."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'How to Win Back the One You Love'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingHeartDiscomfortTestDecisionsCh15 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Heart-discomfort test for decisions"@en, "Herz-Unbehagen-Probe für Entscheidungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Weigh others' advice but decide with the heart: if a decision brings even slight gut unease akin to obligation, the heart says no; if no discomfort, the heart says yes or is undecided, and the mind makes the final call."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingDiscomfortAsSign: adds the neutral case: when the heart shows no unease it says yes or does not know, and the mind decides. Right decisions arise where heart and mind are one."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'How to Win Back the One You Love'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHeartTestYieldsFittingDecisionsCh15 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Heart test yields fitting decisions"@en, "Herzprobe bewirkt passende Entscheidungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Using the discomfort signal of the heart, with the mind deciding in neutral cases, is said to give the right decision."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingHeartDiscomfortTestDecisionsCh15 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingMakingFittingDecisionCh15 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'How to Win Back the One You Love'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDoNotTormentOneselfFindGoalCh15 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not torment oneself to find a goal"@en, "Sich nicht quälen, ein Ziel zu finden"@de ;
    skos:definition "If no goal can be defined, stop trying; one can live without one; move with the flow (not merely be carried), keep coordination, and life runs calmly; the goal is said to surface once the fitful searching ends."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingDefineGoalStepTowardItIgnoreCh15 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'How to Win Back the One You Love'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Intention'
#

pmc:TranserfingNaturePurityIntentionCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Nature and purity of intention"@en, "Wesen und Reinheit der Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Intention can do anything; the question is its force. It is neither desire (strong wanting tends to fail) nor faith (which harbours doubt), but a calm, unconditional resolve that one's will shall manifest plus quiet certainty that it will. It is pure when free of wanting, fear, doubt and other potentials of importance, like the intention of fetching mail from the letterbox. The power of intention is said to be unteachable; Transurfing provides methods that let outer intention act regardless of will."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingPureIntentionVersusDesireCh7: faith is now set beside desire as what intention is not, and the example is fetching one's mail. Intention as such is pmc:TranserfingNamerenie."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingJesusChristMeasureIntentionsForceCh15 a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Jesus Christ as measure of intention's force"@en, "Jesus Christus als Maß der Absichtskraft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Named as one whose intention had the force to heal; used as the standard for an intention strong enough to cure."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingJesusAsExemplarCh7: here the measure is the force of intention needed to heal, not walking on water."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Jesus Christ" ;
    pm:nameRole "exemplar of healing intention" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingEffortStrongDesireDoNotProduceCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Effort and strong desire do not produce the result"@en, "Anstrengung und starkes Wollen bringen das Ergebnis nicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Wanting something very strongly makes getting it unlikely; results do not come from effort, just as a paralysed person cannot exert himself into walking, though he might regain movement by chance 'remembering' how."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Wanting something very strongly makes getting it unlikely; results do not come from effort, just as a paralysed person cannot exert himself into walking, though he might regain movement by chance 'remembering' how; it bears on pmc:TranserfingNaturePurityIntentionCh15. Differs from pmc:TranserfingWantingPreventsGetting: adds that effort does not bring the result either, with the image of the paralysed person who can only remember how to move."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPowerIntentionCannotBeTaughtCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Power of intention cannot be taught"@en, "Kraft der Absicht ist nicht lehrbar"@de ;
    skos:definition "Nobody, the author included, can teach the force of intention; what Transurfing supplies are methods that let intention act regardless of one's will, namely outer intention (pmc:TranserfingVneshneeNamerenie)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHealingOthersPureIntentionCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Healing others by pure intention"@en, "Heilen anderer durch reine Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "With intention of sufficient force (that of Jesus Christ is the example), healing is possible; a mother's will to heal her children, if as pure as fetching mail, would heal them."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable. Conditional; author warns effort does not do it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingStopTryingHealIfTreatmentDoesCh15 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Stop trying to heal if treatment does not help"@en, "Heilversuche aufgeben, wenn die Behandlung nicht hilft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Where treatment fails, the mother should cease trying to cure her children and accept them as they are."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingHealingOthersPureIntentionCh15 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMentalIllnessAttunementUnrealisedFieldRegionsCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Mental illness as attunement to unrealised field regions"@en, "Psychische Krankheit als Einstimmung auf unrealisierte Feldbereiche"@de ;
    skos:definition "A psychological disturbance is said to be the soul tuned to a region of the alternatives space not materialised physically; such people are not ill but different, hovering in an area that seems abnormal from our viewpoint. Sameness of everyone is called the real abnormality."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingIntoxicationPsychosisAttunementUnrealisedSectorsCh8: the mentally ill are now said to be not sick but different, and uniformity is what is called abnormal."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingForcingIntentionAggravatesSituationCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Forcing intention aggravates the situation"@en, "Erzwingen der Absicht verschlimmert die Lage"@de ;
    skos:definition "Trying hard, straining and getting frustrated creates excess potential that only makes things worse; intention cannot be forced."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Trying hard, straining and getting frustrated creates excess potential that only makes things worse; intention cannot be forced; it bears on pmp:TranserfingAcceptingChildrenTheyAreCh15."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAcceptanceYieldsOuterIntentionCh15 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Acceptance yields outer intention"@en, "Annahme bewirkt äußere Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Accepting the children unchanged is said to let intention work indirectly as outer intention."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingAcceptingChildrenTheyAreCh15 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingInnerIntentionTurningIntoOuterIntentionCh15 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingInnerIntentionTurningIntoOuterIntentionCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Inner intention turning into outer intention"@en, "Umschlagen innerer Absicht in äußere"@de ;
    skos:definition "The power of intention arriving indirectly once forcing stops, inner intention converting into outer intention."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingAcceptingChildrenTheyAreCh15 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Accepting one's children as they are"@en, "Die eigenen Kinder annehmen, wie sie sind"@de ;
    skos:definition "Stop trying to make the children normal; accept them and acknowledge their sanity; give attention, love and as much freedom as possible; free them from having to be normal and oneself from needing to normalise them."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingTreatingAsGuests: applied to children held to be mentally ill: stop trying to normalise them and grant them freedom from having to be normal. Author adds he is not a psychiatrist and the reader must decide whether to follow him."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingResultsComeTimeNotAtOnceCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Results come in time, not at once"@en, "Ergebnisse kommen mit der Zeit, nicht sofort"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: after accepting and freeing the children, results will begin to show, perhaps not immediately but over time."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingAcceptingChildrenTheyAreCh15."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTrustYourHeartOverAuthorCh15 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Trust your heart over the author"@en, "Dem eigenen Herzen mehr trauen als dem Autor"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author warns his advice is not a specialist's, questions his own right to give it, and tells the reader to place the heart's voice above others' views including his; his only edge is lacking emotional attachment, hence pure intention in answering."@en ;
    skos:note "Self-warning against its own advice."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingAuthorsAdviceFallibleIntuitionThenHarmlessCh15 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingProjectsMakeEveryoneHappyBreedPendulumsCh15 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Projects to make everyone happy breed pendulums"@en, "Vorhaben, alle glücklich zu machen, erzeugen Pendel"@de ;
    skos:definition "One person can only shape their own layer; ideas uniting people for general happiness, even spiritual ones built on love of God, create pendulums that lead followers off their path and wage war on rivals; nations have perished for God and earthly happiness. Happiness is individual: everyone becomes happy only by heading to their own goal by their own door. Transurfing is called a pendulum for individualists, yet the only true path to lasting happiness."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingMayatnik ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWantingVersusIntendingCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Wanting versus intending"@en, "Wollen versus Beabsichtigen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The world gives back exactly one's choice: believing nobody is lucky in all things makes it true; merely wanting returns only the state of wanting; only when one stops wanting and intends to have does one receive. Motto: not wanting or hoping, but intending."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingWantingPreventsGetting: the world returns only the state of wanting; one receives once one stops wanting and intends to have."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Importance Potential'
#

pmc:TranserfingFearImportancePotentialCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fear as importance potential"@en, "Angst als Bedeutsamkeitspotenzial"@de ;
    skos:definition "Fear is an excess potential arising from giving the feared object too much meaning; balanced forces would remove it by the cheapest route (e.g. throwing one off the cliff one fears); resisting them costs double energy, for the potential and for holding it, leaving one numb; if strong enough, control fails and panic carries one toward the potential's discharge. There is no universal remedy; reducing importance consciously would end fear but is impossible in such a moment."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingPotentialFromImportance: adds that resisting balanced forces doubles the expense of energy and that panic sets in once the potential can no longer be held. Linked to pmc:TranserfingVazhnost and pmc:TranserfingUravnoveshivayushchieSily."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Importance Potential'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingArguingOneselfOutFearFailsCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Arguing oneself out of fear fails"@en, "Sich die Angst ausreden scheitert"@de ;
    skos:definition "Persuading oneself not to be afraid, self-deception and any inner fight with fear are futile, draining energy and enlarging the excess potential."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Persuading oneself not to be afraid, self-deception and any inner fight with fear are futile, draining energy and enlarging the excess potential; it bears on pmp:TranserfingAllowingFearInsteadFightingItCh15."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Importance Potential'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingAllowingFearInsteadFightingItCh15 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Allowing the fear instead of fighting it"@en, "Die Angst zulassen statt sie zu bekämpfen"@de ;
    skos:definition "If fear cannot be avoided, feel it; act as well as one can but do not battle the fear; e.g. before a talk, be nervous on purpose and with relish, giving oneself wholly to the feeling and allowing oneself to lose one's head in whatever way pleases."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Importance Potential'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAllowingFearYieldsItsDissolutionCh15 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Allowing fear yields its dissolution"@en, "Angst zulassen bewirkt ihre Auflösung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Permitting the nervousness is said to make anxiety vanish because the energy of fighting it is released."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingAllowingFearInsteadFightingItCh15 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingDissolvingFearAnxietyCh15 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Importance Potential'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDissolvingFearAnxietyCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Dissolving fear and anxiety"@en, "Angst und Unruhe auflösen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Letting anxiety and worry fade, freeing the energy otherwise spent on struggling against them."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Importance Potential'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingDispersingWorryThroughActionCoordinationCh15 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Dispersing worry through action and coordination"@en, "Sorge durch Handeln und Koordination auflösen"@de ;
    skos:definition "For anxiety and worry (milder fear born of anticipating the unknown): remind oneself that worrying is self-defeating since dreaded expectations tend to come true; take any action at all, even unrelated, and keep busy; use the coordination principle as reference, permit oneself ignorance of how things ought to develop, release control and let the situation resolve itself, going with the flow."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingIdleWorry: turned into a remedy: any action at all disperses the potential of worry, helped by the coordination principle. The coordination principle is pmc:TranserfingKoordinatsiyaNamereniya; lowering importance relates to pmc:TranserfingKoordinatsiyaVazhnosti."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Importance Potential'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingActionCoordinationYieldReliefFromWorryCh15 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Action and coordination yield relief from worry"@en, "Handeln und Koordination bewirken Entlastung von Sorge"@de ;
    skos:definition "The potential created by worry is said to dissipate in action; coordination lowers importance."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingDispersingWorryThroughActionCoordinationCh15 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingDissolvingFearAnxietyCh15 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Importance Potential'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAnxietyEasesAtOnceWhenBusyCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Anxiety eases at once when busy"@en, "Unruhe lässt sofort nach, wenn man tätig wird"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: once occupied with something, one will see immediately that the worry has lessened; circumstances begin to turn positive when one consciously goes with the flow."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingDispersingWorryThroughActionCoordinationCh15."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Importance Potential'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingProsperityLeastEnergyNormCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Prosperity as least-energy norm"@en, "Wohlergehen als Norm geringsten Energieaufwands"@de ;
    skos:definition "Coordination works not because forces care for anyone but because nature spends least energy; difficulties always involve excess energy expenditure, while prosperity is the norm needing minimal energy; the mind ignores the easiest path and struggles against the flow, creating its own obstacles; appeal is made to conservation of energy."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Importance Potential'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCoordinationPrincipleNotBeTakenLiterallyCh15 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Coordination principle not to be taken literally"@en, "Koordinationsprinzip nicht wörtlich nehmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "One cannot charge into danger while telling oneself all is going as it should; the principle is reliable only in general, not categorically."@en ;
    skos:note "Self-limit on the method."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingCoordinationIntentionAfterChoosingCh15 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Importance Potential'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHighGoalsPendulumInterferenceCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "High goals and pendulum interference"@en, "Hohe Ziele und Störung durch Pendel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pendulums obstruct everyone; their counter-pressure is minimised by keeping importance low; most problems come from excessive inner and outer importance. Lofty goals are not hard as such, only stereotypes and false thought patterns make them so; any goal can be reached if it is truly one's own. Others' words may be considered but given no more weight; follow the heart, not relatives' well-meant advice."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Importance Potential'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWeighRelativesWordsLightlyWhenChoosingCh15 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Weigh relatives' words lightly when choosing a goal"@en, "Worte der Verwandten bei der Zielwahl leicht nehmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Others may be heard on the choice of goal and route, but their remarks deserve no extra weight; guidance comes from the heart, not from advisers, least of all from kin who claim to want only the best."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingTsel ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Importance Potential'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingPlayingFoolTeddyBearRitualCh15 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Playing the fool (teddy-bear ritual)"@en, "Den Narren spielen (Teddybär-Ritual)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Choose with care an inanimate 'fool', e.g. a teddy bear; draft a meticulous plan stating the place, time and manner of fooling it around, plus detailed formal instructions (e.g. rotating it about its long axis on a level surface by hand), including safety measures; present the project professionally in a business folder; then carry it out strictly by the instructions with a focused, intelligent face; if laughter bursts out, pause, laugh it out, and resume when calm."@en ;
    skos:note "Prescribed to a disciplined reader who felt hindered by others; meant literally."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Importance Potential'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingInnerImportancePolarisesCurvesMirrorCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Inner importance polarises and curves the mirror"@en, "Innere Bedeutsamkeit polarisiert und krümmt den Spiegel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Casting oneself as a serious, responsible person with an important mission draws people with opposite traits like filings to a magnet, as balanced forces work to cancel the potential; excess importance distorts the mirror; obstructers are pendulum puppets that the pendulum moves to provoke irritation, which it feeds on. Polarisation stems not from good qualities but from dependent relationships, activated by comparing oneself with others."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Importance Potential'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSamePeopleChangedBehaviourCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Same people, changed behaviour"@en, "Dieselben Menschen, verändertes Verhalten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: as importance drops, the outer picture transforms gradually; one is surrounded by the same people who now treat one quite differently; the world looks inexplicably different and stops obstructing."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingPlayingFoolTeddyBearRitualCh15."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Importance Potential'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFoolRitualYieldsNullifiedImportanceCh15 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Fool ritual yields nullified importance"@en, "Narrenritual bewirkt aufgehobene Bedeutsamkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Carrying out the ritual is said to cancel inner importance."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingPlayingFoolTeddyBearRitualCh15 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingNullifyingInnerImportanceCh15 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Importance Potential'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNullifyingInnerImportanceCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Nullifying inner importance"@en, "Innere Bedeutsamkeit aufheben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Dissolving the surplus potential that inner importance builds, so that polarisation stops, the mirror straightens, and the same people start acting differently and no longer obstruct one."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Importance Potential'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingRefrainingFromComparisonOthersCh15 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Refraining from comparison with others"@en, "Auf Vergleiche mit anderen verzichten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Alternative to the ritual: resist comparing oneself with those around (disciplined versus sloppy, focused versus scattered); be oneself and let others be themselves; loosen the grip."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingSuperiorityAsDependence: turned into a practice: refrain from contrasting one's discipline with others' sloppiness, as an alternative to the fool ritual."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Importance Potential'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCeasingComparisonYieldsNullifiedImportanceCh15 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Ceasing comparison yields nullified importance"@en, "Vergleichsverzicht bewirkt aufgehobene Bedeutsamkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Stopping comparison is said to end polarisation so the world stops getting in one's way."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingRefrainingFromComparisonOthersCh15 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingNullifyingInnerImportanceCh15 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Importance Potential'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLazinessSoulDutyPendulumInventionCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Laziness of the soul; duty as pendulum invention"@en, "Faulheit der Seele; Pflicht als Pendelerfindung"@de ;
    skos:definition "People avoid 'serious' things because those are not meant for them; laziness is a state of the soul, which does not wish to labour at others' affairs or for a pendulum; duty and obligation are inventions of pendulums; the world is rich enough for all if each follows their own goal by their own door, and anyone can make their layer a cosy corner."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Importance Potential'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSoulSaysIDontWantMindCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Soul says 'I don't want', mind says 'must'"@en, "Seele sagt „will nicht“, Verstand sagt „muss“"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sign of following another's goal through another's door, i.e. working for a pendulum: the soul keeps refusing while the mind keeps insisting on obligation; this path leads nowhere however reasonable it looks."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Sign of following another's goal through another's door, i.e. working for a pendulum: the soul keeps refusing while the mind keeps insisting on obligation; this path leads nowhere however reasonable it looks; it bears on pmc:TranserfingDver."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Importance Potential'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingPlayRemedyForcedObligationCh15 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Play as remedy for forced obligation"@en, "Spiel als Mittel gegen Zwangspflicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Until one's own goal is found: treat the imposed work as play, as children play at shop or hospital; take the participating spectator's role, act detached, do not give oneself wholly to the forced work, rent oneself out."@en ;
    skos:note "Suffering arises only when the mind sinks into the game."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Importance Potential'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPlayYieldsFreedomFromForcedObligationCh15 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Play yields freedom from forced-obligation suffering"@en, "Spiel bewirkt Freiheit vom Pflichtleiden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Treating work as a game, detached, is said to end the suffering that comes from immersion."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingPlayRemedyForcedObligationCh15 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingFreedomFromSufferingForcedObligationCh15 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Importance Potential'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFreedomFromSufferingForcedObligationCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Freedom from the suffering of forced obligation"@en, "Freiheit vom Leiden an Zwangspflicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Doing imposed work without suffering under it."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Importance Potential'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Reality Inversion'
#

pmc:TranserfingAsymmetryDarkeningBrighteningCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Asymmetry of darkening and brightening"@en, "Asymmetrie von Verdunkeln und Aufhellen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Low mood where heart and mind concur that life is bad lets outer intention shift reality steadily toward darker regions of that space; the mirror answers quickly, while brightening comes slowly because a depressed attitude keeps darkening one's layer; sometimes one lacks energy even to remember Transurfing."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingLingeringAnxietyRealisesWorstExpectationsCh9: adds the asymmetry: the mirror darkens quickly while brightening comes slowly, since a low mood keeps darkening one's layer."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Reality Inversion'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingRealityInversionCh15 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Reality inversion"@en, "Realitätsinversion"@de ;
    skos:definition "When things go badly, reverse one's relationship to the situation: instead of suffering, worrying and collapsing as pendulum rules dictate, do the opposite and greet the misfortune with mock delight, phrasing setbacks as strokes of luck in witty paradox; laughter that follows is part of it."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingFlowingGameGreetingSetbacksJoyfulSurpriseX10: inversion goes further than glad surprise: misfortune is greeted with mocking, exaggerated delight, as a game among friends. Originated as a game among physics students at a harsh faculty, later recognised by the author as fully conforming to Transurfing. Concept: pmc:TranserfingInversiya."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Reality Inversion'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingInversiya a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Reality inversion"@en, "Inversion der Realität"@de ;
    skos:definition "Turning one's stance toward a bad turn of events upside down: where the rules of pendulums call for suffering and collapse, one answers with mock delight. Presented as a sharper, humour-driven variant of the coordination of intention (pmc:TranserfingKoordinatsiyaNamereniya)."@en ;
    skos:note "Shared system term of Stupen' III, typed by this part; its practice is pmp:TranserfingRealityInversionCh15."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Reality Inversion'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingInversionYieldsEvenedOutRealityCh15 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Inversion yields evened-out reality"@en, "Inversion bewirkt ausgeglichene Realität"@de ;
    skos:definition "Inversion lowers importance and hence excess potential; its delight energy, however silly, mismatches gloomy lines, so a positive shift happens at once and the fast mirror answers. Called a more radical, humour-based form of coordination of intention."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingRealityInversionCh15 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingEveningOutRealityAfterDarkTurnCh15 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Reality Inversion'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingEveningOutRealityAfterDarkTurnCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Evening out reality after a dark turn"@en, "Realität nach einer dunklen Wendung ausgleichen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Breaking the vicious circle of low mood and quickly shifting to brighter life lines, with relief in heart and mind."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Reality Inversion'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingExamStoryInversionCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Author's exam story: inversion worked"@en, "Prüfungsgeschichte des Autors: Inversion wirkte"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author recounts that after a night of mocking banter before a feared probability exam he failed it, celebrated the failure as a triumph with friends, and on the resit next day got the top grade; he insists he is not inventing it."@en ;
    skos:note "Case report of the author's own student days, told to back pmp:TranserfingRealityInversionCh15; not a sign announced in advance."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Reality Inversion'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingQuickResultWellDoneInversionCh15 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Quick result of a well-done inversion"@en, "Schnelles Ergebnis einer gut ausgeführten Inversion"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: if the inversion is done well, the result will not be long in coming."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingRealityInversionCh15."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Reality Inversion'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingContrastMethodExaggeratingLowMoodCh15 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Contrast method: exaggerating the low mood"@en, "Kontrastmethode: die gedrückte Stimmung übersteigern"@de ;
    skos:definition "If too low even to invert, deliberately make the mood worse, pushing it to the extreme, grotesque and absurd, until it flips like a slide whose contrast is maxed into a negative; best done with a group of friends, else alone in one's own way."@en ;
    skos:note "Example witnessed by the author: a depressed girl in black mourning, mock condolences and a wailing song by the group, ending in shared uncontrolled laughter."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Reality Inversion'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingContrastMethodYieldsReleaseFromLowCh15 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Contrast method yields release from low mood"@en, "Kontrastmethode bewirkt Lösung aus dem Tief"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pushing the condition to absurdity is said really to work, ending in laughter that breaks the low state; illustrated by the group episode the author describes."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingContrastMethodExaggeratingLowMoodCh15 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingEveningOutRealityAfterDarkTurnCh15 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), ch. XV Letters from the Past, section 'Reality Inversion'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNoMindAlteringSubstancesContrastMethodCh15 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "No mind-altering substances; contrast method alone not advised"@en, "Keine bewusstseinsverändernden Substanzen; Kontrastmethode allein nicht empfohlen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Avoid consciousness-changing substances, which can make matters worse; the author dislikes applying the contrast method when alone and mentions it for information rather than as recommendation."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingContrastMethodExaggeratingLowMoodCh15 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen3 ;
